 want the commands behind the notebooks. The stage pages tell you what to do. These pages tell you how it works underneath."},"947":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"Three layers do the work. Each has one job."},"948":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"Layer"},"949":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"Where it lives"},"950":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"What it owns"},"951":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"The kit"},"952":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"`setup/` and the `exakit` command"},"953":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"The database, connections, loading, connectors, add-ons and the describe service"},"954":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"The helpers"},"955":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"`notebook/package/exakit_nb/`, imported as `exakit.nb`"},"956":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"One Python call for each thing a notebook does"},"957":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"The guided view"},"958":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"`notebook/package/exakit_guide/`, imported as `exakit.guide`"},"959":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"The cards, which call the helpers. They have no logic of their own."},"960":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"A notebook is cells that call the helpers. A card is a form that calls the same helpers. Neither talks to the database on its own."},"961":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"Every step follows the same path, whether you run a cell or click a card:"},"962":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"The rules the helpers follow:"},"963":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"**The connection comes from the kit.** `nb.connect()` opens it from the kit's encrypted store. No helper prints or returns a host, a user or a password."},"964":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"**The kit does the work.** Describing a table is the kit's describe service. Loading is `exakit data-load`. Connecting a source is `exakit connect`."},"965":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"**SQL is shown.** `nb.sql` records each statement, `nb.show_sql()` prints the last one, and the workflow logs it."},"966":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"**Reads are live.** `nb.components()`, `nb.addons()`, `nb.connectors()` and the rest ask the kit when they are called."},"967":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"Inside the guided view, `actions.py` lists every action as one or more lines of `exakit.nb` code. `actions.code(id, ...)` gives the exact cell text, and `actions.run(id, ...)` runs that text in the notebook's namespace and logs it. A screen changes nothing except through `actions.run`, which is why the **Code** view can always show what a card did."},"968":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-30","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#how-the-pieces-fit","content":"The tests enforce a few more rules: every action calls something the helpers export, no screen names a dataset or a connector (the kit supplies those), no action shows a secret, and every helper has a page in these docs."},"969":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-31","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#the-command-reference","content":"The command reference lists every public helper of `exakit.nb`, 116 in all, with a one-line summary and a link to its page. The pages are generated from the docstrings in `exakit_nb`, one page per module."},"970":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-32","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#the-command-reference","content":"From a notebook, the docs open at a command's page:"},"971":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-33","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#the-command-reference","content":"The `exakit` commands are described in `setup/help/exakit.json`. `exakit <command> --help` shows a command's reference and changes nothing."},"972":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-34","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#where-things-live","content":"Everything is under the kit's home, `~/.exasol-starter-kit`, or `EXAKIT_HOME` when it is set. The main folders are:"},"973":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-35","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#where-things-live","content":"Path"},"974":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-36","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#where-things-live","content":"What it holds"},"975":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-37","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#where-things-live","content":"`descriptors/`"},"976":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-38","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#where-things-live","content":"Approved column maps, one folder per table, every version kept"},"977":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-39","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#where-things-live","content":"`workflows/<id>.jsonl`"},"978":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-40","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#where-things-live","content":"Workflow logs"},"979":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-41","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#where-things-live","content":"`bundles/<workflow id>/`"},"980":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-42","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#where-things-live","content":"Hand-off bundles, each also as a zip"},"981":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-43","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#where-things-live","content":"`handoffs/`"},"982":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-44","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#where-things-live","content":"Training hand-offs for the ML Engineer"},"983":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-45","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#where-things-live","content":"`exakit.env`"},"984":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-46","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#where-things-live","content":"Settings such as the model's id and address"},"985":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-47","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#where-things-live","content":"`credentials/`"},"986":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-48","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#where-things-live","content":"Secrets, readable by you only. Never read or print these from a notebook."},"987":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-49","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#where-things-live","content":"The full table, including what an update touches and the schemas in the database, is in Where things live."},"988":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-50","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#adding-a-command","content":"Four steps, and a test:"},"989":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-51","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#adding-a-command","content":"Add a function with a docstring to a module in `notebook/package/exakit_nb/`. Export it in `exakit_nb/__init__.py` and add its name to `__all__`."},"990":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-52","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#adding-a-command","content":"Call it from the notebook it belongs to, guarded by a variable when it is optional."},"991":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-53","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#adding-a-command","content":"Add one entry to `actions.ACTIONS` in `exakit_guide/actions.py`, so a card can have a button for it."},"992":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-54","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#adding-a-command","content":"Regenerate the notebooks and the command reference with `python3 tools/notebooks.py --marimo` and `python3 tools/nb_docs.py`."},"993":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-55","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#adding-a-command","content":"Then run `python3 -m unittest tests.test_notebook_guide tests.test_notebook_helpers tests.test_notebook_docs`. The full steps, with examples, are in Add a command."},"994":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-56","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#the-notebooks","content":"The notebook sources are `notebook/notebooks/<persona>/<NN>_<name>.py`, in jupytext percent format. The `.ipynb` files and the Marimo versions are built from them:"},"995":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-57","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#building-these-docs","content":"The documentation is MDX pages in `notebook/docs/content/docs/`, one folder per persona. The folder layout is the sidebar, and each folder's `meta.json` sets its title and page order."},"996":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-58","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#building-these-docs","content":"Users never need Node. The built site travels with the kit, and `nb.docs()` serves it from the kit's own Python, on this computer only. The full steps are in These docs."},"997":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-59","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#building-these-docs","content":"Everything under a persona's `reference/` folder is generated. Change the docstring and run `python3 tools/nb_docs.py`; do not edit the generated page."},"998":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-60","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#when-the-documentation-does-not-open","content":"`nb.docs()` reads the site from the kit copy. If it says the site is not there, run:"},"999":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-61","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#when-the-documentation-does-not-open","content":"The site is served on this computer at one of the ports 8790 to 8809, the first one free. A port another program holds is skipped. When all of them are taken, any free port is used. To choose the port, set `EXAKIT_DOCS_PORT` before you start the notebooks."},"1000":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-62","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#when-the-documentation-does-not-open","content":"If the notebook runs on another machine than your browser, the frame cannot reach the site. Run `nb.docs(browser=True)` on the machine that runs the kit."},"1001":{"id":"/data-scientist/development-63","page_id":"/data-scientist/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development#when-the-documentation-does-not-open","content":"To go back to the story, see The data science workflow."},"1002":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/where-things-live","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/where-things-live","type":"page","content":"Where things live","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/where-things-live"},"1003":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/where-things-live-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/where-things-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/where-things-live","content":"The files and folders the notebooks read and write on this computer."},"1004":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/where-things-live-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/where-things-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/where-things-live#in-the-database","content":"In the database"},"1005":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/where-things-live-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/where-things-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/where-things-live#what-an-update-touches","content":"What an update touches"},"1006":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/where-things-live-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/where-things-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/where-things-live#further-reading","content":"Further reading"},"1007":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/where-things-live-4","page_id":"/dat