ve the answer away."},"1059":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/approve-the-column-map-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/approve-the-column-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/approve-the-column-map#what-approval-checks-and-writes","content":"The next **version** is written to the kit's store on this computer, under `~/.exasol-starter-kit/descriptors/`."},"1060":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/approve-the-column-map-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/approve-the-column-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/approve-the-column-map#what-approval-checks-and-writes","content":"The roles are published in Exasol Semantic Views. The schema's model is rebuilt: its time, category and flag columns become dimensions, and its measures become facts with `total_` and `average_` metrics. A sensitive column is never exposed. If publishing fails, the approval still stands, and the message says why."},"1061":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/approve-the-column-map-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/approve-the-column-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/approve-the-column-map#what-approval-checks-and-writes","content":"The active workflow's log gets one line."},"1062":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/approve-the-column-map-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/approve-the-column-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/approve-the-column-map#what-approval-checks-and-writes","content":"When the kit has no Semantic Views in the database, it installs the semantic-views add-on first, the same as `exakit marketplace semantic-views`."},"1063":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/approve-the-column-map-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/approve-the-column-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/approve-the-column-map#worked-example-amazon_sales","content":"The worked example uses `amazon_sales`, the sample orders table: `AMAZON.ORDER_LINES`. The kit ships an approved column map for it.