was refused, and the refusal gave the reason."},"1353":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-58","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#measured-on-a-real-database","content":"**Reading from an AI client.** The read-only MCP user, the one AI clients use, read the model's metrics from `SEMANTIC_CATALOG.METRICS`."},"1354":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-59","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#measured-on-a-real-database","content":"**Rebuilding on approval.** Approving a column map rebuilt its schema's model. It also refreshed every multi-source model that the table is in."},"1355":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-60","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#measured-on-a-real-database","content":"Measured values are for this database and these tables. Your numbers differ if your data differs."},"1356":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-61","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#one-model-across-sources","content":"In the guided view, open **Understand** and scroll to **Semantic views**. Then:"},"1357":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-62","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#one-model-across-sources","content":"Tick the tables. They are listed with their origin: sample data, your data or an external source. Tick as many as the question needs."},"1358":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-63","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#one-model-across-sources","content":"Give the model a name, for example `sales_360`."},"1359":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-64","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#one-model-across-sources","content":"Add the links across schemas, one per line, in the form `SCHEMA.TABLE.COLUMN=SCHEMA.TABLE.KEY`. The approved links inside each schema are used on their own."},"1360":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-65","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#one-model-across-sources","content":"Tick **Let the AI propose business names, synonyms and metrics**, if you have an AI model set up."},"1361":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-66","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#one-model-across-sources","content":"Click **Preview**. Read the dimensions and metrics of each view, what the AI proposed, and what was refused and why. Nothing is written yet."},"1362":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-67","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#one-model-across-sources","content":"Click **Publish the model**."},"1363":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-68","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#one-model-across-sources","content":"**Models in the database** lists every model. **Refresh it** rebuilds a model the kit built, from the column maps and links approved since."},"1364":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-69","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#links-across-sources","content":"Tables of different sources rarely declare how they join, and the same thing is often named differently: a customer number in one, a client id in another. The kit finds such a link from the values the columns hold. It does not match column names, and it needs no foreign key."},"1365":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-70","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#links-across-sources","content":"In the **Semantic views** card, tick the schemas and click **Find links between them**. In a cell or a terminal:"},"1366":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-71","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#links-across-sources","content":"Each link comes back with its evidence. Measured on a real database, between the Amazon sample data and a PostgreSQL source read live:"},"1367":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-72","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#links-across-sources","content":"Only 36 of the 47 different state names match (77%), because 11 are misspelt or abbreviated. Those 11 are 21 rows out of 128,942. The kit counts rows, so the link stands and the misspellings are listed for you to clean."},"1368":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-73","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-a-links-confidence-means","content":"Confidence"},"1369":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-74","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-a-links-confidence-means","content":"When"},"1370":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-75","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-a-links-confidence-means","content":"What to do"},"1371":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-76","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-a-links-confidence-means","content":"high"},"1372":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-77","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-a-links-confidence-means","content":"A text column (a code, a name) whose rows are in another table's key"},"1373":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-78","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-a-links-confidence-means","content":"It is ticked for you. Untick it if the meaning is wrong"},"1374":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-79","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-a-links-confidence-means","content":"low"},"1375":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-80","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-a-links-confidence-means","content":"A link between two plain number columns"},"1376":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-81","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-a-links-confidence-means","content":"Tick it only if you know the two columns mean the same thing"},"1377":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-82","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-a-links-confidence-means","content":"partial"},"1378":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-83","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-a-links-confidence-means","content":"Text values that only partly match, with more than 0.1% of rows missing"},"1379":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-84","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-a-links-confidence-means","content":"Not a link. Look at the spellings first"},"1380":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-85","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-a-links-confidence-means","content":"Numbers get the low mark for a measured reason. A key that is simply 1, 2, 3 and so on holds every small number. On a database with six schemas, the first version of this search proposed 18 links into one such key: a meter id, a quantity and a count of delayed shipments all \"matched\" an order line id. So a number column is only considered when it spans at least half the key's range and something else supports it: a similar name, an approved column map that calls it a key or an identifier, or a pair proposed by you or an AI. Even then the data can only contradict such a link, never prove it. Two were still proposed between unrelated order numbers, which is why the last word is yours."},"1381":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-86","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#let-an-ai-or-an-ai-client-propose-links","content":"An AI reads what the columns mean; the search above does not. With **Let the AI help** ticked (or `--ai`), your model proposes pairs from column names, types and notes. It is never sent a value. Each pair is then checked against the data like any other."},"1382":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-87","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#let-an-ai-or-an-ai-client-propose-links","content":"An AI client such as Claude Code or Codex does the same with its own reading. It checks a pair with:"},"1383":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-88","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#let-an-ai-or-an-ai-client-propose-links","content":"A pair the data contradicts comes back as `[rejected]`."},"1384":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-89","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-is-stored","content":"A link you publish becomes a relationship of the model. Its evidence is stored with it: who proposed it, how many rows matched, and which values did not. Read it back with:"},"1385":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-90","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-is-stored","content":"The model also lists each table it is built on and whether it is a table in this database or an external source read live."},"1386":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-91","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-it-costs-on-large-data","content":"Every statement of the search is bounded: one aggregate per table, one `SELECT DISTINCT ... LIMIT 500` per column, one count with a list of values per pair, and at most 400 pairs. Measured: six schemas with 25 tables took 223 statements and about 60 seconds, most of it the live source. Three schemas took 26 statements and 23 seconds."},"1387":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-92","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-it-costs-on-large-data","content":"Queries on the published model were measured on 10,002,745 rows joined to a 30,000-row table:"},"1388":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-93","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-it-costs-on-large-data","content":"Query"},"1389":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-94","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-it-costs-on-large-data","content":"Semantic SQL"},"1390":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-95","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-it-costs-on-large-data","content":"Hand-written SQL"},"1391":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-96","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-it-costs-on-large-data","content":"Group by a category"},"1392":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-97","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-it-costs-on-large-data","content":"0.20 s"},"1393":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-98","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-it-costs-on-large-data","content":"0.13 s"},"1394":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-99","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-it-costs-on-large-data","content":"Join, group by priority and month (415 groups)"},"1395":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-100","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-it-costs-on-large-data","content":"0.27 s"},"1396":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-101","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-it-costs-on-large-data","content":"0.21 s"},"1397":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-102","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-it-costs-on-large-data","content":"Join with a filter"},"1398":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-103","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-it-costs-on-large-data","content":"0.12 s"},"1399":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-104","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-it-costs-on-large-data","content":"not measured"},"1400":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-105","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#what-it-costs-on-large-data","content":"The totals were identical in all 415 groups, and the row counts added up to the table. The SQL the model compiles is one scan of the main table, one `LEFT JOIN` per table a dimension needs (none when the dimensions are the main table's own), and one `GROUP BY`. See it for any query with `EXECUTE SCRIPT SEMANTIC_ADMIN.COMPILE_SQL('<your Semantic SQL>')`."},"1401":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-106","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#the-ai-proposes-the-fields","content":"With `ai=None`, the notebook asks the AI only when a model is set up. The AI proposes business names, comments, synonyms and the metrics people will ask for. It works from names, types, grains, column notes and a category's most frequent values. It never receives a row, and never a sensitive column."},"1402":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-107","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#the-ai-proposes-the-fields","content":"Every metric the AI proposes is checked before the kit offers it. Semantic Views checks it again when the model is built. A refused metric is skipped, and the preview names it. Without a model, the fields keep the names the column maps give."},"1403":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-108","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#the-ai-proposes-the-fields","content":"To set up the AI model, see Set up Exasol."},"1404":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-109","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#keep-the-model-current","content":"Approving a column map rebuilds every model its table is in. After you add a link or a table, refresh the model yourself:"},"1405":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-110","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#keep-the-model-current","content":"Your AI clients read the same model through the Exasol MCP server. The notebook and the clients answer from one meaning."},"1406":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views-111","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/semantic-views#keep-the-model-current","content":"Back to Explore and understand. Previous: Approve the column map. Next: Linked tables."},"1407":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","type":"page","content":"Troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Explore and understand"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting"},"1408":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","content":"Fixes for approval, semantic model, question and sensitive-column messages in the Explore stage."},"1409":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","content":"Each entry starts with the message or symptom you see. Find it, then read the fix."},"1410":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","content":"Explore, Ask and Share read only an approved column map. A step given a draft raises `DescriptorNotApproved`. Open `00_quickstart`, review the map and approve it. The message says the same."},"1411":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","content":"The message is a `DescriptorNotApproved` error. Explore, Ask and Share do not read a draft. Open `00_quickstart` and approve the map. This is the same error as the entry above."},"1412":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","content":"You approved a different dataset in the quickstart while this notebook was open. Run this notebook's first cell again. It switches to the newly approved dataset."},"1413":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","content":"A warning about a column that gives the target away is not an error. The column stays in the map and is left out of the model. Read the warning, check the column, and approve. If the column is correct, keep it in the map. The model still leaves it out. For the rule, see Columns that give the answer away."},"1414":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","content":"A target must hold 0 and 1, or true and false. A column with other values cannot be predicted. Pick another column, or leave the target empty and explore the data without one."},"1415":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","content":"The dataset has no text column. `amazon_sales` and `fraud_transactions` have none, so the text steps skip on them and say so."},"1416":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","content":"The step needs a column the approved map does not give it. The step prints which role is missing. Set the slot in the column map, or use a dataset that has the column."},"1417":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","content":"The rules drafter drafts only the question shapes it knows. Rephrase the question, or write the SQL yourself with `proposed_sql=` and approve it. If the query cannot run, the message says why. If the MCP server does not answer, run `exakit mcp-doctor`."},"1418":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","content":"The approval still stands, and the message says why. Retry with `exakit describe <id> --comments`, or refresh the model with `nb.refresh_semantic(connection, \"<name>\")` once the cause is fixed."},"1419":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","content":"Under `~/.exasol-starter-kit`:"},"1420":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","content":"Column maps and their versions, in `descriptors/`."},"1421":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","content":"Semantic model definitions, in `semantic/`, so a refresh rebuilds a model the same way."},"1422":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","content":"Workflow logs, in `workflows/`. See Get the data for the workflow log."},"1423":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","content":"Hand-off bundles, written by the share stage."},"1424":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","content":"No. Every step runs without one. A model is used only to draft SQL in Ask and to sort texts into themes, and both are off until you turn them on. Ask also has a drafter with no model: `nb.draft_question`."},"1425":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","content":"The kit marks a column as sensitive when its values look like personal data: e-mail addresses, phone numbers, IBANs or postcodes. A sensitive column is never charted, grouped or sent to a model, and it is never exposed in the semantic model. The card says so beside the column. A sensitive column cannot be the target, a category or an entity."},"1426":{"id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/explore/troubleshooting","content":"Back to Explore and understand. Previous: Is my data sent anywhere?."},"1427":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","type":"page","content":"External sources","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Get the data"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources"},"1428":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","content":"Connect a database or lake that stays where it is, read its tables as you query them, connect from this computer, and keep passwords out of the notebook."},"1429":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#the-kinds-the-kit-can-connect","content":"The kinds the kit can connect"},"1430":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#connect-from-this-computer","content":"Connect from this computer"},"1431":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#a-lakehouse","content":"A lakehouse"},"1432":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#an-example-a-postgresql-source","content":"An example: a PostgreSQL source"},"1433":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#step-by-step-a-new-external-source","content":"Step by step: a new external source"},"1434":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#data-source","content":"Data source"},"1435":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#the-sources-own-settings","content":"The source's own settings"},"1436":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#how-to-fill-it-in","content":"How to fill it in"},"1437":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#details-and-optional-settings","content":"Details and optional settings"},"1438":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#test-connection-then-connect-and-use-this-data","content":"Test connection, then Connect and use this data"},"1439":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#passwords","content":"Passwords"},"1440":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#live-sources-and-ai","content":"Live sources and AI"},"1441":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","content":"An external source is a database or a lake somewhere else. The kit reads it where it lives. Nothing is copied. The kit connects it as a **virtual schema**, which is a schema in your local database whose tables point at the source. A query fetches the rows it needs at the moment you run it."},"1442":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","content":"The kit connects through its source engine, the same engine `exakit connect` runs."},"1443":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#the-kinds-the-kit-can-connect","content":"PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQL Server, Oracle, Snowflake, BigQuery, Databricks and MongoDB."},"1444":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#the-kinds-the-kit-can-connect","content":"Iceberg and Delta tables through a lakehouse catalog: Iceberg REST, Unity Catalog or AWS Glue."},"1445":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#the-kinds-the-kit-can-connect","content":"A folder of Parquet files, or document files in S3 or Azure Blob Storage."},"1446":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#the-kinds-the-kit-can-connect","content":"These helpers list the kinds and what each one asks:"},"1447":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#connect-from-this-computer","content":"The database runs in its own virtual machine. On macOS, the database cannot reach this computer as `localhost`."},"1448":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#connect-from-this-computer","content":"Use `192.168.64.1` for a database on this computer. If you give `localhost` or `127.0.0.1` on macOS, the kit replaces it with that address and prints one line about it. The source must then listen on that address too, not only on the loopback address."},"1449":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#connect-from-this-computer","content":"For a cloud source, allow this computer's public IP address at the source. The card shows the address. `exakit connect` shows it as its first line on a terminal."},"1450":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#a-lakehouse","content":"A lakehouse is one connector for several things. It has two settings: a catalog, and where its files are. Each combination asks for different details. In the **Data source** list it appears as a tree. Pick a leaf and both settings are chosen. Pick the lakehouse itself and the settings are asked one at a time."},"1451":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#a-lakehouse","content":"Some combinations have two secrets: the catalog login and the storage keys. The catalog login is asked like any password. The storage keys go to the kit in a file only you can read, and the file is removed as soon as the kit has read it."},"1452":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#an-example-a-postgresql-source","content":"This example reads a PostgreSQL database that runs on this computer. Your connector, host, database and table will differ."},"1453":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#an-example-a-postgresql-source","content":"Run the cells in order. The reading shows what the connection string did not give. The test checks the inputs and whether this computer reaches the host and port. It changes nothing. The connect step runs the kit's connect command and makes the virtual schema."},"1454":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#step-by-step-a-new-external-source","content":"Under **External sources**, the **Choose your data** card lists the connections you have. Tick one or more and the tables to read from each, then press **Use this data**."},"1455":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#step-by-step-a-new-external-source","content":"Tick **New connection…** and a single form opens under the list, two fields to a row. There is no step to press through: you pick the source, fill in the form, and press one button."},"1456":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#data-source","content":"One list of every kind of source the kit connects, each with a line saying what it is. Type in the box at its top to narrow it. The list opens inside the card, under the field, so it never covers the page."},"1457":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#data-source","content":"The card does not hold this list. It asks the kit (`nb.connectors()`), which answers with what `exakit connect` offers. A source added to the kit appears here without a change to the notebook."},"1458":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-30","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#the-sources-own-settings","content":"Shown only for a source that has several kinds in one. Each setting is its own list, in the order the kit asks them. A lakehouse, for example, asks for its catalog, then where its files are, then how to sign in."},"1459":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-31","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#the-sources-own-settings","content":"A choice decides what the next lists offer. The card asks the kit again after each pick (`nb.connector_inputs(source, catalog=...)`) and takes the kit's default for the settings that follow, so the details below are always the ones that combination needs. A choice the kit does not support yet is shown greyed out with its reason."},"1460":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-32","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#how-to-fill-it-in","content":"**Fill in the details** shows every question below. **Paste a connection string** adds a box for the string: paste it and the kit reads it (`nb.read_connection_string`), fills in the details, and marks only what the string did not hold."},"1461":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-33","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#details-and-optional-settings","content":"Everything `exakit connect` asks for that source, in one place:"},"1462":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-34","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#details-and-optional-settings","content":"Part"},"1463":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-35","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#details-and-optional-settings","content":"What is in it"},"1464":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-36","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#details-and-optional-settings","content":"Details"},"1465":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-37","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#details-and-optional-settings","content":"The name (alias) first: lower case, for example `sales`, and its tables appear as `VS_SALES`. Then every required input, such as the host, the database, the account and the password."},"1466":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-38","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#details-and-optional-settings","content":"Optional settings"},"1467":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-39","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#details-and-optional-settings","content":"A port, a schema, TLS, a CA certificate file and the like. Each shows the kit's default. Change one only to use another value."},"1468":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-40","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#details-and-optional-settings","content":"The password goes into a hidden box. It is never shown, saved or logged by the card."},"1469":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-41","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#test-connection-then-connect-and-use-this-data","content":"**Test connection** checks the inputs and whether this computer reaches the source. It changes nothing and needs no password. **Connect and use this data** runs the kit's connect command with the password on its standard input, then loads what you ticked."},"1470":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-42","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#test-connection-then-connect-and-use-this-data","content":"From an empty card that is two picks and one button: tick **New connection…**, pick the data source, fill in the form, press **Connect and use this data**."},"1471":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-43","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#passwords","content":"A password is asked in a hidden box. The kit receives it on its standard input."},"1472":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-44","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#passwords","content":"It is never written into a cell, the code view, a command line or the workflow log."},"1473":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-45","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#passwords","content":"A password inside a connection string is used and never shown."},"1474":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-46","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#passwords","content":"In Marimo there is no hidden box. Pass a password field, `mo.ui.text(kind=\"password\")`, as the `password` argument, or pass a `password_file`."},"1475":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-47","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#live-sources-and-ai","content":"A table from an external source is read from the source as you query it. Before sampled rows from a live source go to a model, the notebook names the source and asks. Only a yes sends them. A table in the database does not ask."},"1476":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources-48","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources#live-sources-and-ai","content":"Back to Get the data. Next: The data map."},"1477":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","type":"page","content":"Get the data","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Get the data"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data"},"1478":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","content":"Choose where your data comes from, load it, connect an external source, and read every table in the data map."},"1479":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#where-you-do-it","content":"Where you do it"},"1480":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#several-tables-at-once","content":"Several tables at once"},"1481":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#in-this-stage","content":"In this stage"},"1482":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#what-you-have-at-the-end","content":"What you have at the end"},"1483":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","content":"Every data project starts with data that is in one place, can be read again, and is the same each time you read it. In this stage you put a table in front of the kit. The kit offers three origins: a sample dataset that comes with the kit, your own file or folder, and an external database or lake that the kit reads live. Each origin ends in a table the rest of the workflow can describe."},"1484":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","content":"The flow is the same for all three origins. Only the first loading step differs. A sample dataset loads once and stays. Your file is copied into a table. An external source stays where it is: the kit creates a **virtual schema**, a schema in your local database whose tables point at a database or lake somewhere else. Its name is `VS_<NAME>`, where `<NAME>` is the name you gave the connection. Its tables are read when you query them."},"1485":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","content":"You do not need a terminal for this stage. Every step runs from a cell or a card. The terminal commands are listed for scripts and for people who prefer them."},"1486":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#where-you-do-it","content":"Guided view"},"1487":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#where-you-do-it","content":"Notebook code"},"1488":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#where-you-do-it","content":"Terminal"},"1489":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#where-you-do-it","content":"The **Choose your data** card in `00_quickstart`. Tick kit datasets, your own tables and external sources, any number of them together."},"1490":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#where-you-do-it","content":"The shared cells in `00_quickstart`, under *Choose a dataset*, *Load your own data*, *An external source*: `SAMPLE`, `MY_DATA`, `MY_SCHEMA`, `MY_TABLE`, `CONNECTOR`, `SOURCE_URL`, `SOURCE`, then `nb.first(...)`, which picks the first loaded source"},"1491":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#where-you-do-it","content":"`exakit data-load` for a kit dataset, a file or a folder. `exakit connect` for an external source."},"1492":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#several-tables-at-once","content":"The three options of the **Choose your data** card are tick boxes, and so is every list under them: datasets, your tables, connections, and the tables of each connection. Tick what you want from any mix of them and press **Use this data**."},"1493":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#several-tables-at-once","content":"What the card does"},"1494":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#several-tables-at-once","content":"The cell it runs"},"1495":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#several-tables-at-once","content":"Loads each ticked table"},"1496":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#several-tables-at-once","content":"The same cell as for one table: `nb.load_sample`, `nb.use_table`, `nb.dataset` or `nb.load_source`"},"1497":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#several-tables-at-once","content":"Keeps each one by its table name"},"1498":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#several-tables-at-once","content":"`chosen_tables[<table>] = ...`"},"1499":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#several-tables-at-once","content":"Opens the column map on the first"},"1500":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#several-tables-at-once","content":"`chosen_data = chosen_tables[<table>]`"},"1501":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#several-tables-at-once","content":"A table that could not be loaded is named under the card with the kit's reason. The others are used."},"1502":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#several-tables-at-once","content":"What follows from the choice:"},"1503":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#several-tables-at-once","content":"**What each column means** shows a *Table* list when you chose more than one. It says how many still need approval. Picking another table opens its column map; each table is approved on its own."},"1504":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#several-tables-at-once","content":"**Semantic views** starts with the schemas of your tables ticked, so **Find links between them** and **Publish the model** work on the same choice. See Semantic views."},"1505":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#several-tables-at-once","content":"With one table ticked the card runs the cells it always ran, and `chosen_tables` is not created."},"1506":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Sample datasets\" href=\"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets\" description=\"amazon_sales and fraud_transactions: what is in each, with the numbers\" />"},"1507":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Your own file\" href=\"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files\" description=\"Load a CSV, Parquet, JSON or Excel file, a folder, or a table already in the database\" />"},"1508":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-30","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"External sources\" href=\"/data-scientist/get-the-data/external-sources\" description=\"Connect a database or lake that stays where it is, step by step, and handle passwords\" />"},"1509":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-31","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"The data map\" href=\"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map\" description=\"Every table by origin, its column map state and its links\" />"},"1510":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-32","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"The dataset\" href=\"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset\" description=\"A table with its approved column map, and how a notebook picks one\" />"},"1511":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-33","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Troubleshooting\" href=\"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting\" description=\"File, source and table problems\" />"},"1512":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-34","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#what-you-have-at-the-end","content":"A table that the kit can describe, chosen by `nb.first(...)` as `chosen_data`, and a data map that shows it. The table has no approved column map yet. The next stage reviews the roles and approves them."},"1513":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data-35","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data#what-you-have-at-the-end","content":"Next: Explore and understand."},"1514":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","type":"page","content":"Sample datasets","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Get the data"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets"},"1515":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","content":"The two datasets that come with the kit, what is in each, the numbers you should see, and how the first cell loads one."},"1516":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#load-one","content":"Load one"},"1517":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"How we used it: amazon_sales"},"1518":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"How we used it: fraud_transactions"},"1519":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","content":"The kit ships two sample datasets, so you can run every stage before you bring your own data. `amazon_sales` is a clean table of orders. `fraud_transactions` has repeats, gaps and placeholders on purpose, so the cleaning steps have something to find. Both load with the same cell."},"1520":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#load-one","content":"The first cell of `00_quickstart` picks the dataset:"},"1521":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#load-one","content":"If the dataset is not in the database, the cell runs `exakit data-load amazon_sales` and waits for it. If it is already there, the cell says it is loaded and uses it. `nb.sample_datasets()` lists the kit's datasets and which are loaded."},"1522":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"The table is `AMAZON.ORDER_LINES`. It holds order lines of one fashion seller. Each row is one line of an order, so the key is `ORDER_LINE_ID`, and the time column is `ORDER_DATE`. The target for the worked examples is `CANCELLED`, which is 1 when the line was cancelled."},"1523":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"These numbers come from a real local database, read with read-only queries on 12 November 2026:"},"1524":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"Query"},"1525":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"Result"},"1526":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"`COUNT(*)`"},"1527":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"128,975 rows"},"1528":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"`COUNT(DISTINCT ORDER_ID)`"},"1529":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"120,378 orders"},"1530":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"`MIN` and `MAX` of `ORDER_DATE`"},"1531":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"2022-03-31 to 2022-06-29"},"1532":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"`CANCELLED = 1`"},"1533":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"18,332 rows, 14.2% of the lines"},"1534":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"Two facts matter for the later stages:"},"1535":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"**Many lines per order.** 128,975 lines belong to 120,378 orders, so an order can have more than one line. Count orders with `COUNT(DISTINCT ORDER_ID)` when you mean orders."},"1536":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"**STATUS gives the target away.** Every cancelled line has `STATUS = 'Cancelled'`, and no other line does. Run `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM AMAZON.ORDER_LINES WHERE STATUS = 'Cancelled'`: it returns 18,332, the same as `CANCELLED = 1`. A model that sees `STATUS` learns the answer from it, not from the order. Prepare shows how the kit catches this."},"1537":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"The table is `FRAUD.TRANSACTIONS`: 51,000 card and bank transactions. Of these, 2,510 are fraud (4.9%)."},"1538":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"The table is messy on purpose. The dataset's README (`data/datasets/fraud_transactions/README.md`) records what is wrong with it:"},"1539":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"**Repeated ids.** `TRANSACTION_ID` is not unique. 51,000 rows hold 50,000 distinct ids, so 1,000 ids appear twice. The README counts 881 exact copies and 119 copies that disagree. `ROW_ID` is the key for this table."},"1540":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"**Placeholders.** `DEVICE_USED` has 1,530 rows `Unknown Device`, and `PAYMENT_METHOD` has 1,530 rows `Invalid Method`. They look like categories, but they mean \"not known\"."},"1541":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"**Gaps.** Some values are missing, and the README says about 5% of `DEVICE_USED` and `PAYMENT_METHOD` are NULL."},"1542":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"The kit does not clean this table. The cleaning is part of the work, and it is covered in Prepare."},"1543":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/sample-datasets#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"Back to Get the data. Next: Your own file."},"1544":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","type":"page","content":"The data map","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Get the data"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map"},"1545":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","content":"What nb.data_map shows for each table, how it finds links between tables, and what it does not read."},"1546":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#the-data-map","content":"The data map"},"1547":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#how-links-are-found","content":"How links are found"},"1548":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","content":"The data map lists every table the kit can see, grouped by where it came from. It is the place to check what you have before you choose a dataset."},"1549":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#the-data-map","content":"The map has one table per origin: external sources first, then your data, then the samples. Each table shows its rows, its column map state and its roles. Under the tables it lists the links between them."},"1550":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#the-data-map","content":"`nb.data_map(connection)` reads the database's metadata, and only the metadata. It does not read rows from your tables."},"1551":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#the-data-map","content":"Column"},"1552":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#the-data-map","content":"What it shows"},"1553":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#the-data-map","content":"Origin"},"1554":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#the-data-map","content":"`Sample data`, `Your data` or `External source`"},"1555":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#the-data-map","content":"Table"},"1556":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#the-data-map","content":"`SCHEMA.TABLE`. A virtual table shows its rows as `live`."},"1557":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#the-data-map","content":"Column map"},"1558":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#the-data-map","content":"`none yet`, `draft`, `approved vN`, or `shipped` for a kit dataset. It also says whether the table is in a semantic model."},"1559":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#the-data-map","content":"Roles"},"1560":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#the-data-map","content":"The slots by name, then a count of each role"},"1561":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#the-data-map","content":"The map returns a DataFrame through `data.tables`, `data.columns` and `data.links`."},"1562":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#how-links-are-found","content":"Links come from three places:"},"1563":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#how-links-are-found","content":"An approved schema map gives its links."},"1564":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#how-links-are-found","content":"A semantic model you published gives its links."},"1565":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#how-links-are-found","content":"The rest are **possible** links, or **shared dimensions**."},"1566":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#how-links-are-found","content":"Two tables are a **possible** link when they have a key-like column with the same name, for example `ID`, `_ID` or `_CODE`. They are a **shared dimension** when they share a name such as `STATE`, `REGION`, `CATEGORY`, `MONTH` or `YEAR`."},"1567":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#how-links-are-found","content":"A possible link is a lead to check, not a join the kit made for you. Check either kind before you join on it."},"1568":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-data-map#how-links-are-found","content":"Back to Get the data. Next: The dataset."},"1569":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset","type":"page","content":"The dataset","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Get the data"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset"},"1570":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset","content":"What a dataset is, how a notebook picks one, and why its queries come from roles rather than column names."},"1571":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset#pick-the-dataset-for-each-notebook","content":"Pick the dataset for each notebook"},"1572":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset#why-queries-come-from-roles","content":"Why queries come from roles"},"1573":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset","content":"A **dataset** is a table with its approved column map. The column map says what each column is for: its role, and the slot the steps use. The notebooks never read a table directly. They read a dataset and build every query from its roles."},"1574":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset","content":"`nb.dataset(...)` refuses a column map that is not approved. You approve a column map in Explore and understand."},"1575":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset#pick-the-dataset-for-each-notebook","content":"One assignment picks the data for each notebook: `SAMPLE = \"...\"` in the quickstart and `DATASET = \"...\"` in the other notebooks. With `DATASET = None`, each notebook follows the dataset you approved last. Approve a different one in the quickstart. The other notebooks pick it up when you run their first cell again."},"1576":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset#pick-the-dataset-for-each-notebook","content":"To pin one notebook to one dataset, set `DATASET = \"...\"` in that notebook."},"1577":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset#why-queries-come-from-roles","content":"Because queries come from roles, the same cell runs on `amazon_sales`, on `fraud_transactions` and on your own table. A role no column fits is never guessed. `dataset.has(...)` is false, the step that needs it skips, and the step says why."},"1578":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/the-dataset#why-queries-come-from-roles","content":"Back to Get the data. Next: Troubleshooting."},"1579":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","type":"page","content":"Troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Get the data"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting"},"1580":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"What the kit says when a file will not load, a source is not connected, or a connected table does not read, and what to do about each."},"1581":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"Each entry gives the message the kit shows, then what to do."},"1582":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"Yes. Load a file with `nb.load_own_file(...)`, or use a table already in the database with `nb.use_table(...)`. Both are shown on Your own file."},"1583":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"Approve it in the quickstart. With `DATASET = None`, the other notebooks follow the dataset you approved last, when you run their first cell again. To pin one notebook to a dataset, set `DATASET = \"...\"` in that notebook. See The dataset."},"1584":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"The kit names the reason in one line. The usual ones:"},"1585":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"Message"},"1586":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"What to do"},"1587":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"`... is not a file load_own_file reads`"},"1588":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"Use a CSV, Parquet, JSON or Excel file, or a folder of them."},"1589":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"`... has columns that are the same name in SQL`"},"1590":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"Rename the columns in the file so each name is different."},"1591":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"`... holds no rows`"},"1592":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"Check the file. An empty file cannot be loaded."},"1593":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"`... already exists and was not loaded by load_own_file`"},"1594":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"Name another table. To replace the table, pass `replace=True` on purpose."},"1595":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"`'...' is not SCHEMA.TABLE`"},"1596":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"Use plain SQL names: letters, digits and `_`, starting with a letter."},"1597":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"The message is `<name> was not connected:` and the lines after it give the reason. The usual causes:"},"1598":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"Reason"},"1599":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"What to do"},"1600":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"The source refuses the connection, or the connection times out"},"1601":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"Allow this computer's address at the source: a firewall rule, a security group or the server's access list."},"1602":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"The password or user is refused"},"1603":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"Check the user, then enter the password again in the hidden box."},"1604":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"A certificate cannot be verified"},"1605":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"Give the source's CA certificate in the optional settings."},"1606":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"The schema is not found"},"1607":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"Check the schema name and its case."},"1608":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"The host name does not resolve"},"1609":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"Read the note the kit gives. It tells you whether the name is wrong, or whether this network's DNS does not answer. Another network, a VPN, or a DNS server of 1.1.1.1 or 8.8.8.8 on this computer can fix it."},"1610":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-30","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"Use **Test connection** first. It checks the inputs and reaches the source, and changes nothing. To check a connected source later, run `exakit source check <name>`, or `exakit source issues` to list the sources that fail and the command that fixes each."},"1611":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-31","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"`nb.load_source` reads one row to check the table. If it fails, the message names the table and the reason. Run `exakit source check <name>`. If the source has new tables, run `exakit source refresh <name>`."},"1612":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-32","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"More entries are on Set up Exasol: Troubleshooting."},"1613":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting-33","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/troubleshooting","content":"Back to Get the data. Next: Explore and understand."},"1614":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","type":"page","content":"Your own file","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Get the data"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files"},"1615":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","content":"Load a CSV, Parquet, JSON or Excel file, or a folder of them, as a table. Use a table already in the database, and describe its roles by hand."},"1616":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#load-a-file-or-a-folder","content":"Load a file or a folder"},"1617":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#what-the-load-accepts","content":"What the load accepts"},"1618":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#how-the-columns-are-prepared","content":"How the columns are prepared"},"1619":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#use-a-table-that-is-already-there","content":"Use a table that is already there"},"1620":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#roles-written-beside-a-file","content":"Roles written beside a file"},"1621":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","content":"Your own file becomes a table in the database. The file is copied in, so queries run on the copy and not on the file. If the table is already in the database, you can use it without a copy."},"1622":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#load-a-file-or-a-folder","content":"The shared cells of `00_quickstart` take a file or a folder, a schema and an optional table:"},"1623":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#load-a-file-or-a-folder","content":"For a file called `orders.csv` in a folder called `sales-data`, with no schema named, the table is `SALES_DATA.ORDERS`. The table takes its name from the file."},"1624":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#load-a-file-or-a-folder","content":"To call the helper directly, use `nb.load_own_file(path, schema, conn=connection)`."},"1625":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#what-the-load-accepts","content":"**CSV, Parquet and JSON** work. JSON can be an array of records or one record per line. A nested value is kept as JSON text."},"1626":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#what-the-load-accepts","content":"**Excel** works too. The kit makes a CSV or UTF-8 copy next to your file and says so. Your original is not changed."},"1627":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#what-the-load-accepts","content":"**A folder** loads every CSV, Parquet and JSON file at its top level, one table per file, each named after its file. Subfolders are skipped. The schema is asked once."},"1628":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#what-the-load-accepts","content":"**Running it again is safe.** A file already loaded is not loaded twice. A file that changed is loaded again. The table keeps the file's SHA-256 in its comment, so the kit can tell."},"1629":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#how-the-columns-are-prepared","content":"When the kit loads a file, it prepares the columns this way:"},"1630":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#how-the-columns-are-prepared","content":"Column names become plain upper-case SQL names. Other characters become `_`. A name that starts with a digit gets a `C_` prefix."},"1631":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#how-the-columns-are-prepared","content":"Columns with the same name after this change stop the load. Rename them in the file."},"1632":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#how-the-columns-are-prepared","content":"Text that looks like dates (9 in 10 values parse as dates) is stored as `DATE`."},"1633":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#how-the-columns-are-prepared","content":"True and false values become `0` and `1`. Whole numbers become `DECIMAL(18,0)`. Other numbers become `DOUBLE`. Text becomes `VARCHAR` as wide as its longest value."},"1634":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#how-the-columns-are-prepared","content":"A file with no rows is refused."},"1635":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#use-a-table-that-is-already-there","content":"`nb.use_table(connection, \"MY_DATA.ORDERS\")` uses a table that is in the database. `nb.data_map(connection)` lists the tables, and the kit's own schemas are left out unless you pass `include_kit=True`. See The data map."},"1636":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#use-a-table-that-is-already-there","content":"If a table's columns kept names with spaces or small letters, such as `Won` or `Opportunity ID`, the kit's queries cannot read them directly. The kit then creates a view with plain names in `EXAKIT_PREPARED` and uses that view. Your table is not changed. The view is named `EXAKIT_PREPARED.\"<SCHEMA>__<TABLE>__PLAIN\"`."},"1637":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#roles-written-beside-a-file","content":"You can describe your file's roles by hand, instead of reviewing the kit's proposal. Pass a mapping of role to column to `nb.load_own_file(..., descriptor={...})`. The kit writes the roles next to the file as `<name>.descriptor.yaml`, so `DATASET = \"<the file>\"` in a notebook opens it again."},"1638":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#roles-written-beside-a-file","content":"The roles are a draft until you approve them. The approval is covered in Explore and understand."},"1639":{"id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/get-the-data/your-own-files#roles-written-beside-a-file","content":"Back to Get the data. Next: External sources."},"1640":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","type":"page","content":"Your AI model in this stage","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Model"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model"},"1641":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","content":"What an AI model may suggest in the model stage, what it is sent, and what the kit checks before any suggestion is tested."},"1642":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#your-ai-model-in-this-stage","content":"Your AI model in this stage"},"1643":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-is-sent","content":"What it is sent"},"1644":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"What it may suggest"},"1645":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-the-kit-checks-and-what-it-cannot","content":"What the kit checks, and what it cannot"},"1646":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#where-the-data-goes","content":"Where the data goes"},"1647":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#tracing","content":"Tracing"},"1648":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#set-it-up","content":"Set it up"},"1649":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#your-ai-model-in-this-stage","content":"The AI model is optional. Every step in the model stage runs without one. Without a model, `nb.feature_ideas(lab)` still returns the rule-based ideas. With a model, `nb.feature_ideas(lab, ai=True)` adds up to four more."},"1650":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#your-ai-model-in-this-stage","content":"Your model has one job here: it suggests feature ideas. It never sees rows, never approves a column map, and never runs SQL."},"1651":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-is-sent","content":"The code in `lab.py` builds one request with these parts:"},"1652":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-is-sent","content":"the target's name"},"1653":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-is-sent","content":"every column name and its role. A column marked sensitive is left out."},"1654":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-is-sent","content":"the cross-validated score of each model so far, rounded to three decimals"},"1655":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-is-sent","content":"the five kinds of idea it may suggest"},"1656":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-is-sent","content":"a rule: suggest up to four, use only those kinds and existing column names, and never use the target or a column filled in after the outcome"},"1657":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-is-sent","content":"No row and no value is sent."},"1658":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"Five kinds only. The kit builds each one as SQL and tests it like any other idea."},"1659":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"Kind"},"1660":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"Columns"},"1661":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"The SQL the kit writes"},"1662":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"`ratio_to_group`"},"1663":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"a measure and a category"},"1664":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"`\"m\" / AVG(\"m\") OVER (PARTITION BY \"c\")`"},"1665":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"`combine`"},"1666":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"two categories"},"1667":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"`` `\"a\" \\|\\| ' · ' \\|\\| \"b\"` ``"},"1668":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"`days_since`"},"1669":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"a date"},"1670":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"`DAYS_BETWEEN(CURRENT_DATE, \"d\")`"},"1671":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-30","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"`as_number`"},"1672":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-31","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"one column"},"1673":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-32","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"`CAST(\"c\" AS DOUBLE)`"},"1674":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-33","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"`is_missing`"},"1675":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-34","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"one column"},"1676":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-35","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"`CASE WHEN \"c\" IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END`"},"1677":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-36","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-it-may-suggest","content":"A suggestion of another kind, or with the wrong number of columns, is dropped."},"1678":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-37","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-the-kit-checks-and-what-it-cannot","content":"The kit checks two things. It drops a suggestion that names the target, and a suggestion that names a column the data does not have. It reads up to four suggestions and no more."},"1679":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-38","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#what-the-kit-checks-and-what-it-cannot","content":"The prompt also tells the model not to use a column written after the outcome. The kit cannot check that by itself. The verdict from `nb.try_feature` and your reading of the SQL are the check. An idea that scores above 0.98 on the held-out rows gets the verdict `suspicious`, and the kit tells you not to keep it."},"1680":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-39","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#where-the-data-goes","content":"The model is the endpoint you set. It is called only when you pass `ai=True`, or when you run the themes step. With a model set up, feature ideas send names and roles, never rows."},"1681":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-40","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#where-the-data-goes","content":"The optional themes step in `01_explore` is different. It sends a sample of the newest texts on each side of the target to your model, so it needs a text column. The practice datasets have none, so the step skips."},"1682":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-41","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#tracing","content":"When Langfuse is set up, each call is traced. Pass `conn=connection` to `nb.feature_ideas`, and the call goes into one trace named `feature-ideas`, tagged with the database session. Set-up is on AI and Langfuse."},"1683":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-42","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#set-it-up","content":"Run `nb.model_setup()` in a notebook, or call `nb.use_model(MODEL_ID, PROVIDER_BASE_URL)` yourself. Without one, `nb.feature_ideas(lab, ai=True)` stops with the message \"No AI model is set up\". Check what is set with `nb.model_settings()`. The providers and where to find their keys are on Set up Exasol."},"1684":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-43","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#set-it-up","content":"The model is never asked to approve anything, and it never changes your data."},"1685":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model-44","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/ai-model#set-it-up","content":"Back to Model. Troubleshooting is on Model: when it goes wrong."},"1686":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline","type":"page","content":"Start with a baseline","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Model"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/baseline"},"1687":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/baseline","content":"The simplest model you can build, and the score a real model has to beat."},"1688":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/baseline#start-with-a-baseline","content":"Start with a baseline"},"1689":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/baseline#the-notebook-baseline","content":"The notebook baseline"},"1690":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/baseline#do-not-judge-a-rare-answer-by-accuracy","content":"Do not judge a rare answer by accuracy"},"1691":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/baseline#where-to-go-next","content":"Where to go next"},"1692":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/baseline","content":"A model with every column is only worth keeping if it does better than a simple rule. The baseline is that simple rule. If a real model cannot beat it, the columns carry little signal about the outcome. The kit has two baselines."},"1693":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/baseline#start-with-a-baseline","content":"**The notebook baseline** is a small logistic regression in `01_explore`. It uses three inputs: the category, the state and the month of the date."},"1694":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/baseline#start-with-a-baseline","content":"**The lab's baseline** is the model called `baseline` in each prediction task. For yes or no, it always gives the common answer. A constant prediction scores 0.5 ROC AUC, so any real model should score above 0.5."},"1695":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/baseline#the-notebook-baseline","content":"The cell reads the newest 20,000 rows when the table has a date, or the first 20,000 by key when it has none. The key makes a rerun read the same rows. The cell builds the features from the category, the state and the month, then trains this pipeline:"},"1696":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/baseline#the-notebook-baseline","content":"`OneHotEncoder` turns each value of the category, the state and the month into a 0 or 1 column."},"1697":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/baseline#the-notebook-baseline","content":"`class_weight=\"balanced\"` tells the model to weigh the rarer answer more, so it does not just predict the common one."},"1698":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/baseline#the-notebook-baseline","content":"The split is stratified, which keeps the same share of 1s on both sides, with a fixed seed (`random_state=0`). A quarter of the rows is kept back."},"1699":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/baseline#the-notebook-baseline","content":"The cell prints how many rows it trained on and how many it kept back. It uses a category or an entity only when that column is not flagged by `nb.leakage_check`. The notebook's comment gives the reason for the check: a column written after the outcome \"predicts the target perfectly on old rows and fails on new rows.\""},"1700":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/baseline#the-notebook-baseline","content":"For `amazon_sales`, the baseline reads `CATEGORY`, `SHIP_STATE` and the month of `ORDER_DATE`. It never reads `STATUS`."},"1701":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/baseline#do-not-judge-a-rare-answer-by-accuracy","content":"When the answer is rare, accuracy is misleading. A model that always says \"not fraud\" is about 95% accurate on `fraud_transactions`, because 2,510 of its 51,000 rows are fraud (4.9%). `nb.data_checks` reports the rare answer and says what the always-common guess achieves. The readout note also compares every score with that guess. The reasons, and the metric the kit uses instead, are on the rare answers page of Evaluate."},"1702":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/baseline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/baseline#where-to-go-next","content":"The lab trains many models on the same rows: The model lab. Back to Model."},"1703":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","type":"page","content":"Feature ideas","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Model"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas"},"1704":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","content":"New inputs built from the columns you already have, the SQL that builds each one, and the verdict the kit gives after it is tried on the same split."},"1705":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#feature-ideas","content":"Feature ideas"},"1706":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#the-ideas-the-kit-makes","content":"The ideas the kit makes"},"1707":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#try-an-idea","content":"Try an idea"},"1708":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#keep-an-idea","content":"Keep an idea"},"1709":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#feature-ideas","content":"A feature idea is a new input for the model, made from columns you already have. The kit proposes them, writes the SQL that builds each one, and tests them. You decide which ones to keep. Nothing is kept by default."},"1710":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#the-ideas-the-kit-makes","content":"`nb.feature_ideas(lab)` makes these, when the data has the columns for them. It returns at most eight."},"1711":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#the-ideas-the-kit-makes","content":"**How long ago the date was**, when the table has a date. Newer and older records can behave differently."},"1712":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#the-ideas-the-kit-makes","content":"**A measure compared with its category's usual value**, for the first two measures and the first two categories."},"1713":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#the-ideas-the-kit-makes","content":"**Two categories together**, such as a category with a certain state."},"1714":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#the-ideas-the-kit-makes","content":"**A category column that holds numbers, read as a number**, when it has more than two values. The model can then learn that more is worse, or better."},"1715":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#the-ideas-the-kit-makes","content":"**Whether a measure is missing**, when more than 0.5% of its rows are blank."},"1716":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#the-ideas-the-kit-makes","content":"**Whether a long text mentions a problem**, for a text column with long values. The words are price, slow, crash, wrong, cancel and a few others in `NEGATIVE_WORDS`."},"1717":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#the-ideas-the-kit-makes","content":"Each idea shows its title, the reason it was proposed, and the SQL. Read the SQL before you keep it. It is the same expression the kit would run on your table."},"1718":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#try-an-idea","content":"`nb.try_feature(lab, idea)` retrains the picked model with the idea added. It uses the same split and the same cross-validation folds, so the two scores can be compared. It returns a verdict and the idea's values as a series."},"1719":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#try-an-idea","content":"Verdict"},"1720":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#try-an-idea","content":"When"},"1721":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#try-an-idea","content":"What it means"},"1722":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#try-an-idea","content":"`suspicious`"},"1723":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#try-an-idea","content":"The held-out score is above 0.98 for yes or no, or above 0.995 for a number"},"1724":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#try-an-idea","content":"The idea probably gives the answer away. Do not keep it."},"1725":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#try-an-idea","content":"`helps`"},"1726":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#try-an-idea","content":"Cross-validation rises by 0.005 or more, and the held-out score does not fall by more than 0.002"},"1727":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#try-an-idea","content":"Keep it, if you can explain why it should work."},"1728":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#try-an-idea","content":"`hurts`"},"1729":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#try-an-idea","content":"Cross-validation falls by 0.005 or more"},"1730":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#try-an-idea","content":"Leave it out."},"1731":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#try-an-idea","content":"`same`"},"1732":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#try-an-idea","content":"Anything else"},"1733":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#try-an-idea","content":"Not worth the extra column."},"1734":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-30","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#try-an-idea","content":"These thresholds are the kit's rules of thumb. They are not statistical tests. A verdict of `helps` on a small held-out set can still be chance. Read the number of rows held out, and `cv_sd`, before you believe it."},"1735":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-31","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#keep-an-idea","content":"To keep an idea, pass its series to the next lab with `features=`:"},"1736":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-32","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#keep-an-idea","content":"The notebook's `01_explore` does this for the first three ideas. It keeps the ones with the verdict `helps` and drops the others. A kept idea is used on the next run of the lab cell."},"1737":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas-33","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas#keep-an-idea","content":"Back to Model. The AI model's part in feature ideas is on Your AI model in this stage."},"1738":{"id":"/data-scientist/model","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","type":"page","content":"Model","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Model"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model"},"1739":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model","content":"Train a simple baseline, then use the model lab to try better models and feature ideas on the same split."},"1740":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model#the-flow","content":"The flow"},"1741":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model#where-you-do-it","content":"Where you do it"},"1742":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model#how-we-used-it","content":"How we used it"},"1743":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model#in-this-stage","content":"In this stage"},"1744":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model#what-you-have-at-the-end","content":"What you have at the end"},"1745":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model","content":"Modelling turns the columns you approved into a prediction: will this order be cancelled, is this payment fraud, which rows look unusual. A model is only useful if it beats a simple guess, so start with the simplest one and improve it step by step. The kit gives you a baseline model in `01_explore`, a model lab that trains several models on the same rows, and feature ideas that you test before you keep them. Everything trains on this computer with scikit-learn, the Python machine-learning library the kit includes."},"1746":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model#where-you-do-it","content":"Guided view"},"1747":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model#where-you-do-it","content":"Notebook code"},"1748":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model#where-you-do-it","content":"Terminal"},"1749":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model#where-you-do-it","content":"`01_explore`: the **Build a model** card runs the model lab. The baseline's result is in the same notebook."},"1750":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model#where-you-do-it","content":"The cells **Train a baseline model** and **The model lab (optional)** in `01_explore`."},"1751":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model#where-you-do-it","content":"None. Training runs in the notebook."},"1752":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model#where-you-do-it","content":"The first cell of `01_explore` holds the settings. `DATASET` picks the data. `USE_PREPARED = True` makes the model read the typed, cleaned view that Prepare creates. The lab cell looks like this:"},"1753":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model#how-we-used-it","content":"The sample dataset `amazon_sales` is the table `AMAZON.ORDER_LINES`. It has 128,975 order lines. 18,332 of them (14.2%) are cancelled, which is the target `CANCELLED`."},"1754":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model#how-we-used-it","content":"**The baseline** uses three inputs only: the category, the state and the month of `ORDER_DATE`. It does not read `STATUS`, which gives the target away. See Start with a baseline."},"1755":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model#how-we-used-it","content":"**The lab** scores with ROC AUC, because the rarer answer is above 5%. It splits by time, so it learns from the older rows and is tested on the newer ones. See The model lab."},"1756":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model#how-we-used-it","content":"The messy dataset, `fraud_transactions`, has a rare answer, no date and placeholder values. Its differences are listed in The model lab."},"1757":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Start with a baseline\" href=\"/data-scientist/model/baseline\" description=\"The simplest model, and the score a real model must beat\" />"},"1758":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"The model lab\" href=\"/data-scientist/model/model-lab\" description=\"What the lab reads, how it splits the rows, and what it leaves out\" />"},"1759":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"The models the lab tries\" href=\"/data-scientist/model/the-models\" description=\"Every model, the rule that picks one, and the settings\" />"},"1760":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Feature ideas\" href=\"/data-scientist/model/feature-ideas\" description=\"New inputs built from your columns, and the verdict for each\" />"},"1761":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Your AI model in this stage\" href=\"/data-scientist/model/ai-model\" description=\"What an AI model may suggest here, and what it is sent\" />"},"1762":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Saving, MLflow and training in the database\" href=\"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow\" description=\"What is kept after a run, and where the in-database path starts\" />"},"1763":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"When it goes wrong\" href=\"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting\" description=\"The warnings and errors you see while you model\" />"},"1764":{"id":"/data-scientist/model-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model#what-you-have-at-the-end","content":"A baseline score, the lab's leaderboard with the model it picked, the importance list, and the feature ideas you kept with their verdicts. The next step is to check the score on rows the model never trained on, in Evaluate."},"1765":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","type":"page","content":"The model lab","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Model"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab"},"1766":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","content":"What the lab reads, how it splits the rows, what it leaves out, and what the model leans on."},"1767":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-tasks","content":"The tasks"},"1768":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"What the lab reads"},"1769":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-leaves-out-and-why","content":"What the lab leaves out, and why"},"1770":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-metric-and-the-split-for-amazon_sales","content":"The metric and the split for amazon_sales"},"1771":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-model-leans-on","content":"What the model leans on"},"1772":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-messy-dataset-fraud_transactions","content":"The messy dataset: fraud_transactions"},"1773":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#settings","content":"Settings"},"1774":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","content":"`nb.model_lab` trains one task on your approved data. It trains every model of that task on the same rows, scores each one, and picks the best. It is the second half of the model stage, after the baseline. The lab uses the same approved column map as the notebook baseline, but it reads more columns and more rows."},"1775":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-tasks","content":"Task"},"1776":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-tasks","content":"What it learns"},"1777":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-tasks","content":"Example"},"1778":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-tasks","content":"Predict yes or no"},"1779":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-tasks","content":"The 0/1 target"},"1780":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-tasks","content":"Will this order be cancelled?"},"1781":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-tasks","content":"Predict a number"},"1782":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-tasks","content":"A number you name with `target_number`"},"1783":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-tasks","content":"What will this order's amount be?"},"1784":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-tasks","content":"Find natural groups"},"1785":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-tasks","content":"Nothing: no outcome is needed"},"1786":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-tasks","content":"Which orders look alike?"},"1787":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-tasks","content":"Find unusual rows"},"1788":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-tasks","content":"Nothing: no outcome is needed"},"1789":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-tasks","content":"Which rows sit far from the rest?"},"1790":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"The kit decides the inputs from the roles in the column map. You do not type column names. The table gives each role's treatment."},"1791":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"Role"},"1792":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"How the lab uses it"},"1793":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"Left out when"},"1794":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"`measure`"},"1795":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"As a number"},"1796":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-30","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"It gives the answer away, or is personal data"},"1797":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-31","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"`category`, `flag`"},"1798":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-32","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"As groups: one 0 or 1 column per value"},"1799":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-33","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"It gives the answer away, or is personal data"},"1800":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-34","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"`time`"},"1801":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-35","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"Only the month of the date"},"1802":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-36","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"Never left out, but the full date is not used"},"1803":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-37","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"`key`, `identifier`"},"1804":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-38","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"Not used as inputs"},"1805":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-39","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"Almost every row is different"},"1806":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-40","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"`text`"},"1807":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-41","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"Not used, except through a feature idea"},"1808":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-42","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"Always. Free text is not a column the lab can read."},"1809":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-43","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"`other`"},"1810":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-44","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"Not used"},"1811":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-45","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"Always: its role says leave it out"},"1812":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-46","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"target"},"1813":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-47","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"The answer the model learns"},"1814":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-48","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"It is never an input"},"1815":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-49","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-reads","content":"The lab reads at most 50,000 rows (`ROW_LIMIT` in the code). When the table has a date, those are the newest rows. Otherwise the query sorts by its first column and keeps 50,000 rows."},"1816":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-50","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-leaves-out-and-why","content":"`lab_data.left_out` lists every column the lab did not use, with its reason. Read it after every run. The reasons come from the code in `lab.py`:"},"1817":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-51","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-leaves-out-and-why","content":"**gives the answer away**: the column is in the list from `nb.leakage_check`. See Leakage on the Evaluate pages."},"1818":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-52","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-leaves-out-and-why","content":"**personal data**: the column is marked sensitive in the column map. It is never used as an input."},"1819":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-53","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-leaves-out-and-why","content":"**different for (almost) every row, so there is nothing general to learn**: a key or an identifier."},"1820":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-54","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-leaves-out-and-why","content":"**free text: see the feature ideas**: a text column."},"1821":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-55","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-lab-leaves-out-and-why","content":"**marked Leave out**: the column's role is `other`."},"1822":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-56","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-metric-and-the-split-for-amazon_sales","content":"**The metric.** The rarer answer is 14.2% of rows, which is above 5%, so the lab scores with ROC AUC. Below 5%, it uses PR AUC instead. Both are explained on Reading ROC AUC and Metrics."},"1823":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-57","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-metric-and-the-split-for-amazon_sales","content":"**The rows.** `amazon_sales` has 128,975 rows, so the lab reads the newest 50,000 by `ORDER_DATE`."},"1824":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-58","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-metric-and-the-split-for-amazon_sales","content":"**The split.** `ORDER_DATE` is a date, so the lab uses a time split. It learns from the oldest 75% of those rows and is tested on the newest 25%."},"1825":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-59","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-metric-and-the-split-for-amazon_sales","content":"**The inputs.** Every measure, category and flag column the column map gives a role to, plus the month of the date. Keys, identifiers, text, personal data and the answer-givers are left out."},"1826":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-60","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-metric-and-the-split-for-amazon_sales","content":"Check `AMOUNT` before you trust the lab. The dataset README says `AMOUNT` and `QTY` change once an order is cancelled, so a model that reads them learns the answer it was given. The leakage check tests only columns with 2 to 50 distinct values (`GROUPABLE` in `data_checks.py`), so it may not flag `AMOUNT`. To see how many values it has, run `SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT \"AMOUNT\") FROM AMAZON.ORDER_LINES`. If `AMOUNT` tops `lab.importance`, leave it out yourself:"},"1827":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-61","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-model-leans-on","content":"`lab.importance` lists up to eight inputs, the strongest first. For each input, the kit scrambles its values on the held-out rows and measures how far the score drops. A large drop means the model relies on that input. Only inputs whose drop is above zero are listed."},"1828":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-62","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#what-the-model-leans-on","content":"The list is a lead, not proof. A value with few rows can look strong by chance."},"1829":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-63","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-messy-dataset-fraud_transactions","content":"The README of `fraud_transactions` gives 51,000 rows, with 4.9% of them fraud. Measured on the database, the table has 50,000 distinct `TRANSACTION_ID` values, so 1,000 ids appear twice. Three things change for the lab:"},"1830":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-64","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-messy-dataset-fraud_transactions","content":"**A rare answer.** Under 5% of rows are 1s, so the lab scores with PR AUC, which focuses on finding the rare rows. The lab records the reason in `lab.run.notes`: \"The 1s are rare, so the score is PR AUC, which focuses on finding them.\""},"1831":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-65","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-messy-dataset-fraud_transactions","content":"**No date.** The table has only the hour of the day. The lab splits at random, stratified so both sides keep the same share of fraud. With no date it sorts by the first column of its query and keeps 50,000 of the 51,000 rows. The notebook baseline reads the first 20,000 rows by `ROW_ID` and leaves the month out."},"1832":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-66","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#the-messy-dataset-fraud_transactions","content":"**Placeholder values.** The README lists 1,530 `Unknown Device` and 1,530 `Invalid Method` values. The lab does not clean them. Each placeholder becomes one more category value. To read the typed, cleaned view from Prepare instead, set `USE_PREPARED = True` in `01_explore`."},"1833":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-67","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#settings","content":"Pass settings by name. An unknown name is an error."},"1834":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-68","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#settings","content":"Setting"},"1835":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-69","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#settings","content":"What it does"},"1836":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-70","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#settings","content":"`train_pct`"},"1837":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-71","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#settings","content":"The share of rows used for training, from 50 to 90. The default is 75."},"1838":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-72","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#settings","content":"`split_method`"},"1839":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-73","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#settings","content":"`time`, `random` or `group`. See Hold-out."},"1840":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-74","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#settings","content":"`split_group`"},"1841":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-75","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#settings","content":"The column whose whole groups are kept on one side, for `group`"},"1842":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-76","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#settings","content":"`folds`"},"1843":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-77","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#settings","content":"The number of cross-validation folds on the training rows. The default is 5."},"1844":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-78","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#settings","content":"`effort`"},"1845":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-79","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#settings","content":"`fast`, `balanced` (the default) or `thorough`. It sets the number of trees: 100, 200 or 400."},"1846":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-80","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#settings","content":"`max_depth`, `C`, `neighbours`, `learning_rate`, `clusters`"},"1847":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-81","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#settings","content":"The settings of the models that use them"},"1848":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-82","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#settings","content":"`contamination`"},"1849":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-83","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#settings","content":"The share of rows to flag as unusual. The default is 2%. The code keeps it between 0.5% and 20%."},"1850":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-84","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#settings","content":"The full signatures are in the model lab reference."},"1851":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab-85","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/model-lab#settings","content":"Back to Model. Next: The models the lab tries."},"1852":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","type":"page","content":"Saving, MLflow and training in the database","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Model"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow"},"1853":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","content":"What is kept after a model run, the optional MLflow record of training runs, and where in-database training starts."},"1854":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow#saving-a-model","content":"Saving a model"},"1855":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow#mlflow-when-it-is-installed","content":"MLflow, when it is installed"},"1856":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow#training-inside-the-database-the-ml-engineers-path","content":"Training inside the database (the ML Engineer's path)"},"1857":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","content":"Three things sit beside the model lab and are easy to confuse: keeping a result, the optional MLflow record, and the training that runs inside the database. The Data Scientist notebooks use the first only. The other two belong to the ML Engineer's path."},"1858":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow#saving-a-model","content":"Nothing in the Data Scientist notebooks saves a fitted model to disk or to the database. The lab's fitted model lives in your kernel until you stop it. To keep a result, keep the numbers: the board, the importance list and the notes."},"1859":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow#saving-a-model","content":"The workflow log records only that a model ran, with its task, its row count and, for the small model, its score. See The workflow log."},"1860":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow#mlflow-when-it-is-installed","content":"MLflow is an optional record of training runs. The Data Scientist notebooks do not start MLflow runs. The runs come from the in-database training that the ML Engineer's notebooks do, described below."},"1861":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow#mlflow-when-it-is-installed","content":"`nb.use_mlflow()` sets where runs are recorded for this kernel. An empty address means the kit's own MLflow server (`exakit mlflow start`), or whatever the shell set. `nb.use_mlflow(login=True)` asks for a username and a password in a hidden box."},"1862":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow#mlflow-when-it-is-installed","content":"`nb.check_mlflow()` checks the client and the server. If the client is missing, it says to run `exakit update notebook`."},"1863":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow#mlflow-when-it-is-installed","content":"`exakit mlflow start` installs the MLflow server into the notebook environment when it is missing."},"1864":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow#mlflow-when-it-is-installed","content":"The settings are listed in Model, Langfuse and MLflow settings."},"1865":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow#training-inside-the-database-the-ml-engineers-path","content":"This is not a Data Scientist step, but it is where the kit's trained models come from. `nb.prepare_training(conn, ds, handoff, container=..., seed=0)` prepares in-database training from a training hand-off:"},"1866":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow#training-inside-the-database-the-ml-engineers-path","content":"It refuses a hand-off that is stale, and a random split that nobody asked for. See The training hand-off for what a hand-off holds."},"1867":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow#training-inside-the-database-the-ml-engineers-path","content":"It creates a feature view in `STARTER_KIT`, drops features that are constant, and writes a training function that fits a logistic regression with a fixed seed."},"1868":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow#training-inside-the-database-the-ml-engineers-path","content":"It returns a plan. The caller runs `plan.create_script`, then `plan.training_sql`."},"1869":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow#training-inside-the-database-the-ml-engineers-path","content":"It needs a Python container inside the database: `PYTHON3_ML` (`exakit udf-use default`) or `PYTHON3` (`exakit udf-setup`). Both come from the udf-devkit add-on, `exakit marketplace udf-devkit`. The add-ons page explains how add-ons are installed."},"1870":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/saving-and-mlflow#training-inside-the-database-the-ml-engineers-path","content":"Back to Model."},"1871":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","type":"page","content":"The models the lab tries","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Model"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models"},"1872":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","content":"Every model in the lab, the name that selects it, and the rule that picks the best one."},"1873":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#the-models-the-lab-tries","content":"The models the lab tries"},"1874":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#how-the-best-one-is-picked","content":"How the best one is picked"},"1875":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#choose-a-model-yourself","content":"Choose a model yourself"},"1876":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#the-settings-that-change-the-models","content":"The settings that change the models"},"1877":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","content":"The lab does not rely on one model. For each task it trains every model in a list on the same training rows, and it picks one. This page lists the models, the rule for the pick, and how to choose a model yourself. Every model is from scikit-learn. The key in brackets is the name you pass as `model=`."},"1878":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#the-models-the-lab-tries","content":"Task"},"1879":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#the-models-the-lab-tries","content":"Models"},"1880":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#the-models-the-lab-tries","content":"How the best one is picked"},"1881":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#the-models-the-lab-tries","content":"`predict_yes_no`"},"1882":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#the-models-the-lab-tries","content":"baseline (`baseline`), logistic regression (`logistic`), logistic regression with L1 (`logistic_l1`), decision tree (`decision_tree`), random forest (`random_forest`), extra trees (`extra_trees`), gradient boosting (`boosting`), k-nearest neighbours (`knn`), naive Bayes (`naive_bayes`), linear support vector machine (`svm`)"},"1883":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#the-models-the-lab-tries","content":"Cross-validated ROC AUC, or PR AUC when the rarer answer is under 5%"},"1884":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#the-models-the-lab-tries","content":"`predict_number`"},"1885":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#the-models-the-lab-tries","content":"baseline (`baseline`), linear (`linear`), ridge (`ridge`), lasso (`lasso`), decision tree, random forest, extra trees, gradient boosting, k-nearest neighbours"},"1886":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#the-models-the-lab-tries","content":"Cross-validated R squared"},"1887":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#the-models-the-lab-tries","content":"`find_groups`"},"1888":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#the-models-the-lab-tries","content":"k-means (`kmeans`), Gaussian mixture (`gaussian_mixture`), hierarchical (`agglomerative`)"},"1889":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#the-models-the-lab-tries","content":"Silhouette score. If you do not set the number of groups, the lab tries 2 to 6 and keeps the best."},"1890":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#the-models-the-lab-tries","content":"`find_unusual`"},"1891":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#the-models-the-lab-tries","content":"isolation forest (`isolation_forest`), local outlier factor (`lof`)"},"1892":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#the-models-the-lab-tries","content":"No score. The share you set as `contamination` (2% by default) decides how many rows are flagged."},"1893":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#how-the-best-one-is-picked","content":"With `model=\"all\"`, the lab does this:"},"1894":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#how-the-best-one-is-picked","content":"It scores each model by cross-validation on the training rows. The score is the metric for the task."},"1895":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#how-the-best-one-is-picked","content":"It takes the model with the highest mean score."},"1896":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#how-the-best-one-is-picked","content":"It goes down a list of models from simplest to most complex. The first model on that list whose score is within 0.01 of the best wins."},"1897":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#how-the-best-one-is-picked","content":"The order is: logistic regression, linear, ridge, logistic L1, lasso, naive Bayes, decision tree, k-nearest neighbours, SVM, random forest, extra trees, gradient boosting. The baseline is not on that list. It is picked only when it has the highest score and no model on the list is within 0.01 of it."},"1898":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#how-the-best-one-is-picked","content":"The pick is made on cross-validation. The held-out rows are scored after the pick, for reading. They do not choose the model."},"1899":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#how-the-best-one-is-picked","content":"The 0.01 rule is a rule for choosing a simple model. It is not a test that the gap between two models is real. To judge a gap, read `cv_sd` on the board. See Comparing models on the Evaluate pages."},"1900":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#choose-a-model-yourself","content":"Pass one key to `model=`, and the lab trains that model and its baseline on the same rows:"},"1901":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#choose-a-model-yourself","content":"With a named model, the pick is yours: the result's `chosen_by` is `you`, and the board holds only that model and the baseline."},"1902":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models-30","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/the-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/the-models#the-settings-that-change-the-models","content":"`effort` sets the number of trees for the tree models: `fast` 100, `balanced` 200 (the default) and `thorough` 400. The other settings are listed on The model lab. Back to Model."},"1903":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","type":"page","content":"Troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Model"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting"},"1904":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","content":"The warnings and errors you can see while you model, what each one means, and what to do."},"1905":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","content":"Each entry quotes the message the kit prints, or describes the step that stops."},"1906":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","content":"The dataset has no target, or no category or entity that is free of the answer, so the baseline cannot run. The step says so. Choose a target in the column map, approve it, and run the notebook again. `nb.model_settings()` shows whether the AI steps have a model. No model is needed for the baseline or the lab."},"1907":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","content":"The lab was asked to predict yes or no, but the column map has no yes-or-no target. The error reads \"Nothing to predict was chosen\". Pick a 0 or 1 column as the target in the column map, or choose another task: predict a number, find natural groups or find unusual rows."},"1908":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","content":"The error reads \"One side of the split has only one answer, so no score can be computed\". A time split can put all the 1s on one side. Change the split to `split_method=\"random\"`, which is stratified for yes or no. See Hold-out."},"1909":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","content":"The warning reads \"Only N rows with a 1 are held out, so the held-out score is shaky\". It appears when fewer than 30 rows with a 1 are held out. Lower `train_pct` (50 is the lowest it accepts), so more rows are held out."},"1910":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","content":"The error reads \"No model could be trained on this data\", and lists the reason for each model that failed. The most common cause is a dataset with almost no rows on one side of the answer. Check the split first."},"1911":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","content":"`nb.feature_ideas(lab, ai=True)` stops with \"No AI model is set up\". Run `nb.model_setup()`, or `nb.use_model(MODEL_ID, PROVIDER_BASE_URL)`. Or call `nb.feature_ideas(lab)` without `ai=True`, which needs no model."},"1912":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","content":"Read `lab_data.left_out`. It gives the reason for each column left out: gives the answer away, personal data, a key or identifier, free text, or marked Leave out. A column marked sensitive, or flagged by the leakage check, is not used. Change the column map if the role is wrong, and approve it again."},"1913":{"id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/model/troubleshooting","content":"Back to Model."},"1914":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","type":"page","content":"Monitor and iterate","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Monitor and iterate"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor"},"1915":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor","content":"What the kit records, what it notices when you run it again, and how you re-approve, refresh or rerun to get back to the right stage."},"1916":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor#where-you-do-it","content":"Where you do it"},"1917":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor#how-we-used-it","content":"How we used it"},"1918":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor#in-this-stage","content":"In this stage"},"1919":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor#what-you-have-at-the-end","content":"What you have at the end"},"1920":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor","content":"Monitoring means noticing that something has changed since you last looked, and deciding what to redo. A table gets a new column. A column map is approved again. A model is retrained on newer rows. In most data science work this loop never ends. The kit helps with the record and with the checks it can make when you run a step again. It does not watch your data in the background, it does not detect drift, and it does not retrain anything on its own. You do the iterating, and the kit tells you where to go back to."},"1921":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor#where-you-do-it","content":"Guided view"},"1922":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor#where-you-do-it","content":"Notebook code"},"1923":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor#where-you-do-it","content":"Terminal"},"1924":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor#where-you-do-it","content":"The workflow list and log in the quickstart's cards. The column map card's **History** lists its versions, and **Restore** saves an older version's choices as a new one. A published model has a **Refresh** action."},"1925":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor#where-you-do-it","content":"`nb.list_workflows()`, `nb.workflow_log(id)`, `nb.continue_workflow(...)`, `nb.column_map_versions(id)`, `nb.refresh_semantic(conn, name)`, `nb.handoff_is_stale(...)`, `nb.tracing()`, `nb.trace(...)`"},"1926":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor#where-you-do-it","content":"`exakit workflow list`, `exakit workflow show <id>`, `exakit describe <id> --versions`, `exakit describe <id> --show --version <n>`, `exakit describe --model <NAME> --refresh`"},"1927":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor#how-we-used-it","content":"Suppose someone adds a column to `AMAZON.ORDER_LINES`. The kit does not notice until you describe the table again. Here is how you find out and what you do, in four steps:"},"1928":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor#how-we-used-it","content":"The workflow log shows what the last run did. The describe call returns a draft when the schema changed, and the changed columns say so. You review the draft, correct what is wrong, and approve. The approval writes the next version and rebuilds every semantic model the table is in. Then run the notebooks again, from the first cell. They read the newest approval."},"1929":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"What changed, and where you go\" href=\"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed\" description=\"Each kind of change, what the kit notices, and which stage to return to\" />"},"1930":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"The workflow log\" href=\"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log\" description=\"The record each workflow keeps, and which workflow a notebook continues\" />"},"1931":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Versions and semantic models\" href=\"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models\" description=\"Every saved column map version, restoring one, and refreshing a semantic model\" />"},"1932":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"A training hand-off that went stale\" href=\"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off\" description=\"How the kit refuses an old training hand-off, and how to write a new one\" />"},"1933":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Tracing model calls\" href=\"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing\" description=\"Each model call as a trace in your Langfuse project\" />"},"1934":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Rerunning, and what the kit does not do\" href=\"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits\" description=\"What moves when you rerun, and the limits to know before you schedule anything\" />"},"1935":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"When it goes wrong\" href=\"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting\" description=\"Approval, staleness and log problems, and their fixes\" />"},"1936":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor#what-you-have-at-the-end","content":"A record of what each run did, a column map whose versions you can read and restore, a semantic model that matches the approved roles, and a plain list of what needs redoing. The loop has no end. When something changes, go back to the stage in the table on What changed, and where you go and work forward from there."},"1937":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits","type":"page","content":"Rerunning, and what the kit does not do","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Monitor and iterate"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits"},"1938":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits","content":"What changes when you run a notebook again, and the limits to know before you rely on the kit for a recurring job."},"1939":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits#rerunning-the-notebooks","content":"Rerunning the notebooks"},"1940":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits#what-the-kit-does-not-do","content":"What the kit does not do"},"1941":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits#rerunning-the-notebooks","content":"Run a notebook again to see what has changed. These are the things that move:"},"1942":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits#rerunning-the-notebooks","content":"`DATASET = None` picks up the dataset approved last. Approve a different one in the quickstart, then run the first cell of the other notebook again to follow it. To pin a dataset, set `DATASET = \"...\"` in the notebook."},"1943":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits#rerunning-the-notebooks","content":"The baseline reads the newest 20,000 rows, and the lab reads the newest 50,000, when the table has a date. New rows change which rows the models see."},"1944":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits#rerunning-the-notebooks","content":"The log grows. Every rerun adds lines to the same workflow."},"1945":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits#rerunning-the-notebooks","content":"Dashboards and hand-off bundles are not rebuilt by a rerun. Make a new draft and a new bundle when the result changes."},"1946":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits#rerunning-the-notebooks","content":"After you update the kit, restart the kernel. A running kernel keeps the helpers it loaded before the update. In JupyterLab, choose **Kernel**, then **Restart Kernel**."},"1947":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits#what-the-kit-does-not-do","content":"Be clear about these limits before you rely on the kit for a recurring job."},"1948":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits#what-the-kit-does-not-do","content":"**It does not detect drift.** It does not compare this month's data with last month's, and it does not warn you when a score falls."},"1949":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits#what-the-kit-does-not-do","content":"**It does not retrain.** A model is trained when you run its cell, and nothing runs it again on a schedule."},"1950":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits#what-the-kit-does-not-do","content":"**It does not watch the database.** Nothing checks the table between your runs."},"1951":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits#what-the-kit-does-not-do","content":"**It does not alert.** Tracing and the log record what happened. They do not send a message."},"1952":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits#what-the-kit-does-not-do","content":"Monitoring the data over time is a job you schedule yourself, with your own tools. The kit gives you the record to read and the steps to redo."},"1953":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/rerunning-and-limits#what-the-kit-does-not-do","content":"Back to Monitor and iterate."},"1954":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off","type":"page","content":"A training hand-off that went stale","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Monitor and iterate"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off"},"1955":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off","content":"How the kit detects that a training hand-off no longer matches the column map or the data, and how to write a new one."},"1956":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off#a-training-hand-off-that-went-stale","content":"A training hand-off that went stale"},"1957":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off#what-the-check-looks-at","content":"What the check looks at"},"1958":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off#the-fix","content":"The fix"},"1959":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off#the-hand-off-bundle-has-no-such-check","content":"The hand-off bundle has no such check"},"1960":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off#a-training-hand-off-that-went-stale","content":"The training hand-off is written with `nb.write_handoff` on the ML Engineer's side, and read by the training step. A hand-off is a snapshot. When the column map or the rows change after it was written, the hand-off is stale. The kit can tell you that, and refuses to train on it."},"1961":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off#what-the-check-looks-at","content":"`nb.handoff_is_stale(conn, handoff, ds)` returns `None` when the hand-off still describes the dataset and its data. Otherwise it returns one line that says what changed and what to do. It checks, in this order:"},"1962":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off#what-the-check-looks-at","content":"**The hand-off is for another descriptor.** The line names both ids."},"1963":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off#what-the-check-looks-at","content":"**The descriptor's version changed**, or its digest did. The line gives both versions, such as v2 to v3."},"1964":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off#what-the-check-looks-at","content":"**The data no longer matches.** With a connection, the check compares the data digest. A mismatch means the rows or the dates differ."},"1965":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off#the-fix","content":"The fix in every case is the same: write it again with `nb.write_handoff(conn, ds)`. The old file stays where it is. The file name carries the descriptor version, so the new one is saved beside the old one."},"1966":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off#the-fix","content":"The training step on the ML Engineer's side refuses a stale hand-off and prints the same line. Check the line first, so you know whether the change was to the column map or to the data."},"1967":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off#the-hand-off-bundle-has-no-such-check","content":"The hand-off bundle, from The hand-off bundle, is a snapshot too. It has no staleness check. Write a new one when the work changes."},"1968":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/stale-hand-off#the-hand-off-bundle-has-no-such-check","content":"Back to Monitor and iterate. Next: Tracing model calls."},"1969":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","type":"page","content":"The workflow log","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Monitor and iterate"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log"},"1970":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","content":"The record each workflow keeps, the kinds of line it writes, what it never holds, and which workflow a notebook continues."},"1971":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"The workflow log"},"1972":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#what-the-log-never-holds","content":"What the log never holds"},"1973":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#when-nothing-is-written","content":"When nothing is written"},"1974":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#which-workflow-a-notebook-continues","content":"Which workflow a notebook continues"},"1975":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","content":"A workflow is the record of one piece of work across the notebooks. Its log is the file where each helper that does something writes a line. The workflows reference describes the workflow as a kit feature. This page covers what the log holds."},"1976":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"Every workflow has one log, `~/.exasol-starter-kit/workflows/<id>.jsonl`: one JSON object per line, append-only, readable by you only. While a workflow is active, each helper that does something adds a line. The kinds you will see are:"},"1977":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"Kind"},"1978":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"Written when"},"1979":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"`start`"},"1980":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"A workflow begins, with its name, the kit version, and the Python and platform"},"1981":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"`step`"},"1982":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"A later notebook continues the work"},"1983":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"`sql`"},"1984":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"A statement runs, with its digest and row count"},"1985":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"`describe.draft`, `describe.approve`"},"1986":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"A column map is drafted, or approved as a new version"},"1987":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"`model`"},"1988":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"A model is trained and scored, with its row count and, where the note shows one, its score"},"1989":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"`trace`"},"1990":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"A model call is traced to Langfuse, with the trace id"},"1991":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"`handoff`"},"1992":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"A training hand-off or a hand-off bundle is written"},"1993":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"`dashboard.revision`"},"1994":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"A dashboard is previewed or published"},"1995":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"`ask.approve`, `ask.answer`"},"1996":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"A question's SQL is approved, and its answer is read"},"1997":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"`mlflow.run`"},"1998":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"An MLflow run is recorded, on the in-database training path"},"1999":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#the-workflow-log","content":"Read it with the commands in the table on Monitor and iterate, or in a notebook:"},"2000":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-30","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#what-the-log-never-holds","content":"The log never holds a credential. The helpers refuse any field named password, token, secret or api_key, and a connection string with a password in it. SQL that looks credential-bearing, such as a statement with a PASSWORD or API_KEY column, is logged with its text replaced and its digest kept, and a warning is shown."},"2001":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-31","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#what-the-log-never-holds","content":"A log that cannot be written warns, and the cell goes on. Logging never fails the work it describes."},"2002":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-32","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#when-nothing-is-written","content":"Without an active workflow nothing is written. There are no implicit workflows."},"2003":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-33","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#which-workflow-a-notebook-continues","content":"`nb.continue_workflow(name)` continues this kernel's workflow. Failing that, it takes the one in `EXAKIT_WORKFLOW_ID`, then the last one started on this computer. It starts a new one only when none exists."},"2004":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-34","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#which-workflow-a-notebook-continues","content":"The quickstart's workflow cell resumes the workflow of this kernel, when there is one. In a new kernel, it starts a new workflow."},"2005":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-35","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#which-workflow-a-notebook-continues","content":"`nb.workflow(resume=\"wf-...\")` continues a named workflow from another kernel."},"2006":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-36","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#which-workflow-a-notebook-continues","content":"`nb.list_workflows()` and `exakit workflow list` show every workflow on this computer."},"2007":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-37","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#which-workflow-a-notebook-continues","content":"The helpers are in the workflow reference."},"2008":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log-38","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/the-workflow-log#which-workflow-a-notebook-continues","content":"Back to Monitor and iterate. Next: Versions and semantic models."},"2009":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing","type":"page","content":"Tracing model calls","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Monitor and iterate"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing"},"2010":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing","content":"How each model call is recorded as a trace in your own Langfuse project, how to group calls into one trace, and what tracing does not do."},"2011":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing#tracing-model-calls","content":"Tracing model calls"},"2012":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing#tracing-model-calls","content":"With Langfuse set up, each model call is one trace in your own Langfuse project, with its input, output, token use and time. Langfuse is the tracing service the kit connects to. Set it up on AI and Langfuse."},"2013":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing#tracing-model-calls","content":"Check whether tracing is on:"},"2014":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing#tracing-model-calls","content":"Pass a block to group several calls into one trace:"},"2015":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing#tracing-model-calls","content":"Each trace is tagged with the database session, the workflow id and, with a dataset, its id and descriptor version. When the block ends, the kit prints the trace id and where to find it, and adds a `trace` line to the workflow log. The secret key is never printed or logged."},"2016":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing#tracing-model-calls","content":"Tracing lets you compare runs by their cost, time and answers. It does not alert you to anything."},"2017":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/tracing#tracing-model-calls","content":"Back to Monitor and iterate. Next: Rerunning, and what the kit does not do."},"2018":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting","type":"page","content":"Troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Monitor and iterate"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting"},"2019":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting","content":"Fixes for the approval, staleness, update and log problems you can meet when you run the work again."},"2020":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting","content":"Each entry quotes the message the kit shows, or describes the step that stops."},"2021":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting","content":"You approved another dataset in the quickstart while this notebook was open. Run this notebook's first cell again. It switches to the newly approved dataset."},"2022":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting","content":"The step raised `DescriptorNotApproved`. Explore, Ask and Share do not read a draft. Open `00_quickstart`, review the map and approve it. The roles and the approval are described on Explore."},"2023":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting","content":"The table's columns or types changed after you described it. Run `nb.describe(...)` again, review the new draft, and approve it. See What changed, and where you go."},"2024":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting","content":"The approval stands, but the semantic model could not be rebuilt. The message says why. Fix the cause, then run `exakit describe <id> --comments`. See Versions and semantic models."},"2025":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting","content":"A running kernel keeps the helpers it loaded before the update. Restart it: in JupyterLab, **Kernel**, then **Restart Kernel**."},"2026":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting","content":"`handoff_is_stale` named what changed. Write the hand-off again with `nb.write_handoff(conn, ds)`. Check the line first, so you know whether the change was to the column map or to the data. See A training hand-off that went stale."},"2027":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/troubleshooting","content":"Back to Monitor and iterate."},"2028":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models","type":"page","content":"Versions and semantic models","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Monitor and iterate"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models"},"2029":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models","content":"How every column map approval is saved as a version you can read and restore, and how a semantic model is rebuilt or refreshed."},"2030":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models#versions-and-restoring-one","content":"Versions, and restoring one"},"2031":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models#semantic-models","content":"Semantic models"},"2032":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models","content":"This page covers two things that change together: the saved versions of a column map, and the semantic model that is built from the approved version."},"2033":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models#versions-and-restoring-one","content":"Every approval is a new version. Nothing is overwritten."},"2034":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models#versions-and-restoring-one","content":"`nb.column_map_versions(id)` lists each version with its approval time, its roles, its slots and its evidence."},"2035":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models#versions-and-restoring-one","content":"`nb.current_version(id)` gives the approved one."},"2036":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models#versions-and-restoring-one","content":"In the quickstart's card, **History** lists the versions. **Restore** applies an older version's choices and saves them as a new version. The card says which version it restored and which new one it saved."},"2037":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models#versions-and-restoring-one","content":"In code, restoring means approving that version's roles again. The version the kit saves is the newest."},"2038":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models#semantic-models","content":"Approving a column map rebuilds every semantic model its table is in, so AI clients read the same meaning. The model is in Exasol Semantic Views. The semantic views page describes the feature."},"2039":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models#semantic-models","content":"A link between tables is not part of a column map. So after you add or remove one, refresh the model yourself:"},"2040":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models#semantic-models","content":"`nb.semantic_models(connection)` lists every model in the database. If publishing fails, the approval still stands and the message says why. Run `exakit describe <id> --comments` to publish it again."},"2041":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/versions-and-semantic-models#semantic-models","content":"Back to Monitor and iterate. Next: A training hand-off that went stale."},"2042":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","type":"page","content":"What changed, and where you go","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Monitor and iterate"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed"},"2043":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","content":"Each kind of change to your data, what the kit notices about it, and the stage to return to."},"2044":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"What changed, what the kit notices, where you go"},"2045":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#the-table-changed","content":"The table changed"},"2046":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","content":"Not every change is noticed. This table says, for each kind of change, what the kit notices on its own and what it does not. The last column names the stage to return to."},"2047":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"What changed"},"2048":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"What the kit notices"},"2049":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"What you do"},"2050":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Go back to"},"2051":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Columns added, removed, renamed or retyped"},"2052":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"`describe` returns a draft, because the schema digest no longer matches"},"2053":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Review the draft and approve a new version"},"2054":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Explore: the column map"},"2055":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"New roles in an approved column map"},"2056":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Every semantic model the table is in is rebuilt by the approval"},"2057":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Check the result of the new roles"},"2058":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Model, to see the effect on the score"},"2059":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Rows changed, with no column change"},"2060":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Nothing on its own. Approval checks the data again, and a training hand-off is refused when its data digest no longer matches."},"2061":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Run Prepare and Explore again, and look at what moved"},"2062":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Prepare"},"2063":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"A new table, or a new link between tables"},"2064":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Nothing, until the model is rebuilt"},"2065":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Refresh the semantic model"},"2066":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Semantic views"},"2067":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"The model's inputs or settings changed"},"2068":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Nothing. The fitted model is not saved, so each run trains it again."},"2069":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Rerun the lab, then score it again"},"2070":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Model"},"2071":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"The dashboard's query changed"},"2072":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Nothing. The preview was made from the old query."},"2073":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-30","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Make a new dashboard draft and preview it"},"2074":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-31","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Communicate and deploy"},"2075":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-32","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"The AI model or its settings changed"},"2076":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-33","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Nothing"},"2077":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-34","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Run `nb.model_settings()` to check what is set"},"2078":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-35","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#what-changed-what-the-kit-notices-where-you-go","content":"Set up Exasol"},"2079":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-36","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#the-table-changed","content":"`nb.describe` compares the table's column names and types with the approved version. If they match, the approved version comes back. If they do not, it makes a draft:"},"2080":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-37","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#the-table-changed","content":"Roles for the columns whose name and type did not change are carried over."},"2081":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-38","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#the-table-changed","content":"Changed or new columns are flagged with low confidence, and the evidence says the column changed since the approved version."},"2082":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-39","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#the-table-changed","content":"The approved version stays approved for the old columns. Nothing is overwritten."},"2083":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-40","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#the-table-changed","content":"`approve` refuses if the table changed since it was described, and says to describe it again. Explore, Ask and Share read only an approved column map. If a step reports that the map is not approved, open the quickstart and approve it."},"2084":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-41","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#the-table-changed","content":"The kit checks columns and types when you describe. It does not compare every row on each run. Rows are checked when you approve, and again by a training hand-off's staleness check."},"2085":{"id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed-42","page_id":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/monitor/what-changed#the-table-changed","content":"Back to Monitor and iterate. Next: The workflow log."},"2086":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views","type":"page","content":"A typed, cleaned view","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Prepare"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views"},"2087":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views","content":"What nb.typed_view changes in a table (types, text, blanks, placeholders and copies), how to read the proposal, and how to create the view in EXAKIT_PREPARED."},"2088":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views#propose-the-view","content":"Propose the view"},"2089":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"How we used it: fraud_transactions"},"2090":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"How we used it: amazon_sales"},"2091":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views","content":"Numbers and dates often arrive as text, when a file loads as text. Blank cells, placeholders and copies make a result quietly wrong. The **typed view** fixes these. It is a view, a stored query that reads your table, so your table is never changed. The kit proposes the changes first, and creates the view only when you call `create`."},"2092":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views#propose-the-view","content":"The kit reads the table's values, not only its names. It then proposes these changes:"},"2093":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views#propose-the-view","content":"**Types.** A text column whose every value is a number becomes `DECIMAL`. A column with exponents becomes `DOUBLE`. A text column whose every value is a date becomes `DATE`, in one of these formats: `YYYY-MM-DD`, `DD-MM-YYYY`, `DD.MM.YYYY`, `MM/DD/YYYY`, or `DD/MM/YYYY`. A timestamp becomes `TIMESTAMP`, and true or false becomes `BOOLEAN`."},"2094":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views#propose-the-view","content":"**Kept as text.** An identifier or key column stays text. So does a number with a leading zero, and a column named like a code, such as a postal code, a phone number, an SKU, or a name ending in `_ID`."},"2095":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views#propose-the-view","content":"**Cleaning.** Text is trimmed. A blank cell becomes `NULL`. A placeholder becomes `NULL`, where the placeholder can be listed."},"2096":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views#propose-the-view","content":"**Copies.** Rows that are exact copies of another row are dropped. The first row, by the key, is kept. When the table has no key, a row that copies another in every column is dropped."},"2097":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views#propose-the-view","content":"Nothing changes until `create()`. The proposal shows each change with the evidence for it."},"2098":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"The typed view proposes what it will change. For this table it turns each placeholder into `NULL` and drops the copies:"},"2099":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"The proposal lists the cleaning in the same form as the checks, for example `DEVICE_USED: 'Unknown Device' (1,530 rows) becomes NULL`. The copies are counted after cleaning, so the number can differ from the check's number. The check's counts are on Data checks."},"2100":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"The measured semantic model was built on `EXAKIT_PREPARED.AMAZON__ORDER_LINES`, the typed view of `AMAZON.ORDER_LINES`. The view holds 128,969 rows and the table 128,975. Every row of the table is distinct (`SELECT COUNT(*) FROM (SELECT DISTINCT * FROM AMAZON.ORDER_LINES)` returns 128,975), so the 6 rows are not exact copies. The view's own SQL (`SELECT VIEW_TEXT FROM SYS.EXA_ALL_VIEWS WHERE VIEW_NAME = 'AMAZON__ORDER_LINES'`) says why: it trims every text value, turns an empty one into NULL, and then keeps one row of each group that is the same in every column except `ORDER_LINE_ID` (`ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY` every other column `ORDER BY ORDER_LINE_ID)`, `WHERE COPY_ = 1`). Six order lines were copies of another line apart from their row id, and the view dropped them. The semantic model's measurements are on Semantic views."},"2101":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"Back to Prepare. Previous: Linked tables and the joined view. Next: Prepared views."},"2102":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","type":"page","content":"Data checks","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Prepare"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks"},"2103":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","content":"The five checks nb.data_checks runs on a table, what each finding means for a result, and what the fraud_transactions and amazon_sales checks report."},"2104":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"The checks"},"2105":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"How we used it: fraud_transactions"},"2106":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"How we used it: amazon_sales"},"2107":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","content":"The data checks read your table and report five kinds of problem: repeated ids, exact copies, empty cells, placeholder values and a rare outcome. Each finding is one sentence in the notebook and one row in the result. The checks change nothing. Deciding what to do about a finding is yours."},"2108":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","content":"A **target** is the column you want to predict. The **label** in the code is the same column. ROC AUC is a score from 0 to 1 for how well a model puts the rows with a 1 above the rows with a 0. A model that guesses at random scores 0.5."},"2109":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"`nb.data_checks` finds five kinds of problem. Each is built from the column map alone, so the same cell runs on every dataset."},"2110":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"Check"},"2111":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"What it finds"},"2112":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"What it means for a result"},"2113":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"Repeated key or id"},"2114":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"A column with the role `key` or `identifier` where at least 90% of rows are distinct. A value that many rows share, such as a customer on every purchase, is not reported."},"2115":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"A count of rows counts the repeats twice. Count distinct values, or keep one row per value."},"2116":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"Exact copies"},"2117":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"Rows equal to another row in every column except the key"},"2118":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"The copies count twice. Drop them before you count."},"2119":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"Empty cells"},"2120":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"Blank values in any column"},"2121":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"An average leaves those rows out. A grouping puts them in a group of their own."},"2122":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"Placeholders"},"2123":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"Values that stand for \"not known\" but look like categories, in category and flag columns with at most 50 values. Examples: `Unknown...`, `Invalid...`, `N/A`, `none`, `null`, `missing`, `not available`, `undefined`, `TBD`, dashes and question marks."},"2124":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"The value counts as a category. Treat it as empty, or say what it is."},"2125":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"Rare outcome"},"2126":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"A target that is 1 in less than 10% of rows, or 0 in less than 10%"},"2127":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"A model that always gives the common answer is right most of the time. Judge a model by a ranking score, or by the baseline. Never by accuracy alone."},"2128":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"The rules are in `notebook/package/exakit_nb/data_checks.py`. The placeholder list is one pattern, `PLACEHOLDER`, in the same file."},"2129":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"The guided card shows the findings under plain titles: **Repeated IDs**, **Repeated rows**, **Empty cells**, **Placeholder values** and **Rare outcome**."},"2130":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"Run the checks:"},"2131":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#the-checks","content":"For the rare outcome, the ranking score depends on the outcome's rate. In the lab, a rate under 5% makes the score PR AUC, which focuses on finding the rare 1s. Otherwise the score is ROC AUC. See `notebook/package/exakit_nb/lab.py`."},"2132":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"`fraud_transactions` is the messy sample table, so it shows every check. The dataset README records the problems in the table on purpose, with counts. The checks look for these same things. The table below lists each problem, the README's count, and what the check reports."},"2133":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-30","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"Problem"},"2134":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-31","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"Count"},"2135":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-32","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"What the check reports"},"2136":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-33","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"`TRANSACTION_ID` repeats"},"2137":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-34","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"Measured: 51,000 rows, 50,000 distinct ids, so 1,000 rows repeat an id. The README says 881 are exact copies and 119 disagree."},"2138":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-35","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"A repeated-id line for `TRANSACTION_ID`. The row key `ROW_ID` is unique."},"2139":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-36","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"Exact copies"},"2140":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-37","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"The README: 881 rows copy another row in every column except the key"},"2141":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-38","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"An exact-copies line"},"2142":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-39","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"Empty cells"},"2143":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-40","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"The README: about 5% each in amount, hour, device, city and payment method"},"2144":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-41","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"An empty-cells line for each column"},"2145":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-42","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"Placeholders"},"2146":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-43","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"The README: 1,530 `Unknown Device` in `DEVICE_USED`, 1,530 `Invalid Method` in `PAYMENT_METHOD`"},"2147":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-44","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"A placeholder line for each value"},"2148":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-45","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"Rare outcome"},"2149":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-46","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"Measured: 2,510 of 51,000 rows are `FRAUDULENT = 1`, which is 4.9%"},"2150":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-47","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"A rare-outcome line: a model that always says \"not fraud\" is right 95.1% of the time"},"2151":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-48","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"No date"},"2152":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-49","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"The table has an hour, but no date"},"2153":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-50","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"No time check. The steps that need a date skip."},"2154":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-51","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"The repeated-id count is measured: 51,000 rows minus 50,000 distinct `TRANSACTION_ID` values is 1,000. The fraud rate is measured too, as 2,510 of 51,000. The other counts are the README's. Run the checks to see the lines the kit prints for your copy of the data."},"2155":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-52","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"A finding for a placeholder reads, in the kit's words, like this: `PAYMENT_METHOD = 'Invalid Method' in 1,530 rows looks like a category but means 'not known': treat it as empty, or say what it is`."},"2156":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-53","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"For the rare outcome, the printed line has this form, with the measured 4.9%:"},"2157":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-54","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-fraud_transactions","content":"The typed view proposes what it will change. For this table it turns each placeholder into `NULL` and drops the copies. See A typed, cleaned view."},"2158":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-55","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"`amazon_sales` is cleaner, so its checks stay quiet on most lines and one warning matters."},"2159":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-56","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"**A repeated id that is by design.** `ORDER_ID` is an identifier. The descriptor records 120,378 distinct values in 128,975 rows, measured on the database. That is 8,597 repeats. An order has several lines, so repeats are expected. The check still names it, because 93% of the rows are distinct, which is above the 90% line. The line reads:"},"2160":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-57","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"Here the repeat is correct, because one row is one order line. Read the line, then decide. Nothing in the data changes."},"2161":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-58","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"**A rare outcome that is not rare.** `CANCELLED` is 1 in 14.2% of rows, measured as 18,332 of 128,975. That is above the 10% line, so the checks do not report a rare outcome."},"2162":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-59","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"**The answer-giving column.** The checks above do not catch `STATUS`. It is found by the leakage check. See Columns that give the answer away."},"2163":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks-60","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"Back to Prepare. Next: Columns that give the answer away."},"2164":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","type":"page","content":"Features","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Prepare"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/features"},"2165":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","content":"What a feature is, the rule-based ideas the kit proposes, how each idea is tested on held-out rows, and how to keep one for the model."},"2166":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/features#propose-and-test-an-idea","content":"Propose and test an idea"},"2167":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/features#the-ideas","content":"The ideas"},"2168":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/features#how-an-idea-is-judged","content":"How an idea is judged"},"2169":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/features#keep-an-idea","content":"Keep an idea"},"2170":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","content":"A **feature** is a new input for a model, built from the columns you have. For example, \"how long ago the order date was\" is a feature built from one column. The kit proposes feature ideas from your data, and it tests each one before you keep it. The model is trained in the Model stage. These helpers belong to the model lab, and you can call them from here."},"2171":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/features#the-ideas","content":"The ideas come from rules. They include:"},"2172":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/features#the-ideas","content":"how long ago the time column's date was,"},"2173":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/features#the-ideas","content":"a value compared with its group's usual value,"},"2174":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/features#the-ideas","content":"two categories taken together,"},"2175":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/features#the-ideas","content":"a number read as a number, when it holds counts,"},"2176":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/features#the-ideas","content":"whether a number is missing, when some rows are blank,"},"2177":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/features#the-ideas","content":"a flag for words such as `price`, `slow` or `wrong`, in a column of sentences."},"2178":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/features#the-ideas","content":"The rules are in `notebook/package/exakit_nb/lab.py`, in `feature_ideas`."},"2179":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/features#how-an-idea-is-judged","content":"The lab leaves out the columns that give the answer away and the personal data. See Columns that give the answer away."},"2180":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/features#how-an-idea-is-judged","content":"The kit tests each idea on rows the model did not train on. An idea helps when the score rises in cross-validation and does not fall on the held-out rows. An idea that pushes a yes-or-no score almost to perfect is marked suspicious, usually because it gives the answer away. The card does not let you keep a suspicious idea."},"2181":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/features#keep-an-idea","content":"Keep an idea by passing its series to the next model lab:"},"2182":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/features#keep-an-idea","content":"With an AI model set up, `nb.feature_ideas(lab, ai=True)` adds up to four more ideas. The model receives the column names, their roles and the scores. It never receives a row or a value."},"2183":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/features","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/features#keep-an-idea","content":"Back to Prepare. Previous: Prepared views. Next: When it goes wrong."},"2184":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","type":"page","content":"Prepare","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Prepare"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare"},"2185":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare","content":"Check the data for repeats, copies, empty cells and placeholders, find columns that give the answer away, and create cleaned or joined views only when you ask."},"2186":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare#the-flow","content":"The flow"},"2187":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare#where-you-do-it","content":"Where you do it"},"2188":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare#in-this-stage","content":"In this stage"},"2189":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare#what-you-have-at-the-end","content":"What you have at the end"},"2190":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare","content":"Before you compute from data, you check that the data says what you think it says. A repeated ID counts a customer twice. An empty cell drops out of an average without a warning. A placeholder such as `Unknown Device` looks like a category, and it means \"not known\". A column written after the outcome makes a model look perfect. In this stage the kit finds these problems and explains what each one does to a result. It never changes your table. When you ask for a cleaned or joined version, it creates a view next to your table, and that view gets its own approved column map."},"2191":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#the-flow","content":"Preparation has two halves. The first half only reads: the checks, the links and the leakage check. The second half creates views, and only when you say so."},"2192":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#the-flow","content":"**Check.** Run the data checks, and read each finding."},"2193":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#the-flow","content":"**Look at the links.** Read the schema map to see which tables link to yours."},"2194":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#the-flow","content":"**Propose a view.** A joined view brings in the linked tables. A typed view fixes types and cleans values. Read the proposal. It shows each change with its evidence and the exact SQL."},"2195":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#the-flow","content":"**Create.** Create only the views you want. Each view is described and approved, and the steps after it read the view."},"2196":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#where-you-do-it","content":"Guided view"},"2197":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#where-you-do-it","content":"Notebook code"},"2198":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#where-you-do-it","content":"Terminal"},"2199":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#where-you-do-it","content":"**Is the data clean?** in the **Explore and predict** card, with **Linked tables** and **A cleaned copy** under it. Each has a button that creates the view."},"2200":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#where-you-do-it","content":"`01_explore`, *Prepare the data*: `nb.data_checks`, `nb.describe_schema`, `schema_map.joined_view(...)`, `joined_view_proposal.create(...)`, `nb.typed_view`, `typed_view_proposal.create(...)`, `nb.leakage_check`."},"2201":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#where-you-do-it","content":"`exakit describe --schema SCHEMA` lists the links. `--approve --link` and `--unlink` change them. No command runs the checks or creates a view."},"2202":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#where-you-do-it","content":"In the first cell of `01_explore`, `USE_JOINED = True` and `USE_PREPARED = True` create the proposed views and make the later steps read them. Both are `False` at the start, so nothing is created until you set them."},"2203":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Data checks\" href=\"/data-scientist/prepare/data-checks\" description=\"Repeats, copies, empty cells, placeholders and a rare outcome, with the fraud_transactions counts\" />"},"2204":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Columns that give the answer away\" href=\"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage\" description=\"The leakage check, the rule it uses, and the amazon_sales STATUS column measured\" />"},"2205":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Linked tables and the joined view\" href=\"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view\" description=\"Join linked tables into one wide view of your table\" />"},"2206":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"A typed, cleaned view\" href=\"/data-scientist/prepare/cleaned-views\" description=\"Fix types, trim text, turn placeholders into NULL, and drop copies, after you read the changes\" />"},"2207":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Prepared views\" href=\"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views\" description=\"The views EXAKIT_PREPARED holds, their names, and how each gets its column map\" />"},"2208":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Features\" href=\"/data-scientist/prepare/features\" description=\"New inputs for a model, tested before you keep them\" />"},"2209":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"When it goes wrong\" href=\"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting\" description=\"Findings, skipped views, and code columns that stayed text\" />"},"2210":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#what-you-have-at-the-end","content":"A checked table, with the findings you have decided on. Optionally, a joined view and a typed view in `EXAKIT_PREPARED`, each with its own approved column map. The steps after this one read the view you created, or your table if you created none."},"2211":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare#what-you-have-at-the-end","content":"Next: Model."},"2212":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","type":"page","content":"Columns that give the answer away","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Prepare"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage"},"2213":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","content":"What nb.leakage_check flags, the three rules it uses, and the measured proof that amazon_sales STATUS gives CANCELLED away."},"2214":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage#columns-that-give-the-answer-away","content":"Columns that give the answer away"},"2215":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage#the-proof-on-amazon_sales","content":"The proof on amazon_sales"},"2216":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage#run-the-check","content":"Run the check"},"2217":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","content":"A column whose values almost decide the target on their own makes a model look better than it is. Such a column is usually written after the outcome. A cancelled order gets a cancelled status, so the status is known only once the outcome is known. A model that reads it learns the answer, not a pattern, and scores well on the data it was trained on. For an order whose outcome is not yet known, the same column cannot help."},"2218":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","content":"`nb.leakage_check(connection, dataset)` looks for these columns. It is the check the approval runs, and the model lab leaves out every column it lists."},"2219":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage#columns-that-give-the-answer-away","content":"The check flags a column when all three of these hold:"},"2220":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage#columns-that-give-the-answer-away","content":"it has between two and 50 distinct values,"},"2221":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage#columns-that-give-the-answer-away","content":"at least 95% of its rows sit in values where the target is almost always 1, or almost always 0 (at least 99% or at most 1%), and"},"2222":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage#columns-that-give-the-answer-away","content":"those values hold at least 90% of all the rows where the target is 1."},"2223":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage#columns-that-give-the-answer-away","content":"The check looks at every column except the target, the key, identifiers and text. It lists the flagged columns and prints why each one was flagged. The rule is in `leakage_check` in `notebook/package/exakit_nb/data_checks.py`."},"2224":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage#columns-that-give-the-answer-away","content":"A flagged column is a warning, not an error. The column stays in the column map. The model does not use it."},"2225":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage#the-proof-on-amazon_sales","content":"The approval warns about `STATUS` in `AMAZON.ORDER_LINES`. A cancelled order has a cancelled status, so the status gives the answer away. You can check this on the table. These two queries are read-only, and both were run on a real database on 12 November 2026:"},"2226":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage#the-proof-on-amazon_sales","content":"Both counts are 18,332. Every row with `STATUS = 'Cancelled'` has `CANCELLED = 1`, and the table holds no other row with `CANCELLED = 1`. The status alone gives the target away completely."},"2227":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage#the-proof-on-amazon_sales","content":"The check prints this line for `STATUS`:"},"2228":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage#the-proof-on-amazon_sales","content":"The printed text is generated from the data. The line above is what the check prints for these measured counts."},"2229":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage#the-proof-on-amazon_sales","content":"The dataset README also names `COURIER_STATUS`, `QTY` and `AMOUNT` as changing once an order is cancelled. The check reports the columns it finds from the data, not the ones the README names. So read the printed list rather than assume it."},"2230":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage#run-the-check","content":"The quickstart and `01_explore` run this check. Each run prints one line per flagged column, and returns the list of column names. The model lab calls the same check when you do not pass a list of your own (`nb.model_lab(..., leaks=...)` in `notebook/package/exakit_nb/lab.py`), and it leaves the flagged columns out."},"2231":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage#run-the-check","content":"If the list is empty, the check prints that no column decides the target on its own."},"2232":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/leakage#run-the-check","content":"Back to Prepare. Previous: Data checks. Next: Linked tables and the joined view."},"2233":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view","type":"page","content":"Linked tables and the joined view","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Prepare"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view"},"2234":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view","content":"How a joined view brings the columns of linked tables into one wide view of your table, how to correct the links first, and what the amazon_sales example shows."},"2235":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view#linked-tables","content":"Linked tables"},"2236":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view#create-the-joined-view","content":"Create the joined view"},"2237":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"How we used it: amazon_sales"},"2238":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view#when-there-is-nothing-to-join","content":"When there is nothing to join"},"2239":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view","content":"A **joined view** is a view that combines your table with the tables it links to. Each row of your table keeps one row, and the linked columns are added beside it. You need one when the questions you ask use columns that live in another table. The links come from the schema map, which you check in Linked tables in the Explore stage."},"2240":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view#linked-tables","content":"A link adds the other table's columns without adding rows. A link is many to one: each row of your table matches at most one row of the other table. The joined view follows links up to three tables away from your table. A table reached along two paths is joined once for each path. The joined table's key is left out, because your table's key identifies the row."},"2241":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view#linked-tables","content":"To correct the map before you create a view:"},"2242":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view#create-the-joined-view","content":"Create the joined view when you want it:"},"2243":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view#create-the-joined-view","content":"`create` approves the schema map if it is still a draft. It creates the view `EXAKIT_PREPARED.\"<SCHEMA>__<TABLE>__JOINED\"`. It describes the view and approves its column map, with your table's roles carried over. The steps after it then read the joined data. The view is described in Prepared views."},"2244":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"The dataset loads one table into the `AMAZON` schema. The schema map finds no link to another table, so there is no joined view to build:"},"2245":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view#how-we-used-it-amazon_sales","content":"The schema map says `No links: every table stands on its own.` That is the right result for one table. The proposal creates nothing."},"2246":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view#when-there-is-nothing-to-join","content":"If your table links to no other table in its schema, the proposal says so and creates nothing. The schema map shows which links the search found. To add a link the search missed, use `schema_map.link(...)`. A link needs every value of the column in the other table's key, with at most 0.1% missing. A name alone never makes a link."},"2247":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/linked-tables-view#when-there-is-nothing-to-join","content":"Back to Prepare. Previous: Columns that give the answer away. Next: A typed, cleaned view."},"2248":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","type":"page","content":"Prepared views","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Prepare"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views"},"2249":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","content":"The views the preparation steps create in EXAKIT_PREPARED, their names, how each gets its own approved column map, and why your table is never changed."},"2250":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#the-views-and-their-names","content":"The views and their names"},"2251":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#each-view-gets-its-own-column-map","content":"Each view gets its own column map"},"2252":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#your-table-stays-as-it-was","content":"Your table stays as it was"},"2253":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","content":"Every view the preparation steps create goes into one schema, `EXAKIT_PREPARED`. Your table is never changed. The kit creates a view and never alters the table under it. Each view is a separate dataset, so the later stages can read it like any table."},"2254":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#the-views-and-their-names","content":"View"},"2255":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#the-views-and-their-names","content":"Created by"},"2256":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#the-views-and-their-names","content":"Name"},"2257":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#the-views-and-their-names","content":"Joined view"},"2258":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#the-views-and-their-names","content":"`schema_map.joined_view(...).create(...)`"},"2259":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#the-views-and-their-names","content":"`EXAKIT_PREPARED.\"<SCHEMA>__<TABLE>__JOINED\"`"},"2260":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#the-views-and-their-names","content":"Typed view of a table in another schema"},"2261":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#the-views-and-their-names","content":"`nb.typed_view(...).create(...)`"},"2262":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#the-views-and-their-names","content":"`EXAKIT_PREPARED.\"<SCHEMA>__<TABLE>\"`"},"2263":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#the-views-and-their-names","content":"Typed view of a view in `EXAKIT_PREPARED`"},"2264":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#the-views-and-their-names","content":"`nb.typed_view(...).create(...)`"},"2265":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#the-views-and-their-names","content":"`EXAKIT_PREPARED.\"<NAME>__TYPED\"`"},"2266":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#the-views-and-their-names","content":"Plain-name view of a table with spaces in its column names"},"2267":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#the-views-and-their-names","content":"`nb.use_table(...)`"},"2268":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#the-views-and-their-names","content":"`EXAKIT_PREPARED.\"<SCHEMA>__<TABLE>__PLAIN\"`"},"2269":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#the-views-and-their-names","content":"The plain-name view is for tables whose column names have spaces or small letters. See When it goes wrong."},"2270":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#each-view-gets-its-own-column-map","content":"Each view gets its own approved column map. The new map starts from the roles of the table it came from. A text column that became a date takes the time role. If the time slot is empty, the converted column fills it."},"2271":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#each-view-gets-its-own-column-map","content":"Each view is a separate dataset with its own versions, so approving a view does not change its source table's map. A view you create is saved with the same rules as any column map: each approval is a new version, and nothing is overwritten. See Approve the column map."},"2272":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#each-view-gets-its-own-column-map","content":"The column map itself, its roles and slots, is described in The column map."},"2273":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#your-table-stays-as-it-was","content":"The checks only read. The joined view and the typed view are views in `EXAKIT_PREPARED`, and they are created only when you ask. The kit never alters the table under a view."},"2274":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/prepared-views#your-table-stays-as-it-was","content":"Back to Prepare. Previous: A typed, cleaned view. Next: Features."},"2275":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","type":"page","content":"Troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Prepare"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting"},"2276":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","content":"What each data-check finding means, why a joined or typed view is not created, and how to see the SQL that ran."},"2277":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","content":"Each entry starts with the finding or symptom you see. Find it, then read the fix."},"2278":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","content":"No. The checks only read. The joined view and the typed view are views in `EXAKIT_PREPARED`, and they are created only when you ask."},"2279":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","content":"One identifier repeats in some rows. If one row should be one value, those rows count twice. Count distinct values, or keep one row per value. If the repeats are correct, for example an order with several lines, keep the data as it is and say so in your notes."},"2280":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","content":"Some rows copy another row in every column except the key. They count twice. Drop them before you count. The typed view can drop them for you when you create it."},"2281":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","content":"A column has blank values. An average leaves those rows out, and a grouping puts them in a group of their own. Decide whether a blank means zero, not known, or not applicable. The typed view turns a blank into `NULL`."},"2282":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","content":"A value such as `Unknown Device` looks like a category and means \"not known\". Treat it as empty. The typed view turns it into `NULL` for you, when the check can list its values."},"2283":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","content":"The target is 1 in less than 10% of rows, or 0 in less than 10%. A model that always gives the common answer is right most of the time. Judge a model by a ranking score, ROC AUC or PR AUC, or by the baseline, and not by accuracy. The lab uses PR AUC when the rarer answer is under 5% of rows."},"2284":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","content":"This is a warning, not an error. Read the column's values. If the column is written after the outcome, leave it out of the model, as the model does. If it is not, keep it in the map and say why it looks perfect. For the rule, see Columns that give the answer away."},"2285":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","content":"Your table links to no other table in its schema. The schema map shows which links the search found. To add a link the search missed, use `schema_map.link(...)`. A link needs every value of the column in the other table's key, with at most 0.1% missing. A name alone never makes a link."},"2286":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","content":"Every column already has its type, and nothing needs cleaning. That is the right result. No view is created."},"2287":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","content":"The typed view keeps a column named like a code as text, even when its values are digits. A postal code, a phone number and a SKU are names, not quantities. A number with a leading zero also stays text, so no zero is lost."},"2288":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","content":"The kit's queries cannot read such names without quotes. `nb.use_table` then creates a view with plain names in `EXAKIT_PREPARED`, and uses it. The message says so in one line. The table itself is unchanged. See Prepared views."},"2289":{"id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/prepare/troubleshooting","content":"Back to Prepare."},"2290":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"page","content":"Set up AI and Langfuse","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Set up Exasol"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse"},"2291":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","content":"Connect a text model and, optionally, Langfuse tracing. Where to get each key, how to give it to the kit, what the kit sends, and how to check it works."},"2292":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-flow","content":"The flow"},"2293":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"The settings"},"2294":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-quickest-way-the-home-card","content":"The quickest way: the Home card"},"2295":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#get-a-model-provider","content":"Get a model provider"},"2296":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#openai","content":"OpenAI"},"2297":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#mistral","content":"Mistral"},"2298":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#claude-anthropic","content":"Claude (Anthropic)"},"2299":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#ollama-on-this-computer","content":"Ollama (on this computer)"},"2300":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#lm-studio-on-this-computer","content":"LM Studio (on this computer)"},"2301":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#vllm-on-your-own-server","content":"vLLM (on your own server)"},"2302":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#gemini-google","content":"Gemini (Google)"},"2303":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#groq","content":"Groq"},"2304":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#another-openai-compatible-server","content":"Another OpenAI-compatible server"},"2305":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"Choose the model and its effort"},"2306":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#get-langfuse","content":"Get Langfuse"},"2307":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"Langfuse Cloud"},"2308":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#your-own-langfuse","content":"Your own Langfuse"},"2309":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#give-them-to-the-kit","content":"Give them to the kit"},"2310":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#set-them-once-before-exakit-notebook-recommended","content":"Set them once, before `exakit notebook` (recommended)"},"2311":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#in-a-notebook-cell","content":"In a notebook cell"},"2312":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-kits-settings-file","content":"The kit's settings file"},"2313":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"What the kit sends to a model"},"2314":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#check-it-works","content":"Check it works"},"2315":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#when-it-goes-wrong","content":"When it goes wrong"},"2316":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-you-have-at-the-end","content":"What you have at the end"},"2317":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","content":"An AI model and tracing are both optional. A **model** is the text model the kit calls for two steps: drafting SQL from your question in `02_ask_your_data`, and sorting texts into themes in `01_explore`. **Tracing**, through Langfuse, records each model call as a trace you can inspect later: its input, its output and its token usage. Set them up here, once, so every notebook uses them. The kit runs fine without either."},"2318":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"The kit reads these names. Set only what you use. A value you leave out switches its feature off. It breaks nothing."},"2319":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"Setting"},"2320":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"What it is"},"2321":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-30","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"Secret"},"2322":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-31","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"`EXAKIT_MODEL_ID`"},"2323":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-32","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"The model's id, exactly as your provider or server names it"},"2324":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-33","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"No"},"2325":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-34","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"`EXAKIT_PROVIDER_BASE_URL`"},"2326":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-35","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"The address of the model's API, including its version prefix, such as `/v1/`. Not a full request path."},"2327":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-36","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"No"},"2328":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-37","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"`EXAKIT_PROVIDER_API_KEY`"},"2329":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-38","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"The model's key. Leave it unset for a local server that asks for no key."},"2330":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-39","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"Yes"},"2331":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-40","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"`LANGFUSE_BASE_URL`"},"2332":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-41","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"Langfuse's address for your region, or your own Langfuse"},"2333":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-42","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"No"},"2334":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-43","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"`LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY`"},"2335":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-44","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"The Langfuse public key, which starts `pk-lf-`"},"2336":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-45","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"Yes"},"2337":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-46","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"`LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY`"},"2338":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-47","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"The Langfuse secret key, which starts `sk-lf-`"},"2339":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-48","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"Yes"},"2340":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-49","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"`EXAKIT_PROVIDER_HEADERS`"},"2341":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-50","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"Optional. A JSON object of extra routing headers, for example a Claude workspace. Omit unless a provider needs it."},"2342":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-51","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"No"},"2343":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-52","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"`EXAKIT_MODEL_TEMPERATURE`"},"2344":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-53","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"Optional, from 0 to 2. Unset sends no temperature. Set `0` for a local model that should answer the same way twice."},"2345":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-54","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"No"},"2346":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-55","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"Rules the kit enforces:"},"2347":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-56","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"A model needs an explicit base URL. With no model ID, the AI steps stay off."},"2348":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-57","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"A key is sent only to an `https://` address, or to a server on this computer or your own network, such as a local Ollama. A key is never sent across a network in clear text."},"2349":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-58","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"The same rule applies to `LANGFUSE_BASE_URL`. With plain `http://` to a host outside this machine and your network, tracing stays off."},"2350":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-59","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"Do not put a username, a password, a query or a request path such as `/chat/completions` in the base URL. Put authentication in the key setting, not in a custom `Authorization` or `api-key` header."},"2351":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-60","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-settings","content":"`LANGFUSE_HOST` is the name Langfuse's SDK 3 and 4 used for the address. The kit still accepts it when `LANGFUSE_BASE_URL` is unset."},"2352":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-61","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-quickest-way-the-home-card","content":"The Home card of `00_quickstart` sets the model up from menus. You never type an address or a model name unless you want to."},"2353":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-62","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-quickest-way-the-home-card","content":"Open `00_quickstart`. On the Home card, find the **AI model** row and click **Set up** (or **Change**)."},"2354":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-63","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-quickest-way-the-home-card","content":"**Provider:** pick yours from the menu. Its address fills in by itself. To use another address (a proxy, a server on another port), click the pencil beside it and type it."},"2355":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-64","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-quickest-way-the-home-card","content":"**API key:** paste it into the hidden box. **How do I get this?** under the box opens this page at your provider's section; the second link opens the provider's own key page. A server on this computer (Ollama) needs no key."},"2356":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-65","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-quickest-way-the-home-card","content":"Click **Check and list the models**. The kit sends one request to the provider with the key and lists the chat models the key may use. A refused key says so here."},"2357":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-66","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-quickest-way-the-home-card","content":"**Model:** pick one. The pencil lets you type any model name instead."},"2358":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-67","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-quickest-way-the-home-card","content":"**Effort:** pick how hard the model thinks, where the model takes an effort setting (see Choose the model and its effort). Otherwise the card says the model uses its own."},"2359":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-68","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-quickest-way-the-home-card","content":"Click **Use this model**. The row then reads *Using your-model · effort high*."},"2360":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-69","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-quickest-way-the-home-card","content":"The **Langfuse tracing** row works the same way: pick your region (the pencil types your own Langfuse's address), paste the public and secret keys, and click **Trace to Langfuse**. See Get Langfuse for where the keys come from."},"2361":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-70","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-quickest-way-the-home-card","content":"The code behind the card is one cell of `00_quickstart` (*Your AI model and Langfuse tracing*): set `PROVIDER`, `SHOW_MODELS = True` to list the models, then `MODEL_ID` and `EFFORT`."},"2362":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-71","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-quickest-way-the-home-card","content":"The provider list, each provider's address and its key rule are in `notebook/package/exakit_nb/providers.py` (`model_providers`). The model list call is `nb.provider_models`, in the same file."},"2363":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-72","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#get-a-model-provider","content":"Each provider below needs one of two things: a key from its console, or a server you run yourself. The links go to the provider's own page. Check the model list on the provider's page, because model names change. The Home card lists the models your key may use, so you rarely need to look one up."},"2364":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-73","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#openai","content":"Sign in and open API keys: platform.openai.com/api-keys. Create a key and copy it: it is shown once."},"2365":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-74","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#openai","content":"The address is `https://api.openai.com/v1/`."},"2366":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-75","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#openai","content":"The Home card lists the models your key may use. Reasoning models (the `o` series, `gpt-5` and later) take an effort setting."},"2367":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-76","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#mistral","content":"Sign in to Mistral's console and create an API key there."},"2368":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-77","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#mistral","content":"The address is `https://api.mistral.ai/v1/`."},"2369":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-78","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#mistral","content":"Mistral's reasoning models (Magistral) take an effort setting."},"2370":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-79","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#claude-anthropic","content":"Sign in to the Claude Console and open API keys: platform.claude.com/settings/keys. Create a key and copy it."},"2371":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-80","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#claude-anthropic","content":"Choose a model ID from the models overview. Copy it exactly, for example `claude-opus-5-5`."},"2372":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-81","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#claude-anthropic","content":"Use this base URL: `https://api.anthropic.com/v1/`."},"2373":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-82","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#claude-anthropic","content":"If your key is a personal or service key that is not scoped to a workspace, the provider also needs a workspace header. A workspace-scoped key does not need it. Set the optional headers setting:"},"2374":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-83","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#claude-anthropic","content":"Leave `EXAKIT_MODEL_TEMPERATURE` unset. Claude Opus 4.7 and later refuse a temperature setting."},"2375":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-84","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#claude-anthropic","content":"The kit uses Anthropic's OpenAI-compatible layer, which has known limits. It is for text chat. The kit does not use the native Claude API."},"2376":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-85","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#ollama-on-this-computer","content":"Install Ollama from ollama.com/download. Choose your system."},"2377":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-86","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#ollama-on-this-computer","content":"Pull a chat model. The names and sizes are on the Ollama library. For example: `ollama pull <model-name>`."},"2378":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-87","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#ollama-on-this-computer","content":"Check the exact name: `ollama list`. Use that name as the model ID."},"2379":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-88","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#ollama-on-this-computer","content":"Use this base URL: `http://localhost:11434/v1/`. No key is needed."},"2380":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-89","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#ollama-on-this-computer","content":"The kit's connection is Ollama's OpenAI-compatible API. Keep the key unset. Ollama's cloud models have their own sign-in, which is separate from this setup."},"2381":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-90","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#lm-studio-on-this-computer","content":"Download LM Studio from lmstudio.ai and install it."},"2382":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-91","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#lm-studio-on-this-computer","content":"Load a chat model, then start its local server in the **Developer** area."},"2383":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-92","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#lm-studio-on-this-computer","content":"Use its base URL: `http://localhost:1234/v1/`, unless you changed the port. The model ID is the name the server shows for the loaded model."},"2384":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-93","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#lm-studio-on-this-computer","content":"If you turn on server authentication, create a token and put it in the key setting. The docs say to turn on the toggle under **Developers > Server Settings**, then create a token under **Manage Tokens**. Copy the token when it appears, because it is not shown again. See LM Studio authentication."},"2385":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-94","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#lm-studio-on-this-computer","content":"The compatibility details are on LM Studio's OpenAI endpoints page."},"2386":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-95","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#vllm-on-your-own-server","content":"Install vLLM by following its installation guide. The guide is organized by hardware, and NVIDIA CUDA is listed first."},"2387":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-96","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#vllm-on-your-own-server","content":"Start an OpenAI-compatible server with a chat model: `vllm serve <model>`. See vLLM online serving."},"2388":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-97","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#vllm-on-your-own-server","content":"Use your server's base URL with the `/v1/` path, for example `http://localhost:8000/v1/`. The model ID is the name the server serves."},"2389":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-98","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#vllm-on-your-own-server","content":"If the server requires a key, use that key. The model needs a chat template for the kit to use it."},"2390":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-99","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#vllm-on-your-own-server","content":"Running the vLLM server is separate from connecting the kit to it."},"2391":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-100","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#gemini-google","content":"Sign in to Google AI Studio and open API keys. Create a key and copy it."},"2392":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-101","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#gemini-google","content":"Choose a Gemini model ID that your key can call. Google's OpenAI compatibility page explains how the endpoint is used."},"2393":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-102","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#gemini-google","content":"Use this base URL, and keep the full path: `https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/`."},"2394":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-103","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#groq","content":"Sign in to the Groq console and open API keys. Create a key and copy it."},"2395":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-104","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#groq","content":"The address is `https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/`."},"2396":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-105","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#groq","content":"The reasoning models (GPT-OSS, Qwen 3) take an effort setting; see Groq's reasoning page."},"2397":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-106","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#another-openai-compatible-server","content":"Any server that speaks the OpenAI Chat Completions API works. Pick **Another OpenAI-compatible server**, type its address with the pencil (including the version path, such as `/v1/`), and give its key if it asks for one. The kit lists the models from `<address>models`. Offered no effort setting: the server decides."},"2398":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-107","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"**The model.** A larger model drafts better questions and feature ideas, and costs more per call. A small or local model is fine to try the steps. The kit sends the model the column names, types, roles and notes for the step, never a row of your data (see What the kit sends to a model)."},"2399":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-108","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"**The effort.** A reasoning model can think longer before it answers. The kit sends your choice as the provider's own `reasoning_effort` setting:"},"2400":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-109","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"Effort"},"2401":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-110","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"What it changes"},"2402":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-111","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"The model's default"},"2403":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-112","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"Nothing is sent: the provider decides"},"2404":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-113","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"Low"},"2405":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-114","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"Quicker and cheaper answers"},"2406":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-115","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"Medium"},"2407":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-116","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"A balance"},"2408":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-117","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"High"},"2409":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-118","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"Slower, more thorough answers"},"2410":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-119","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"The card offers an effort only where the provider documents one for that model:"},"2411":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-120","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"Provider"},"2412":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-121","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"Models with an effort setting"},"2413":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-122","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"OpenAI"},"2414":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-123","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"the `o` series, `gpt-5` and later (OpenAI reasoning guide)"},"2415":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-124","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"Gemini"},"2416":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-125","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"Gemini 2.5 and later (Gemini OpenAI compatibility)"},"2417":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-126","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"Groq"},"2418":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-127","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"GPT-OSS and Qwen 3"},"2419":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-128","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"Mistral"},"2420":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-129","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"Magistral"},"2421":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-130","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"Ollama"},"2422":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-131","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"thinking models such as GPT-OSS, Qwen 3, DeepSeek-R1 (Ollama compatibility)"},"2423":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-132","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"Anthropic"},"2424":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-133","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"none: Claude's OpenAI-compatible API ignores the setting (Anthropic's compatibility page)"},"2425":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-134","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"LM Studio, vLLM, another server"},"2426":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-135","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"none"},"2427":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-136","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#choose-the-model-and-its-effort","content":"In a terminal or a cell, the same setting is `EXAKIT_MODEL_EFFORT` (`low`, `medium` or `high`; unset sends nothing), or `nb.use_model(model, address, effort=\"high\")`. The code that sends it is in `notebook/package/exakit_nb/model_config.py`, which passes the value as `reasoning_effort`."},"2428":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-137","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#get-langfuse","content":"Langfuse records the calls. You need a project in a Langfuse you can reach, and a key pair from that project."},"2429":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-138","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"Create an account at cloud.langfuse.com/auth/sign-up, or sign in if you have one. The getting-started guide describes the same steps."},"2430":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-139","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"Open the project you want the traces in. If you have none, create one in the Langfuse interface."},"2431":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-140","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"Go to **Project > Settings**, then **API Keys**. Create new API credentials. You get a public key (`pk-lf-...`) and a secret key (`sk-lf-...`). Langfuse shows the secret key only once, so copy it then."},"2432":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-141","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"Use the base URL of the region your project is in. The regions are separate, and each has its own base URL:"},"2433":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-142","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"Region"},"2434":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-143","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"Base URL"},"2435":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-144","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"Where it runs"},"2436":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-145","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"EU"},"2437":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-146","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"`https://cloud.langfuse.com`"},"2438":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-147","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"Ireland"},"2439":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-148","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"US"},"2440":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-149","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"`https://us.cloud.langfuse.com`"},"2441":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-150","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"Oregon"},"2442":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-151","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"Japan"},"2443":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-152","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"`https://jp.cloud.langfuse.com`"},"2444":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-153","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"Tokyo"},"2445":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-154","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"HIPAA"},"2446":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-155","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"`https://hipaa.cloud.langfuse.com`"},"2447":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-156","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"Oregon"},"2448":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-157","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#langfuse-cloud","content":"The regions are described on Langfuse's data regions page."},"2449":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-158","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#your-own-langfuse","content":"Langfuse can run on your own infrastructure. The self-hosting page lists the options: Docker Compose for one machine, Kubernetes for production, and others. Then use your own address in `LANGFUSE_BASE_URL`. It must be `https://`, unless it is on this computer or your network. Create the keys in your own project the same way."},"2450":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-159","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#give-them-to-the-kit","content":"There are three ways. Use the one that fits how you work. You can combine them."},"2451":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-160","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#set-them-once-before-exakit-notebook-recommended","content":"The notebook server reads its environment from the terminal that starts it. Its kernels read theirs from the server. So set everything in one terminal, then start the notebooks from that terminal. Every notebook then has the model and Langfuse."},"2452":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-161","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#set-them-once-before-exakit-notebook-recommended","content":"Each key is typed into a hidden prompt. It is never part of a command, so it is not in the shell's history."},"2453":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-162","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#set-them-once-before-exakit-notebook-recommended","content":"Mac and Linux, bash or zsh, for Claude:"},"2454":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-163","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#set-them-once-before-exakit-notebook-recommended","content":"Windows PowerShell 5.1 or later, the same names:"},"2455":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-164","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#set-them-once-before-exakit-notebook-recommended","content":"A local Ollama needs no key and no Langfuse. After you load a chat model:"},"2456":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-165","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#set-them-once-before-exakit-notebook-recommended","content":"Skip any value at its hidden prompt by pressing Enter. An empty key is the same as no key."},"2457":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-166","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#set-them-once-before-exakit-notebook-recommended","content":"Three rules for this way:"},"2458":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-167","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#set-them-once-before-exakit-notebook-recommended","content":"**Already running?** The server read its environment when it started. A kernel restart does not read it again. Run `exakit notebook stop`, then `exakit notebook`, in the terminal that has the variables. For Marimo, use `exakit notebook marimo` the same way."},"2459":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-168","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#set-them-once-before-exakit-notebook-recommended","content":"**The plain values can live in the settings file.** `~/.exasol-starter-kit/exakit.env` takes the model's ID and address (`EXAKIT_MODEL_ID`, `EXAKIT_PROVIDER_BASE_URL`, and optionally `EXAKIT_PROVIDER_HEADERS` and `EXAKIT_MODEL_TEMPERATURE`). Remove the `# ` in front of a line and set it once. The file refuses any key, secret or token. It does not hold the Langfuse address or the Langfuse keys. Those stay in the terminal as shown above."},"2460":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-169","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#set-them-once-before-exakit-notebook-recommended","content":"**Leave out what you do not use.** No model ID means the AI steps skip and say so. No Langfuse variables means tracing is off."},"2461":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-170","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#in-a-notebook-cell","content":"The quickstart has a cell called **Your AI model and Langfuse tracing**. Fill in the values at the top and run the cell:"},"2462":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-171","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#in-a-notebook-cell","content":"The cell asks for each key in a hidden box. With `remember=True` it saves them in the kit's credentials folder, readable by you only, so every notebook of this kit has them. Run `FORGET = True` in that cell to delete what was saved."},"2463":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-172","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#in-a-notebook-cell","content":"To set them for the current notebook only, call the helper directly:"},"2464":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-173","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#in-a-notebook-cell","content":"Those values disappear when the kernel stops. Add `remember=True` to keep them."},"2465":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-174","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#in-a-notebook-cell","content":"To ask for whatever is missing, run:"},"2466":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-175","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#in-a-notebook-cell","content":"It asks for the model ID and address, the Langfuse address, and then each key in a hidden box. It prints what is set. For anything still missing, it prints the terminal lines for your system, so you can set it once for every notebook."},"2467":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-176","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#in-a-notebook-cell","content":"To delete what was remembered:"},"2468":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-177","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-kits-settings-file","content":"Only the model's plain values go in `exakit.env`, as described in the first way. Keys and the Langfuse settings never go there."},"2469":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-178","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#the-kits-settings-file","content":"Never type a key into a cell. Use the hidden box or the hidden prompt. A key typed into a cell is saved in the notebook file."},"2470":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-179","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"The model sees only what each step needs. It never sees rows."},"2471":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-180","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"Step"},"2472":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-181","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"What the model does"},"2473":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-182","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"What is sent"},"2474":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-183","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"Ask your data (`02_ask_your_data`)"},"2475":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-184","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"Drafts SQL for your question"},"2476":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-185","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"The approved column map and your question. No rows."},"2477":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-186","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"Themes in text (`01_explore`)"},"2478":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-187","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"Sorts texts into themes"},"2479":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-188","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"A sample of texts from each side of the target"},"2480":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-189","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"Column notes"},"2481":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-190","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"Writes one line per column on a new draft"},"2482":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-191","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"Each column's name, type, role, evidence and top values. Never a row."},"2483":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-192","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"A column marked sensitive is named with its role only, and the model is told never to select its values. A sensitive column is never grouped, charted or sent to a model as data."},"2484":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-193","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"The model may never do three things:"},"2485":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-194","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"**Approve roles.** Only you approve a column map."},"2486":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-195","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"**Run SQL.** A drafted query runs only after you approve that exact text. Editing the text removes the approval."},"2487":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-196","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"**Write to the database.** Approved questions run as the kit's read-only user."},"2488":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-197","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"Where the model runs decides where the data goes. A model on your own machine keeps the model's work on this computer. With Langfuse Cloud on, the recorded inputs and outputs of each call are sent to Langfuse. With tracing off, nothing goes to Langfuse."},"2489":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-198","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-the-kit-sends-to-a-model","content":"The kit never writes a key into a cell, the code view or the workflow log."},"2490":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-199","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#check-it-works","content":"Work through these checks in order. Each one proves a bit more."},"2491":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-200","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#check-it-works","content":"**What the kit has.** Run this in a notebook. It shows which settings are set, without their values. `nb.model_settings()` makes no network request (`notebook/package/exakit_nb/__init__.py`), so a configured result does not prove the key is valid. Check the key with the Home card's **Check and list the models**, or with step 2."},"2492":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-201","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#check-it-works","content":"**A real model call.** In `02_ask_your_data`, set `DRAFT_WITH_MODEL = True` and run the Ask cells. The model drafts SQL from your question and the column map. Read the SQL, and the model's assumptions and doubts, before you approve anything. A failed call says what went wrong."},"2493":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-202","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#check-it-works","content":"Explore's themes step needs a text column. The reference datasets have none, so use Ask for this check."},"2494":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-203","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#check-it-works","content":"**The trace.** Open your Langfuse project and its traces. Each model call from the kit is one trace, with its input, its output and, when the provider returns them, its token counts. Themes in Explore make two calls, and both go into one trace named `explore-themes`."},"2495":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-204","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#when-it-goes-wrong","content":"Either no model is set, or the dataset has no column for that step. Run `nb.model_settings()` to see what is set. Set the model as shown above. The themes step also skips on a dataset with no text column, and says so. The reference datasets, `amazon_sales` and `fraud_transactions`, have no text column."},"2496":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-205","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#when-it-goes-wrong","content":"The settings are refused before any call is made. The message names the setting. Common causes:"},"2497":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-206","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#when-it-goes-wrong","content":"The base URL is `http://` to a host outside this computer and your network. Use the provider's `https://` address."},"2498":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-207","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#when-it-goes-wrong","content":"The base URL includes a path such as `/chat/completions`, a query, or a username and password. Remove them. Give only the API base, such as `/v1/`."},"2499":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-208","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#when-it-goes-wrong","content":"`EXAKIT_PROVIDER_HEADERS` is not a JSON object of plain values, or it sets an authorization header. Put the key in `EXAKIT_PROVIDER_API_KEY` instead."},"2500":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-209","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#when-it-goes-wrong","content":"The message names the missing setting. Tracing needs all three: the public key, the secret key and the base URL. A plain `http://` address to a host outside this computer and your network also turns tracing off. Use the `https://` address."},"2501":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-210","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#when-it-goes-wrong","content":"The notebook server read its environment when it started. Run `exakit notebook stop`, then `exakit notebook` from the terminal that has the variables. A kernel restart does not read them again, and a new terminal does not reach a server that is already running."},"2502":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-211","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#when-it-goes-wrong","content":"No. Every step runs without one. A model is used only to draft SQL in Ask and to sort texts into themes in Explore. Both are off until you turn them on. Ask also has a drafter that needs no model: `nb.draft_question`."},"2503":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-212","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#when-it-goes-wrong","content":"Not by default. The database and the notebooks run on this computer. With a model set up, Ask sends the column map and your question, never rows. The themes step sends a sample of texts. It asks first when the data is a live external source. With Langfuse Cloud on, the recorded inputs and outputs of each model call are sent to Langfuse."},"2504":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-213","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#when-it-goes-wrong","content":"No. Nothing runs until you approve the exact text. Approved questions run as the read-only user, and writes are rejected by the database."},"2505":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-214","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-you-have-at-the-end","content":"A model and a tracing setup you have checked, or a clear choice to leave them off. The notebooks use the same settings."},"2506":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse-215","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse#what-you-have-at-the-end","content":"Back to Set up Exasol. Next: Troubleshooting."},"2507":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit","type":"page","content":"Check the kit","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Set up Exasol"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit"},"2508":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit","content":"Two checks that show the install works, one in a terminal and one in a notebook cell. Both change nothing, and both are safe to run at any time."},"2509":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit#check-from-a-terminal","content":"Check from a terminal"},"2510":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit#check-from-a-cell","content":"Check from a cell"},"2511":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit#how-we-used-it","content":"How we used it"},"2512":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit#change-the-kit-from-a-cell","content":"Change the kit from a cell"},"2513":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit","content":"A check tells you whether the database answers. Run the terminal check once after the install. The quickstart runs the cell check first."},"2514":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit#check-from-a-terminal","content":"`exakit status` reports `Status: running` and exits with code 0 when the kit is ready. The `exakit sql` line prints the database's current time. A timestamp means the query went through."},"2515":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit#check-from-a-terminal","content":"On Windows, the command is `exakit.cmd` in `%USERPROFILE%\\.local\\bin`. Git Bash does not find it on the path, so call `~/.local/bin/exakit.cmd` there."},"2516":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit#check-from-a-cell","content":"The first cell of `00_quickstart` checks the kit and changes nothing:"},"2517":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit#check-from-a-cell","content":"`nb.kit_check()` returns the state as a value (`kit_state`), so a later cell can read it."},"2518":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit#how-we-used-it","content":"On a fresh machine, install with the Data Scientist persona, as shown on Install the kit. Then open `00_quickstart` and run the check cell. It shows what is installed and running, and changes nothing:"},"2519":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit#how-we-used-it","content":"Then run the workflow cell, the one that starts `data-scientist-quickstart`. It prints the workflow id, and the other notebooks continue that workflow. You do not need to note the id down. See Workflows."},"2520":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit#change-the-kit-from-a-cell","content":"To change the kit from a cell, use `nb.exakit(...)`. It runs the same command as a terminal and returns the exit code:"},"2521":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit#change-the-kit-from-a-cell","content":"A command run from a cell has no terminal. A question it would ask takes its default. Give the answer up front instead, for example `nb.exakit(\"mcp-setup\", env={\"EXAKIT_MCP_CLIENTS\": \"claude\"})`."},"2522":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit#change-the-kit-from-a-cell","content":"Back to Set up Exasol. Next: Workflows."},"2523":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","type":"page","content":"Set up Exasol","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Set up Exasol"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up"},"2524":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up","content":"Install the kit, open its notebooks, check that the database answers, and connect an AI model if you want one."},"2525":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"Where you do it"},"2526":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up#in-this-stage","content":"In this stage"},"2527":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up#what-you-have-at-the-end","content":"What you have at the end"},"2528":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up","content":"Every data science project needs a place to work: a database that holds the data, a way to query it, and a notebook to write in. The kit gives you all three on your computer: a local Exasol database, the tools that load and query it, and four notebooks that run on it. Setup takes one install command and one check."},"2529":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"Task"},"2530":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"Guided view"},"2531":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"Notebook code"},"2532":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"Terminal"},"2533":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"Check the kit"},"2534":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"The **Home** card in `00_quickstart`, tab **Your kit**"},"2535":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"`nb.kit_check()`"},"2536":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"`exakit status`"},"2537":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"Start the database"},"2538":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"Not in a card"},"2539":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"`nb.exakit(\"start\")`"},"2540":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"`exakit start`"},"2541":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"Install an add-on"},"2542":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"Home card, tab **Marketplace**, **Install**"},"2543":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"`nb.addon_ready(\"dash-server\")`"},"2544":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"`exakit marketplace dash-server`"},"2545":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"Connect AI clients"},"2546":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"Not in a card"},"2547":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"`nb.exakit(\"mcp-setup\", env={\"EXAKIT_MCP_CLIENTS\": \"claude\"})`"},"2548":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"`exakit mcp-setup`"},"2549":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"Open the notebooks"},"2550":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"Not in a card"},"2551":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"Not in a cell"},"2552":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"`exakit notebook` or `exakit notebook marimo`"},"2553":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#where-you-do-it","content":"Commands run from a cell do not need a terminal. Each one streams its output into the cell and returns its exit code, so a cell can act on the result."},"2554":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-30","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Install the kit\" href=\"/data-scientist/set-up/install\" description=\"The install command for each system, and what it puts on this computer\" />"},"2555":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-31","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Open the notebooks\" href=\"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks\" description=\"JupyterLab or Marimo, the kernel, and the docs from a cell\" />"},"2556":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-32","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Check the kit\" href=\"/data-scientist/set-up/check-the-kit\" description=\"The two checks that show the database answers\" />"},"2557":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-33","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Workflows\" href=\"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows\" description=\"The id that links the notebooks, and the log it writes\" />"},"2558":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-34","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Set up AI and Langfuse\" href=\"/data-scientist/set-up/ai-and-langfuse\" description=\"Optional: a text model and tracing, with their keys\" />"},"2559":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-35","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#in-this-stage","content":"<Card title=\"Troubleshooting\" href=\"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting\" description=\"Install, database, notebook and docs problems\" />"},"2560":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up-36","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up#what-you-have-at-the-end","content":"A local Exasol database that answers, the kit's notebooks ready to open, and a workflow that logs what you do. Next, load the data you will work on in Get the data."},"2561":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","type":"page","content":"Install the kit","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Set up Exasol"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install"},"2562":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","content":"The install command for each system, the Data Scientist option, what the install puts on this computer, and how to wait for it to finish."},"2563":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install#the-command","content":"The command"},"2564":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install#choose-the-data-scientist-set","content":"Choose the Data Scientist set"},"2565":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install#what-the-install-puts-on-this-computer","content":"What the install puts on this computer"},"2566":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install#wait-for-the-install-to-finish","content":"Wait for the install to finish"},"2567":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","content":"Run the command for your system in a terminal. The first install deploys the database. It is usually done in under 2 minutes."},"2568":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install#the-command","content":"macOS and Linux (and WSL):"},"2569":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install#the-command","content":"Windows, in PowerShell:"},"2570":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install#choose-the-data-scientist-set","content":"To install the Data Scientist set of parts without the menus, name the persona. On macOS and Linux:"},"2571":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install#choose-the-data-scientist-set","content":"On Windows, set `$env:EXAKIT_PERSONA = \"data-scientist\"` before the `irm` line."},"2572":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install#choose-the-data-scientist-set","content":"The Data Scientist persona loads two sample datasets, `amazon_sales` and `fraud_transactions`. It connects every AI client it finds on the machine, and it installs Dash Server and the notebook add-on."},"2573":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install#choose-the-data-scientist-set","content":"Without the variable, an interactive install asks which persona you want. Choose Data Scientist. A persona is a named set of answers: which datasets, AI clients and add-ons you get. See the kit's personas."},"2574":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install#what-the-install-puts-on-this-computer","content":"**A local Exasol database.** It runs in a container. The kit uses Docker when Docker is running, and Podman otherwise. The kit never installs or starts Docker itself."},"2575":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install#what-the-install-puts-on-this-computer","content":"**exapump**, the command-line tool that loads data files and runs SQL."},"2576":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install#what-the-install-puts-on-this-computer","content":"**pyexasol**, the Python driver the notebooks use."},"2577":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install#what-the-install-puts-on-this-computer","content":"**A read-only AI connection.** The kit's MCP server gives AI clients read access to the database, as a database user that cannot write. Passwords stay in `~/.exasol-starter-kit/credentials/`. Connecting a client is covered in the kit's AI page."},"2578":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install#what-the-install-puts-on-this-computer","content":"**The notebook add-on.** It holds the notebooks' Python, JupyterLab, Marimo and the kernel named **Exasol (Starter Kit)**. The Data Scientist persona installs it."},"2579":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install#what-the-install-puts-on-this-computer","content":"**Personas and sample data.** See the persona section above."},"2580":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install#what-the-install-puts-on-this-computer","content":"**Agent skills** for AI clients, placed where CLI agents look (`~/.claude/skills` and `~/.agents/skills`)."},"2581":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install#wait-for-the-install-to-finish","content":"While the install runs, `exakit status` answers `installing` and exits with code 3. Poll it until it reports running."},"2582":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install#wait-for-the-install-to-finish","content":"Re-running the installer is safe. It skips the steps that finished and retries the ones that failed."},"2583":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/install#wait-for-the-install-to-finish","content":"Back to Set up Exasol. Next: Open the notebooks."},"2584":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","type":"page","content":"Open the notebooks","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Set up Exasol"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks"},"2585":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","content":"Start JupyterLab or Marimo on the kit's own Python, find the four notebooks, and read the docs from a cell."},"2586":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks#start-them","content":"Start them"},"2587":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks#run-the-notebooks-in-order","content":"Run the notebooks in order"},"2588":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks#the-guided-card-and-the-code-view","content":"The guided card and the Code view"},"2589":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks#read-these-docs-from-a-notebook","content":"Read these docs from a notebook"},"2590":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","content":"The notebooks run in your browser, on the kit's own Python. Both JupyterLab and Marimo open with the kernel **Exasol (Starter Kit)**. That kernel knows where the kit's database connection is, so no notebook asks for a host, a user or a password."},"2591":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks#start-them","content":"Run `exakit notebook` again after an install or an update to check the notebook environment and the database connection. It fixes what it can and says what it cannot fix."},"2592":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks#run-the-notebooks-in-order","content":"Your copies are in `~/.exasol-starter-kit/notebooks/starter-kit-notebooks/data-scientist/`. Run them in this order:"},"2593":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks#run-the-notebooks-in-order","content":"`00_quickstart`"},"2594":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks#run-the-notebooks-in-order","content":"`01_explore`"},"2595":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks#run-the-notebooks-in-order","content":"`02_ask_your_data`"},"2596":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks#run-the-notebooks-in-order","content":"`03_share`"},"2597":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks#run-the-notebooks-in-order","content":"A notebook you edited is never overwritten by an update. A notebook you deleted is not copied back."},"2598":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks#the-guided-card-and-the-code-view","content":"Each notebook opens with a guided card. A card has buttons and forms for the page's steps. The first card has a **Docs** button beside the logo. It opens this documentation on the page for that notebook."},"2599":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks#the-guided-card-and-the-code-view","content":"Every card has a **Guided / Code** switch. **Guided** is the default. **Code** shows the calls behind each button. Two ways through each notebook explains both."},"2600":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks#read-these-docs-from-a-notebook","content":"The site ships with the kit and is served from this computer. Reading and searching work without internet."},"2601":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks#read-these-docs-from-a-notebook","content":"If `nb.docs()` reports that the site is missing, run `nb.exakit(\"update\", \"notebook\")`. More on this in Troubleshooting."},"2602":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/open-the-notebooks#read-these-docs-from-a-notebook","content":"Back to Set up Exasol. Next: Check the kit."},"2603":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","type":"page","content":"Troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Set up Exasol"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting"},"2604":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","content":"What to run when the install, the database, the notebooks, the docs or the AI settings do not behave as expected."},"2605":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#install-and-the-command-line","content":"Install and the command line"},"2606":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#notebooks-and-docs","content":"Notebooks and docs"},"2607":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#files-and-updates","content":"Files and updates"},"2608":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#ai-model-and-tracing","content":"AI model and tracing"},"2609":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","content":"Each entry gives the message or the symptom, then the command to run. The AI entries are at the end."},"2610":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#install-and-the-command-line","content":"The command is in `~/.local/bin`, and that folder is not on a bare shell's `PATH`. This does not mean the kit is missing. Run `export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\"`, or call `~/.local/bin/exakit` by its full path. On Windows, call `exakit.cmd`."},"2611":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#install-and-the-command-line","content":"`installing` with exit code 3 means the install is still running. Poll `exakit status` until it reports running. If the status names a re-run instead, the installer stopped. Run the installer again. It resumes where it stopped."},"2612":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#install-and-the-command-line","content":"`exakit status` also tells you what to run. If it says `interrupted`, do not loop on `exakit start`. Run `exakit repair-runtime` only after you have agreed to it: it rebuilds the database, and that destroys the data you loaded. The bundled datasets are loaded again afterwards. The kit asks before it does this."},"2613":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#install-and-the-command-line","content":"It installs the add-on when it is missing and starts it when it is stopped."},"2614":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#install-and-the-command-line","content":"A running kernel keeps the helpers it loaded before the update. Restart the kernel. In JupyterLab, choose **Kernel**, then **Restart Kernel**."},"2615":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#notebooks-and-docs","content":"Port 8888 (JupyterLab) or 2718 (Marimo) belongs to another program. Without `--port`, the kit uses the next free port and says which one. To pick a port yourself, run `exakit notebook --port 8890`. A port you name is refused when it is taken."},"2616":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#notebooks-and-docs","content":"Run `exakit notebook setup`. It installs the kit's JupyterLab again at its pinned version. Without a terminal it does this without asking. If the notebook environment itself is broken, run `exakit update notebook`."},"2617":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#notebooks-and-docs","content":"Run `exakit notebook setup`. Every `exakit notebook` command registers the kernel again."},"2618":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#notebooks-and-docs","content":"Run `exakit notebook --no-browser`. It prints the address. The login token is in `~/.exasol-starter-kit/credentials`. Do not paste the token anywhere else."},"2619":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#notebooks-and-docs","content":"Run `exakit notebook check`. It finds the kit's database connection and checks it."},"2620":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#notebooks-and-docs","content":"`nb.docs()` reads the copy of the site in the kit. If it reports the site is missing, run `nb.exakit(\"update\", \"notebook\")`. The site is served on this computer at one of the ports 8790 to 8809, the first one free. To choose the port, set `EXAKIT_DOCS_PORT` before you start the notebooks. If the notebook runs on another machine than your browser, the page cannot reach the site. Use `nb.docs(browser=True)` on the machine that runs the kit."},"2621":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#notebooks-and-docs","content":"`nb.docs(\"words\")` searches these docs. `nb.docs(nb.some_command)` opens that command's page. The command reference lists every helper."},"2622":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#files-and-updates","content":"No. Everything the notebooks need runs from a cell or a card: `nb.kit_check()`, `nb.exakit(...)`, `nb.addon_ready(...)`. You need a terminal once, to run the installer and open the notebooks."},"2623":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#files-and-updates","content":"Under `~/.exasol-starter-kit`: column maps, workflow logs, hand-off bundles and the kit's credentials. The data you load lives in the database on this computer."},"2624":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#files-and-updates","content":"No. A notebook you edited is never overwritten. A notebook you deleted is not copied back."},"2625":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#ai-model-and-tracing","content":"These entries are about the optional model and Langfuse settings. The setup steps are in Set up AI and Langfuse."},"2626":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#ai-model-and-tracing","content":"Either no model is set, or the dataset has no column for that step. Run `nb.model_settings()` to see what is set. Set the model as shown on Set up AI and Langfuse. The themes step also skips on a dataset with no text column, and says so. The reference datasets, `amazon_sales` and `fraud_transactions`, have no text column."},"2627":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#ai-model-and-tracing","content":"The settings are refused before any call is made. The message names the setting. Common causes:"},"2628":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#ai-model-and-tracing","content":"The base URL is `http://` to a host outside this computer and your network. Use the provider's `https://` address."},"2629":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#ai-model-and-tracing","content":"The base URL includes a path such as `/chat/completions`, a query, or a username and password. Remove them. Give only the API base, such as `/v1/`."},"2630":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#ai-model-and-tracing","content":"`EXAKIT_PROVIDER_HEADERS` is not a JSON object of plain values, or it sets an authorization header. Put the key in `EXAKIT_PROVIDER_API_KEY` instead."},"2631":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#ai-model-and-tracing","content":"The message names the missing setting. Tracing needs all three: the public key, the secret key and the base URL. A plain `http://` address to a host outside this computer and your network also turns tracing off. Use the `https://` address."},"2632":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#ai-model-and-tracing","content":"The notebook server read its environment when it started. Run `exakit notebook stop`, then `exakit notebook` from the terminal that has the variables. A kernel restart does not read them again, and a new terminal does not reach a server that is already running."},"2633":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#ai-model-and-tracing","content":"No. Every step runs without one. A model is used only to draft SQL in Ask and to sort texts into themes in Explore. Both are off until you turn them on. Ask also has a drafter that needs no model: `nb.draft_question`."},"2634":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-30","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#ai-model-and-tracing","content":"Not by default. The database and the notebooks run on this computer. With a model set up, Ask sends the column map and your question, never rows. The themes step sends a sample of texts. It asks first when the data is a live external source. With Langfuse Cloud on, the recorded inputs and outputs of each model call are sent to Langfuse."},"2635":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-31","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#ai-model-and-tracing","content":"No. Nothing runs until you approve the exact text. Approved questions run as the read-only user, and writes are rejected by the database."},"2636":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting-32","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/troubleshooting#ai-model-and-tracing","content":"Back to Set up Exasol. Next stage: Get the data."},"2637":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows","type":"page","content":"Workflows","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Set up Exasol"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows"},"2638":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows","content":"The id that every query and decision in a piece of work carries, the log file it writes, and what is never written to it."},"2639":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows#workflows","content":"Workflows"},"2640":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows#start-and-continue","content":"Start and continue"},"2641":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows#the-workflow-log","content":"The workflow log"},"2642":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows#what-is-never-written","content":"What is never written"},"2643":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows#workflows","content":"A **workflow** is one id that every query and decision in a piece of work carries. The quickstart starts it, and every later notebook continues it, so you never paste an id."},"2644":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows#start-and-continue","content":"`nb.continue_workflow` takes the workflow of this kernel, or else the last one started on this computer. It starts a new one only when there is none. Nothing is logged without an active workflow, and the kit never starts one on its own."},"2645":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows#the-workflow-log","content":"While a workflow is active, each helper that does something adds one line to its log. That includes a SQL statement, a column-map draft or approval, a model call and its trace, a dashboard revision and a hand-off. Every guided card action is a line too, with the code it ran and whether it worked."},"2646":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows#the-workflow-log","content":"The log is one file per workflow: `~/.exasol-starter-kit/workflows/<id>.jsonl`. Each line is a JSON object. The file is append-only and readable by you only. Ids look like `wf-20261027-3f9a1c`."},"2647":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows#what-is-never-written","content":"A value named like a secret is refused before anything is written."},"2648":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows#what-is-never-written","content":"A connection string with a password is refused too."},"2649":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows#what-is-never-written","content":"SQL that looks credential-bearing, such as a statement with a `PASSWORD` or `API_KEY` column, is logged with its text replaced. Its digest is kept, and a warning is shown."},"2650":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows#what-is-never-written","content":"A log that cannot be written warns, and the cell goes on. Logging never stops the work it describes."},"2651":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows#what-is-never-written","content":"The kit never writes a key into a cell, the code view or the log."},"2652":{"id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/set-up/workflows#what-is-never-written","content":"Back to Set up Exasol. Next: Set up AI and Langfuse."},"2653":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","type":"page","content":"All exakit commands","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","All personas","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/kit/reference/commands"},"2654":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-0","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands","content":"Every command of the kit, 42 in all, with what it takes and what it does."},"2655":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-1","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"Everyday"},"2656":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-2","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/reference/commands#ai-clients-mcp","content":"AI clients (MCP)"},"2657":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-3","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/reference/commands#external-sources-virtual-schemas","content":"External sources (virtual schemas)"},"2658":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-4","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/reference/commands#personas-and-notebooks","content":"Personas and notebooks"},"2659":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-5","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/reference/commands#models-and-udfs-udf-devkit-hidden-for-now","content":"Models and UDFs (udf-devkit, hidden for now)"},"2660":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-6","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/reference/commands#add-ons","content":"Add-ons"},"2661":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-7","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/reference/commands#keeping-up-to-date","content":"Keeping up to date"},"2662":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-8","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/reference/commands#repair-and-removal","content":"Repair and removal"},"2663":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-9","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/reference/commands#reference","content":"Reference"},"2664":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-10","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/reference/commands#other","content":"Other"},"2665":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-11","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands","content":"`exakit help <command>` prints a command's full reference on this computer, and `exakit catalog <word>`\nsearches them."},"2666":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-12","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"Command"},"2667":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-13","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"Takes"},"2668":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-14","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"What it does"},"2669":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-15","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"`exakit status`"},"2670":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-16","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"`[--json]`"},"2671":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-17","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"Is the database up and healthy?"},"2672":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-18","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"`exakit info`"},"2673":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-19","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"`[--json]`"},"2674":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-20","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"Your connection details."},"2675":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-21","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"`exakit start`"},"2676":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-22","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"`[<service>]`"},"2677":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-23","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"Start the database and every add-on service, or one of them."},"2678":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-24","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"`exakit stop`"},"2679":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-25","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"`[<service>]`"},"2680":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-26","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"Stop the add-on services and the database, or one of them."},"2681":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-27","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"`exakit sql`"},"2682":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-28","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"`'<statement>' \\| --file <path> \\| (stdin) [--json] [--write] [--help]`"},"2683":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-29","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"Run one SQL statement, with the error translated."},"2684":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-30","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"`exakit data-load`"},"2685":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-31","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"`[<file-or-folder-or-dataset>] [--force]`"},"2686":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-32","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"Load a dataset (downloaded only when you pick it), one file, or a whole folder."},"2687":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-33","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/reference/commands#everyday","content":"`exakit logs`"},"2688":{"id":"/kit/reference/commands-34","page_id":"/kit/reference/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/refer