page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#the-four-layers","content":"Definitions only, no rows"},"3212":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-21","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#the-four-layers","content":"Answers"},"3213":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-22","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#the-four-layers","content":"Semantic SQL is compiled into one query over the live sources"},"3214":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-23","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#the-four-layers","content":"Only the result returns"},"3215":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-24","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#an-example-measured","content":"Three sources that share no key and no column names: Amazon order lines (sample data, 128,975 rows), a PostgreSQL logistics database read live, and a state population table."},"3216":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-25","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#an-example-measured","content":"**1. Find how they join.** No foreign key exists. The kit compares values:"},"3217":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-26","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#an-example-measured","content":"The 21 rows are misspelt state names. The link stands, and you get the list to clean. It took 26 small queries."},"3218":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-27","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#an-example-measured","content":"**2. Put one model over them.**"},"3219":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-28","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#an-example-measured","content":"This published one model over the order lines and the state table, joined on the state name, a link found the same way. Why the link is there is stored with it. (The run was measured under a test model name; `sales_360` stands for it here. The PostgreSQL source was not reachable when the model was published, so its link from step 1 is not in these figures.)"},"3220":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-29","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#an-example-measured","content":"**3. Ask it.** Revenue by region needs both sources. In Semantic SQL you name what you want, not how to join:"},"3221":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-30","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#an-example-measured","content":"Region"},"3222":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-31","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#an-example-measured","content":"Order lines"},"3223":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-32","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#an-example-measured","content":"Revenue"},"3224":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-33","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#an-example-measured","content":"South"},"3225":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-34","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#an-example-measured","content":"52,761"},"3226":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-35","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#an-example-measured","content":"31,314,207.29"},"3227":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-36","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#an-example-measured","content":"North"},"3228":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-37","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#an-example-measured","content":"30,148"},"3229":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-38","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#an-example-measured","content":"19,245,528.38"},"3230":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-39","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#an-example-measured","content":"West"},"3231":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-40","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#an-example-measured","content":"27,956"},"3232":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-41","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#an-example-measured","content":"16,744,010.73"},"3233":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-42","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#an-example-measured","content":"The model compiled that into one scan, one join and one `GROUP BY`. A hand-written join returned the same figures for all 128,975 rows."},"3234":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-43","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#who-uses-the-model","content":"All three read the same definitions, so *revenue* is the same number everywhere."},"3235":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-44","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#what-it-costs","content":"Measured"},"3236":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-45","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#what-it-costs","content":"Result"},"3237":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-46","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#what-it-costs","content":"Model query on 10,002,745 rows joined to 30,000"},"3238":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-47","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#what-it-costs","content":"0.12 to 0.27 s (hand-written: 0.13 to 0.21 s)"},"3239":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-48","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#what-it-costs","content":"Finding links across six schemas, 25 tables"},"3240":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-49","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#what-it-costs","content":"223 small queries, about 60 s"},"3241":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-50","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#what-it-costs","content":"Rows copied out of a source"},"3242":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-51","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#what-it-costs","content":"0"},"3243":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-52","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#what-it-costs","content":"A live source answers at its own speed. Each query to it is a filter or an aggregate the source runs itself."},"3244":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-53","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#the-same-pattern-larger","content":"The hospital chain reference build uses this pattern on three systems that share no patient id: a legacy system on PostgreSQL, a health record on MongoDB and an imaging archive on Amazon S3. Exasol reads all three in place, resolves 1,609 patient records to 1,223 people, and answers a question across them in 0.3 to 4 seconds. The images never pass through the database."},"3245":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-54","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#limits","content":"A link between two plain number columns cannot be proven from the data: numbers in a sequence match by chance. The kit marks it for you to confirm."},"3246":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-55","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#limits","content":"A table needs an approved column map before it joins a model."},"3247":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-56","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#limits","content":"A source that is down cannot be asked. Nothing is cached unless you load a copy yourself."},"3248":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-57","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#further-reading","content":"Semantic views: the commands"},"3249":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-58","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#further-reading","content":"Links across sources: how links are found and what was measured"},"3250":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-59","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#further-reading","content":"Virtual schemas in the Exasol documentation"},"3251":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion-60","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-fusion#further-reading","content":"Exasol Semantic Views on GitHub"},"3252":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","type":"page","content":"Semantic views","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","All personas","Data"],"tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/semantic-views"},"3253":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-0","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views","content":"The kit's semantic layer is Exasol Semantic Views - one model per schema from your approved column maps, or one model across any number of sources, kept current."},"3254":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-1","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#installed-when-it-is-needed","content":"Installed when it is needed"},"3255":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-2","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#one-model-per-schema","content":"One model per schema"},"3256":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-3","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#one-model-across-sources","content":"One model across sources"},"3257":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-4","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#whole-schemas-and-links-found-for-you","content":"Whole schemas, and links found for you"},"3258":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-5","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#let-the-ai-propose-the-fields","content":"Let the AI propose the fields"},"3259":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-6","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#keep-it-current","content":"Keep it current"},"3260":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-7","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#ask-a-model","content":"Ask a model"},"3261":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-8","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#from-a-notebook","content":"From a notebook"},"3262":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-9","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#further-reading","content":"Further reading"},"3263":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-10","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views","content":"The kit's semantic layer is **Exasol Semantic Views**, the database's own semantic layer. A model says what your data means in business terms: its entities (tables), the relationships between them, the dimensions you group by and the metrics you ask for. AI clients read it over MCP and answer from its metrics; notebooks ask it with Semantic SQL."},"3264":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-11","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views","content":"You do not write a model by hand. The kit builds it from what you approved:"},"3265":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-12","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views","content":"You approved"},"3266":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-13","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views","content":"It becomes"},"3267":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-14","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views","content":"A table's column map"},"3268":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-15","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views","content":"An entity, with its key and grain"},"3269":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-16","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views","content":"A link between two tables"},"3270":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-17","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views","content":"A relationship (many-to-one)"},"3271":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-18","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views","content":"A `time`, `category` or `flag` column"},"3272":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-19","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views","content":"A dimension (a time column also gives `<column>_month`)"},"3273":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-20","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views","content":"A `measure` column"},"3274":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-21","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views","content":"A fact, and the metrics `total_<column>` and `average_<column>`"},"3275":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-22","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views","content":"Every table"},"3276":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-23","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views","content":"A row count, `<table>_count`"},"3277":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-24","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views","content":"A column marked **sensitive** is never a dimension and never a public fact."},"3278":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-25","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#installed-when-it-is-needed","content":"Semantic Views is a marketplace add-on (`semantic-views`). The first approval installs it into the database, as this would:"},"3279":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-26","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#installed-when-it-is-needed","content":"If that install fails, the approval still stands and says which command to run."},"3280":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-27","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#one-model-per-schema","content":"Approving a column map rebuilds its schema's model:"},"3281":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-28","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#one-model-per-schema","content":"The model is named after the schema (`amazon`) and its views are published in `SEM_<SCHEMA>` (`SEM_AMAZON.ORDER_LINES`). Approving a schema's links (`exakit describe --schema AMAZON --approve`) rebuilds it with the links as relationships."},"3282":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-29","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#one-model-across-sources","content":"A question often needs more than one schema: a sample dataset, your own files and one or more external sources. Build one model over all of them:"},"3283":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-30","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#one-model-across-sources","content":"Every table needs an approved column map first."},"3284":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-31","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#one-model-across-sources","content":"`--link SCHEMA.TABLE.COLUMN=SCHEMA.TABLE.KEY` joins tables of different schemas. The key side must be unique. The approved links of each schema are used too."},"3285":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-32","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#one-model-across-sources","content":"An external source (a virtual schema, `VS_<NAME>`) is read live: nothing is copied."},"3286":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-33","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#one-model-across-sources","content":"`--dry-run` prints what would be built and writes nothing. Run it again without `--dry-run` to publish."},"3287":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-34","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#whole-schemas-and-links-found-for-you","content":"Name schemas and the kit takes every table of them that has an approved column map. `--find-links` looks for the joins between the schemas in the values, with no foreign key and no matching names needed:"},"3288":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-35","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#whole-schemas-and-links-found-for-you","content":"A text link the data backs is used. A link between plain numbers is only named, because numbers in a sequence match by chance: pass it with `--link` if it is right. A pair you or an AI client believes in is checked with `exakit describe --links A,B --link S.T.COL=S.T.KEY`. How the search works, and what it measured, is on Semantic views."},"3289":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-36","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#let-the-ai-propose-the-fields","content":"With `--ai`, the model you set up for the kit (`EXAKIT_MODEL_ID` and `EXAKIT_PROVIDER_BASE_URL`) proposes business names, comments and synonyms for every field, and the metrics people will ask for: filtered totals (completed revenue), differences and ratios."},"3290":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-37","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#let-the-ai-propose-the-fields","content":"It is sent names, types, grains, column notes and a category's most frequent values. It is never sent a row, and never a sensitive column."},"3291":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-38","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#let-the-ai-propose-the-fields","content":"Every proposed metric is checked before it is used: it may only add up a fact of its view, combine that view's metrics, and filter on a dimension with one of its known values. The product validates it again when it is applied. A refused one is skipped, and the output names it and says why."},"3292":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-39","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#keep-it-current","content":"A model is built from what was approved at the time."},"3293":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-40","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#keep-it-current","content":"Approving a column map rebuilds its schema's model and every multi-source model the table is in."},"3294":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-41","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#keep-it-current","content":"After a new link or a new table, rebuild a model yourself:"},"3295":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-42","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#keep-it-current","content":"The kit only rebuilds models it built. A model of the same name that someone else made is left alone."},"3296":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-43","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#ask-a-model","content":"A published view is queried with Semantic SQL: its metrics, grouped by its dimensions."},"3297":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-44","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#ask-a-model","content":"An AI client sets the preprocessor through the Exasol MCP server (`set_exasol_preprocessor`) and runs the same query. To see what a model holds, read `SEMANTIC_CATALOG.MODELS`, `ENTITIES`, `DIMENSIONS`, `METRICS` and `RELATIONSHIPS`."},"3298":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-45","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#from-a-notebook","content":"In the guided view, the **Semantic views** card in Understand does the same: pick the tables, let the AI propose the fields, preview, publish, refresh."},"3299":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-46","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#further-reading","content":"exasol-labs/exasol-semantic-views, the add-on's repository and README."},"3300":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-47","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#further-reading","content":"What the kit writes, which schemas the semantic models create, and which tables they never change."},"3301":{"id":"/kit/data/semantic-views-48","page_id":"/kit/data/semantic-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/semantic-views#further-reading","content":"What is sent to an AI model, the exact content of the `--ai` proposal."},"3302":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","type":"page","content":"Ask your data","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Development","Notebook commands"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask"},"3303":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","content":"Ask a question, inspect the proposed SQL, approve that exact text, then run through the Exasol MCP server."},"3304":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#ask","content":"nb.ask"},"3305":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"nb.Proposal"},"3306":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","content":"The archived Governed SQL server is not installed. The kit's own model endpoint can draft SQL from an approved\ndescriptor; no SQL runs until the person approves it. The SQL runs on the launcher's MCP server beside the\ndatabase (the sidecar, on loopback), which connects as the dedicated read-only user only - never the notebook's\nadmin connection or an admin fallback. The notebook sends no password: the sidecar holds the read-only login."},"3307":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#ask","content":"Draft SQL from the user's opted-in model endpoint; `proposed_sql` supports manual drafting."},"3308":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#ask","content":"With `conn` (the notebook's connection) and a semantic model the kit built over this data, the model answers\nfrom the semantic layer: it is shown the model's metrics and dimensions, writes Semantic SQL over the published\nview, and Exasol Semantic Views compiles that into the plain SQL you read and approve - the same definitions an\nAI client over MCP uses, so both give the same number. Without a model over the data, or when the question\ncannot be put in its terms, the SQL is drafted from the approved column map as before, and the proposal says so."},"3309":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#ask","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/02_ask_your_data`"},"3310":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"A question with the SQL proposed for it. Nothing runs until `approve()` accepts that exact text; `edit()` replaces\nthe SQL and removes the approval; `run()` runs the approved text through the kit's read-only service."},"3311":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"Member"},"3312":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"What it is"},"3313":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`dataset`"},"3314":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`Any`"},"3315":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`question`"},"3316":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`str`"},"3317":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`sql`"},"3318":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`str`"},"3319":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`assumptions`"},"3320":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`list[str]`"},"3321":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`doubts`"},"3322":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`list[str]`"},"3323":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`edit(sql: str) -> Proposal`"},"3324":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`approve() -> Proposal`"},"3325":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`run()`"},"3326":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","type":"page","content":"ML Engineer checks","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Development","Notebook commands"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks"},"3327":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","content":"The three things the ML Engineer's notebooks depend on, one check each (ml-engineer/00_quickstart): the database's Python container answers a smoke UDF with the packages training needs, the MLflow server is reachable, and the bucket directory is where the kit expects it."},"3328":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks#check_bucket","content":"nb.check_bucket"},"3329":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks#check_container","content":"nb.check_container"},"3330":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks#check_mlflow","content":"nb.check_mlflow"},"3331":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks#check_model_compatibility","content":"nb.check_model_compatibility"},"3332":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks#model_list","content":"nb.model_list"},"3333":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","content":"The three things the ML Engineer's notebooks depend on, one check each (ml-engineer/00_quickstart): the database's\nPython container answers a smoke UDF with the packages training needs, the MLflow server is reachable, and the bucket\ndirectory is where the kit expects it. Each prints one line - `ok` with what it found, or `FAIL` with the reason\nand the fix - and returns True or False, so the notebook shows all three before anything stops."},"3334":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","content":"Nothing here prints a host, a user or a password; an MLflow address is shown without any credentials it holds."},"3335":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks#check_bucket","content":"The deployment's bucket directory exists on this machine where the kit says it is, and - given a connection -\na UDF sees it at its /buckets path too (skipped, with a note, when the container check fails)."},"3336":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks#check_bucket","content":"**Used in:** `ml-engineer/00_quickstart`"},"3337":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks#check_container","content":"The container behind `alias` runs a smoke UDF, and it has every package training needs. The line names the\nalias probed and the fix for that alias (PYTHON3_ML: exakit udf-use default; PYTHON3: exakit udf-setup), so the\nfix installs the container the check looks at. `alias` None is the notebook's default, ml_train.udf_container():\nPYTHON3_ML before PYTHON3 from the kit's manifest, EXAKIT_UDF_CONTAINER first; none installed is a FAIL line."},"3338":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks#check_container","content":"**Used in:** `ml-engineer/00_quickstart`"},"3339":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks#check_mlflow","content":"Check the destination runs will really use: configured server, kit server, or local store."},"3340":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks#check_mlflow","content":"**Used in:** `ml-engineer/00_quickstart`"},"3341":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks#check_model_compatibility","content":"Refuse a pickle whose scikit-learn version differs before any scoring SQL runs."},"3342":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks#check_model_compatibility","content":"**Used in:** `ml-engineer/03_score_external_model`"},"3343":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/checks#model_list","content":"What `exakit model list --json` says: bucket_dir (the host folder), udf_root (the path UDFs read it under) and\nthe models in it. Raises RuntimeError naming why it could not be read."},"3344":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","type":"page","content":"Connect, SQL and tracing","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Development","Notebook commands"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core"},"3345":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","content":"Helpers for the Exasol Personal Local Starter Kit's notebooks: exakit.nb (this module; exakit_nb is the same module under its older name)."},"3346":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#confirm_send","content":"nb.confirm_send"},"3347":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#connect","content":"nb.connect"},"3348":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#model_client","content":"nb.model_client"},"3349":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#model_settings","content":"nb.model_settings"},"3350":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#show_sql","content":"nb.show_sql"},"3351":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#sql","content":"nb.sql"},"3352":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#trace","content":"nb.trace"},"3353":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#tracing","content":"nb.tracing"},"3354":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","content":"The connection comes from the kit. Its Jupyter kernel (\"Exasol (Starter Kit)\") carries two paths: the encrypted\nconfiguration store, and the kit's credential file holding the store's master password, readable by the user only.\nThese helpers open the database from there, in JupyterLab, Marimo, VS Code or any front end that runs the\nkit's notebook Python. Nothing here prints or returns a host, a user or a password."},"3355":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","content":"The quickstarts' shared steps (check_connection, list_schemas, load_sample, load_source, ...) are in quickstart.py;\nthe ML Engineer's checks (check_container, check_mlflow, check_bucket) in checks.py."},"3356":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#confirm_send","content":"Before sampled rows go to a model endpoint: True at once for a table in the database; for a live source (the\ndescriptor names a source) it names the source and asks, and only a yes sends. `answer` answers for a script;\nwith no one to ask (a headless run) the answer is no."},"3357":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#confirm_send","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`"},"3358":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#connect","content":"A pyexasol connection to the local database, opened from the kit's encrypted store, pinned to the database's\nTLS certificate once the kit has recorded it. Exasol's usage telemetry stays off unless EXASOL_TELEMETRY_DISABLE\nwas already set."},"3359":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#connect","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`, `data-scientist/02_ask_your_data`, `data-scientist/03_share`, `ml-engineer/01_train`, `ml-engineer/02_rust_score`, `ml-engineer/03_score_external_model`"},"3360":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#model_client","content":"(client, model ID) for EXAKIT_MODEL_ID and EXAKIT_PROVIDER_BASE_URL; EXAKIT_PROVIDER_API_KEY is optional for\nservers without authentication. Tracing uses Langfuse's instrumented client for the same endpoint and key.\nThis interface makes text Chat Completions calls; it does not provide a provider's native API features."},"3361":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#model_client","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`"},"3362":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#model_settings","content":"Display the chosen model and endpoint without the API key or custom header values; makes no request."},"3363":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#model_settings","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"3364":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#show_sql","content":"Print the last statement sql() ran, so a result can always be traced to the query behind it."},"3365":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#show_sql","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`, `data-scientist/01_explore`, `ml-engineer/00_quickstart`"},"3366":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#sql","content":"Run a query and return its rows as a pandas DataFrame; the statement is remembered for show_sql()."},"3367":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#sql","content":"The rows come over the normal connection rather than pyexasol's HTTP export, which needs the database to connect\nback to this machine - not a given through the local VM or Podman."},"3368":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#sql","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`, `data-scientist/01_explore`, `ml-engineer/00_quickstart`, `ml-engineer/02_rust_score`, `ml-engineer/03_score_external_model`"},"3369":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#trace","content":"Group the model calls made inside the block into one trace in the user's own Langfuse project, tagged with the\ndatabase session, the sample SQL, the workflow id and, given a dataset, its id, descriptor digest and descriptor\nversion (trace_tags). Opt-in: without LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY, LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY and LANGFUSE_BASE_URL (LANGFUSE_HOST,\nthe SDK 3/4 name, still counts) it says so in one line and does nothing else - no exception, no prompt."},"3370":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#trace","content":"Langfuse SDK 5: the block is one observation (`Langfuse.start_as_current_observation`) and, right inside it, the\ntrace name, session id, tags and metadata are propagated (`langfuse.propagate_attributes`, a module function in\nSDK 5) to it and to every observation opened within, so each call the client model_client() returns makes -\nLangfuse's OpenAI drop-in when tracing is on - lands in this one trace with its input, output, token usage and\nlatency, without changes to the calling code. The span is yielded; the client is flushed when the block ends.\nThe active workflow's log gets one `trace` line with the trace id (X-1), and when the block ends one line is\nprinted - `traced: <trace id> (<url or base URL>)` - so the trace can be found in Langfuse. Nothing here prints\nor records the secret key."},"3371":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#tracing","content":"Whether LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY, LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY and LANGFUSE_BASE_URL (or LANGFUSE_HOST) are all set, so trace()\nrecords to the user's Langfuse."},"3372":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/core#tracing","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"3373":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp","type":"page","content":"Dash Server tools","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Development","Notebook commands"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp"},"3374":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp","content":"Call the kit-managed Dash Server through its MCP control plane."},"3375":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp#dash_tools","content":"nb.dash_tools"},"3376":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp#DashTools","content":"nb.DashTools"},"3377":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp#dash_tools","content":"The notebook's Dash Server tool adapter; each call is an MCP tool call. When Dash Server is not installed or\nnot running, it is installed and started first, the way nb.addon_ready(\"dash-server\") does it (`exakit\nmarketplace dash-server`, `exakit start dash-server`), with its progress shown: a cell that previews a dashboard\nworks on its own, and nothing is asked. `ready=False` only reports: it raises when the server is not there."},"3378":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp#dash_tools","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/03_share`"},"3379":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dash-mcp#DashTools","content":"Synchronous adapter for notebook cells, which already run an event loop."},"3380":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks","type":"page","content":"Data checks","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Development","Notebook commands"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks"},"3381":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks","content":"Prepare and Validate: what the data itself says is wrong with it, and any column that gives the label away."},"3382":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks#data_checks","content":"nb.data_checks"},"3383":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks#leakage_check","content":"nb.leakage_check"},"3384":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks","content":"Both are built from the descriptor alone - the key, the label and every column's role - so no column name is typed in\na notebook and the same cell runs on every dataset. Each check is one or two SQL statements, run through nb.sql (so\nthey are shown and logged like every other query), and each finding is one plain sentence saying what it does to a\nresult. Nothing is changed in the data: deciding what to do about a finding is the user's."},"3385":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks#data_checks","content":"Prepare: one row per finding - CHECK, COLUMN_NAME, ROWS_AFFECTED, PCT, MEANS - for repeated keys, repeated\nidentifiers, exact copies of a row, empty cells, placeholder values and a rare label. Prints each finding in one\nsentence (`show=False` only returns them); an empty frame means the table passed every check."},"3386":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks#data_checks","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`"},"3387":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks#leakage_check","content":"Validate: the columns whose values (almost) decide the label on their own - each a value or values where the\nlabel is (nearly) always 1 or always 0, covering most rows. Such a column is usually written after the outcome\n(an order's status once it was cancelled) and makes any model look perfect; leave it out of the features. Returns\nthose columns (none: the list is empty) and prints why each was flagged."},"3388":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-checks#leakage_check","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`"},"3389":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","type":"page","content":"Data map","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Development","Notebook commands"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map"},"3390":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","content":"One semantic map of everything the database holds, wherever it came from."},"3391":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map#data_map","content":"nb.data_map"},"3392":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"nb.DataMap"},"3393":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","content":"Three origins, one view:"},"3394":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","content":"\\*\\*sample\\*\\*: a dataset the kit ships (`exakit data-load amazon_sales`);"},"3395":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","content":"\\*\\*local\\*\\*: your own file or folder (`exakit data-load <path>`, the quickstart's MY_DATA cell);"},"3396":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","content":"\\*\\*source\\*\\*: a connected external source, read live through its virtual schema (`exakit connect`)."},"3397":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","content":"Roles come from the approved column maps in the kit's store, and the semantic layer is Exasol Semantic Views: a table\nthat is an entity of a semantic model the kit built says which model (SEMANTIC_CATALOG.ENTITIES). The links are the\napproved schema maps' and the multi-source models' (nb.semantic_model). Columns that share a key-like name across\ntwo tables are listed as possible links: a lead to check, never a join made for you. Only metadata is read."},"3398":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map#data_map","content":"The semantic map of the database: every table by origin (sample, local, source) with its rows, columns,\ncolumn-map state and roles, then the links between tables - declared, found by an approved schema map, or a\nshared key-like column name across two tables (marked possible). Reads metadata only; returns a DataMap that\nshows itself as a table in a notebook. `include_kit` keeps the kit's own schemas in."},"3399":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"What data_map found: tables, columns and links, each a list of dicts; DataFrames through the properties."},"3400":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"Member"},"3401":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"What it is"},"3402":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`table_rows`"},"3403":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`list[dict[str, Any]]`"},"3404":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`column_rows`"},"3405":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`list[dict[str, Any]]`"},"3406":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`link_rows`"},"3407":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`list[dict[str, Any]]`"},"3408":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`tables`"},"3409":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`columns`"},"3410":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`links`"},"3411":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`table(name: str) -> dict[str, Any]`"},"3412":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"One table's row, by SCHEMA.TABLE (any case)."},"3413":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`roles(name: str) -> dict[str, str]`"},"3414":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"\\{column: role} of one table's approved column map; empty when it has none yet."},"3415":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset","type":"page","content":"Datasets","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Development","Notebook commands"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset"},"3416":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset","content":"A dataset the notebooks run on: its descriptor read, validated by the kit's own rules, held against the database, and the roles turned into SQL names, so one notebook runs unchanged on any dataset whose descriptor is valid."},"3417":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset#chosen_dataset","content":"nb.chosen_dataset"},"3418":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"nb.Dataset"},"3419":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset#dataset","content":"nb.dataset"},"3420":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset#DescriptorNotApproved","content":"nb.DescriptorNotApproved"},"3421":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset","content":"The rules are the kit's descriptor rules (`descriptor_rules`, shipped with this package: the 0.2 kit has no Python\npackage to import them from). It is a copy of tools/descriptor_rules.py, which tools/dataset_check.py uses, and\ntests/test_notebook_contents.py holds the two byte-identical. Nothing is guessed: a descriptor that is invalid, or\nnames a table or column the database lacks, stops the notebook with the reason."},"3422":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset","content":"Which descriptor a name resolves to, in order: a path given (a file, or a folder holding descriptor.yaml); for a\ndata file of your own, `<name>.descriptor.yaml` beside it; for an id, the approved version in the kit's store\n(`~/.exasol-starter-kit/descriptors/<SCHEMA>.<TABLE>/current.yaml`, or an older kit's `descriptors/<id>/current`;\ndescriptor_store), then the descriptor the kit ships under\n`data/datasets/<id>/`. `ds.descriptor_path` and `ds.descriptor_origin` say which one was used."},"3423":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset#chosen_dataset","content":"The dataset a notebook works on: `name` when it is set; with None, the one approved last in a quickstart (so\npicking fraud_transactions there carries on here), else amazon_sales. Says which, and why, in one line."},"3424":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset#chosen_dataset","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`, `data-scientist/02_ask_your_data`, `data-scientist/03_share`, `ml-engineer/01_train`, `ml-engineer/02_rust_score`, `ml-engineer/03_score_external_model`"},"3425":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"A validated descriptor whose every role the database holds, with the SQL names the notebooks build queries from."},"3426":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"Member"},"3427":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"What it is"},"3428":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"t