n approved descriptor was given a draft; the message says how to approve it."},"3486":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe","type":"page","content":"Describe a table","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Development","Notebook commands"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe"},"3487":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe","content":"Describe a table from a notebook (DS-2, DS-5): the role-per-column descriptor of setup/lib/descriptor."},"3488":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe#describe","content":"nb.describe"},"3489":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe#Draft","content":"nb.Draft"},"3490":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe","content":"describe() on a table whose approved descriptor still matches it returns that one (force=True profiles again);\notherwise the table is profiled once, in SQL, and every column gets one of eight roles with the evidence that chose\nit; the slots name the columns the notebooks use. show() lists each column with the schema and table it came from,\nits type, role, confidence, evidence and note, low confidence first, the slots above (rows() gives the same as dicts;\na notebook renders it as a table). approve() checks every column has a role and none sits in two slots, checks\nthe table has not changed since it was profiled, writes the next version into the kit's store and rebuilds the\nschema's Exasol Semantic Views model with it - the roles become its dimensions, facts and metrics; Semantic Views is\ninstalled first when the database does not have it (a publish that fails leaves the approval standing, and says\nwhy). The active workflow's log gets one line."},"3491":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe","content":"The work is the kit's own service, setup/lib/describe_service.py in the kit copy (the one `exakit describe` runs),\nloaded from its file and run in this process over the kit's connection; without the kit copy, `exakit describe --json` runs as a child process instead."},"3492":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe","content":"The role review (role_picker) speaks the five roles of earlier descriptors - entity, category, date, label, text - so\n`roles`, `evidence`, `missing` and `set(role, column)` read and write the matching slots: date is the time\nslot and label the target."},"3493":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe#describe","content":"Describe `SCHEMA.TABLE` (or a dataset id's table): the approved descriptor when the table still matches it,\nelse a fresh draft. Uses the connection given, else opens the kit's. Only SELECTs run."},"3494":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/describe#Draft","content":"A descriptor proposed for a table (status draf