ABLE.KEY)."},"3790":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference-194","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference","content":"`nb.semantic_models`"},"3791":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference-195","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference","content":"Every semantic model in the database: name, published schema, whether the kit built it (and can refresh it)."},"3792":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference-196","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference","content":"`nb.semantic_sql`"},"3793":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference-197","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference","content":"Run Semantic SQL (a query over a published semantic view: its metrics with GROUP BY its dimensions) on this connection: Semantic SQL is switched on for the session first."},"3794":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference-198","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference","content":"`nb.SemanticModel`"},"3795":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference-199","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference","content":"A semantic model: what it holds (`spec`), what the AI proposed, and - once published - its views."},"3796":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference-200","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference","content":"`nb.share`"},"3797":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference-201","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference","content":"Make a draft from approved data and inspected SQL; measure=count enables count totals and composition."},"3798":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference-202","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference","content":"`nb.ShareDraft`"},"3799":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference-203","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference","content":"A dashboard prepared from an approved dataset and one query."},"3800":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference-204","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference","content":"`nb.show_roles`"},"3801":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference-205","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference","content":"The descriptor's roles, one per line, as the notebook will use them."},"3802":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference-206","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference","content":"`nb.show_sql`"},"3803":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference-207","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference","content":"Print the last statement sql() ran, so a result can always be traced to the query behind it."},"3804":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference-208","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference","content":"`nb.source_engine`"},"3805":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference-209","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference","content":"Ask the kit's own source engine (setup/virtual-schemas/engine/cli.py, the coordinator behind `exakit connect` a