cientist/development/reference/semantic-42","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/semantic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/semantic#SemanticModel","content":"`publish(conn=None) -> SemanticModel`"},"4215":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/semantic-43","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/semantic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/semantic#SemanticModel","content":"Build the previewed model in the database (the AI's proposal is asked again only if none was kept)."},"4216":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env","type":"page","content":"Model, Langfuse and MLflow settings","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Development","Notebook commands"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env"},"4217":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env","content":"The optional settings, set from a notebook cell: your model and Langfuse (use_model), the MLflow server (use_mlflow)."},"4218":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env#forget_model","content":"nb.forget_model"},"4219":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env#model_setup","content":"nb.model_setup"},"4220":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env#use_mlflow","content":"nb.use_mlflow"},"4221":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env#use_model","content":"nb.use_model"},"4222":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env","content":"They are the environment variables `exakit notebook` already reads (EXAKIT_MODEL_ID, EXAKIT_PROVIDER_BASE_URL,\nEXAKIT_PROVIDER_API_KEY, LANGFUSE\\_\\*, MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI), so a cell is one more way to give them, not another kind of\nsetting. The plain values come from the cell. The keys are asked for in a hidden prompt and kept in this kernel's\nenvironment only: never in the notebook or its outputs, and gone when the kernel stops - unless `remember=True`,\nwhich saves them beside the kit's credentials (readable by this user only, 0600) so every notebook's kernel has them\n(`import exakit.nb` loads them; `forget_model()` deletes them). A key already set (by\nthe shell that started JupyterLab, or an earlier run of the cell) is not asked again - unless the address it was for\nchanged. Empty values change nothing, so a cell left as shipped is a no-op and a headless run never waits on a prompt."},"4223":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env#forget_model","content":"Delete what use_model(..., remember=True) saved (the model, Langfuse, or both) and clear it from this kernel."},"4224":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env#forget_model","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"4225":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env#model_setup","content":"Set up your model and Langfuse for this kernel, and say how to set them for every notebook. Inside a notebook\n(JupyterLab or Marimo) it first asks for what is missing - the model id and address, the Langfuse address, then\neach key in a hidden box; Enter skips one. `ask=False` only reports; a script or test never waits on a prompt.\nThen it prints what is set and, for anything still missing, the terminal lines for this machine (Windows, Mac,\nLinux or WSL). Prints values, never a key; returns \\{\"machine\", \"set\", \"missing\", \"lines\", \"asked\"}."},"4226":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env#model_setup","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`, `data-scientist/02_ask_your_data`"},"4227":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env#use_mlflow","content":"The MLflow server this kernel records runs to: `tracking_uri` (empty: the kit's own MLflow, or what the shell\nset); `login=True` asks for the server's username and password (hidden). Prints where runs go, never a password."},"4228":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env#use_mlflow","content":"**Used in:** `ml-engineer/00_quickstart`, `ml-engineer/01_train`"},"4229":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env#use_model","content":"Your model and Langfuse tracing for this kernel. `model_id` and `provider_base_url` (a Chat Completions base\nURL) set the model and ask for its API key (Enter for none: a local server); `effort` sets how hard a reasoning\nmodel thinks (\"low\", \"medium\", \"high\"; \"\" for the model's default; nb.effort_levels says which a model takes);\n`langfuse_base_url` turns tracing on and asks for its two keys. Prints what is in use, never a key; returns that summary."},"4230":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/setup-env#use_model","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`, `data-scientist/01_explore`, `data-scientist/02_ask_your_data`"},"4231":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/share","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/share","type":"page","content":"Share a dashboard","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Development","Notebook commands"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/share"},"4232":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/share-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/share","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/share","content":"Prepare a governed Dash Server dashboard and promote only a reviewed preview."},"4233":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/share-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/share","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/share#share","content":"nb.share"},"4234":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/share-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/share","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/development/reference/share#ShareDraft","content":"nb.ShareDraft"},"4235":{"id":"/data-scientist/development/reference/share-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/development/