 whose values are all in another table's key. The kit finds two kinds:"],[1384,"A link you publish becomes a relationship of the model. Its evidence is stored with it: who proposed it, how many rows matched, and which values did not. Read it back with:"],[2880,"A list of add-on ids, or `\"all\"` or `\"none\"`"],[2876,"A list of dataset ids, or `\"all\"` or `\"none\"`"],[3243,"A live source answers at its own speed. Each query to it is a filter or an aggregate the source runs itself."],[2560,"A local Exasol database that answers, the kit's notebooks ready to open, and a workflow that logs what you do. Next, load the data you will work on in Get the data."],[2455,"A local Ollama needs no key and no Langfuse. After you load a chat model:"],[2001,"A log that cannot be written warns, and the cell goes on. Logging never fails the work it describes."],[2650,"A log that cannot be written warns, and the cell goes on. Logging never stops the work it describes."],[1663,"a measure and a category"],[1313,"A measure is a **fact**, with the metrics `total_<column>` and `average_<column>`."],[2505,"A model and a tracing setup you have checked, or a clear choice to leave them off. The notebooks use the same settings."],[1990,"A model call is traced to Langfuse, with the trace id"],[3065,"A model call was traced"],[1319,"A model can span any number of schemas: sample datasets, your own files and folders, and connected external sources, which are read live. Every table in it needs an approved column map first."],[3292,"A model is built from what was approved at the time."],[1988,"A model is trained and scored, with its row count and, where the note shows one, its score"],[2347,"A model needs an explicit base URL. With no model ID, the AI steps stay off."],[1176,"A model never approves roles. The kit never chooses the target. You approve."],[226,"A model or Langfuse key, only if you asked for `remember=True`"],[4179,"A model spans as many schemas as you give it: sample datasets, your own loaded files and folders, and any number of\nconnected external sources (virtual schemas, read live). Every table needs an approved column map first: its roles\ndecide the model's fields - time, category and flag columns become dimensions, measures become facts with total\\_ and\naverage\\_ metrics, every table gets a row count. The approved links of each schema are used, and `links` adds the\nones across schemas (SCHEMA.TABLE.COLUMN=SCHEMA.TABLE.KEY, the key side unique)."],[2127,"A model that always gives the common answer is right most of the time. Judge a model by a ranking score, or by the baseline. Never by accuracy alone."],[444,"A model that sees column names and values can infer what a sensitive column holds. The kit keeps the values out, not the inference."],[1324,"A model was built over the approved prepared view `EXAKIT_PREPARED.AMAZON__ORDER_LINES` and over `EXAKIT_PREPARED.RETAIL_SIGNALS__CUSTOMER_REVIEWS__PLAIN`, and published. It has 2 views, 20 dimensions and 6 metrics: `amazon_order_lines_count`, `total_qty`, `average_qty`, `total_amount`, `average_amount`, and the reviews' row count."],[3063,"A model was trained and scored"],[1692,"A model with every column is only worth keeping if it does better than a simple rule. The baseline is that simple rule. If a real model cannot beat it, the columns carry little signal about the outcome. The kit has two baselines."],[1037,"A model's published semantic views, queried with Semantic SQL"],[2063,"A new table, or a new link between tables"],[3099,"A new version of the column map, kept under `~/.exasol-starter-kit/descriptors/`, and the schema's semantic model (its views in `SEM_<SCHEMA>`) rebuilt from it. The notebooks and AI clients read the approved version from then on."],[919,"A notebook is cells that call the helpers. A card is a form that calls the same helpers. Neither talks to the database on its own."],[960,"A notebook is cells that call the helpers. A card is a form that calls the same helpers. N