abase, opened from the kit's encrypted store, pinned to the database's TLS certificate once the kit has recorded it."],[3282,"A question often needs more than one schema: a sample dataset, your own files and one or more external sources. Build one model over all of them:"],[3769,"A question with the SQL proposed for it."],[3310,"A question with the SQL proposed for it. Nothing runs until `approve()` accepts that exact text; `edit()` replaces\nthe SQL and removes the approval; `run()` runs the approved text through the kit's read-only service."],[1996,"A question's SQL is approved, and its answer is read"],[3061,"A question's SQL was approved, and it answered"],[683,"A random share, with a fixed seed. For yes or no it is stratified, so both sides keep the same share of 1s."],[2150,"A rare-outcome line: a model that always says \"not fraud\" is right 95.1% of the time"],[1936,"A record of what each run did, a column map whose versions you can read and restore, a semantic model that matches the approved roles, and a plain list of what needs redoing. The loop has no end. When something changes, go back to the stage in the table on What changed, and where you go and work forward from there."],[3270,"A relationship (many-to-one)"],[2138,"A repeated-id line for `TRANSACTION_ID`. The row key `ROW_ID` is unique."],[4068,"A result column named after a data column: `CANCELLED` + `PCT` -> `CANCELLED_PCT`; quotes, dots and\nspaces become underscores, so the name works unquoted in SQL."],[3751,"A result column named after a data column: `CANCELLED` + `PCT` -> `CANCELLED_PCT`; quotes, dots and spaces become underscores, so the name works unquoted in SQL."],[3276,"A row count, `<table>_count`"],[1656,"a rule: suggest up to four, use only those kinds and existing column names, and never use the target or a column filled in after the outcome"],[2025,"A running kernel keeps the helpers it loaded before the update. Restart it: in JupyterLab, **Kernel**, then **Restart Kernel**."],[2614