on."],[2961,"A tool you installed yourself is recognised and never offered again."],[1992,"A training hand-off or a hand-off bundle is written"],[1954,"A training hand-off that went stale"],[1956,"A training hand-off that went stale"],[2086,"A typed, cleaned view"],[845,"A useful signal"],[3425,"A validated descriptor whose every role the database holds, with the SQL names the notebooks build queries from."],[3659,"A validated descriptor whose every role the database holds, with the SQL names the notebooks build queries from."],[2173,"a value compared with its group's usual value,"],[2647,"A value named like a secret is refused before anything is written."],[2282,"A value such as `Unknown Device` looks like a category and means \"not known\". Treat it as empty. The typed view turns it into `NULL` for you, when the check can list its values."],[3204,"A virtual schema (`VS_<NAME>`) per external source. A query is pushed down to the source"],[1413,"A warning about a column that gives the target away is not an error. The column stays in the map and is left out of the model. Read the warning, check the column, and approve. If the column is correct, keep it in the map. The model still leaves it out. For the rule, see Columns that give the answer away."],[843,"A weak signal"],[876,"A whole new module gets its own reference page automatically, titled from its file name. Give it a proper title and a place in the order by adding one line to `PAGES` in `tools/nb_docs.py`."],[3082,"A whole schema"],[497,"A whole schema's map (its tables and the links between them) is kept the same way, in `descriptors/<SCHEMA>/`, with `v<n>.json` files. `setup/lib/descriptor/schema.py` says those are never rewritten."],[1980,"A workflow begins, with its name, the kit version, and the Python and platform"],[1975,"A workflow is the record of one piece of work across the notebooks. Its log is the file where each helper that does something writes a line. The workflows reference describes the workflow as a kit feature. This page covers what the log holds."],[841,"About as good as guessing"],[3100,"Add `--json` to any of them for a script."],[3072,"Add `--json` to either command for a script."],[864,"Add a command"],[3112,"Add a dataset to the kit"],[871,"Add a function to a module in `notebook/package/exakit_nb/`, with a docstring. The first sentence becomes its one-line summary here; the rest becomes its reference text. Indented lines in a docstring are shown as code."],[989,"Add a function with a docstring to a module in `notebook/package/exakit_nb/`. Export it in `exakit_nb/__init__.py` and add its name to `__all__`."],[4164,"Add a link the search missed: `link(\"ORDERS.CUSTOMER_REF\", \"CUSTOMERS.ID\")`."],[865,"Add an exakit.nb helper, wire it to a card, and get its documentation for free."],[2822,"Add another persona to this kit"],[991,"Add one entry to `actions.ACTIONS` in `exakit_guide/actions.py`, so a card can have a button for it."],[874,"Add one entry to `actions.ACTIONS` in `exakit_guide/actions.py`: the code and the notebook it belongs to. Have the screen call `actions.run(...)`."],[873,"Add the call to the code section of the notebook it belongs to, guarded by a variable when it is optional:"],[2812,"Add the Kit 2 trust assets to this install (internal)."],[1359,"Add the links across schemas, one per line, in the form `SCHEMA.TABLE.COLUMN=SCHEMA.TABLE.KEY`. The approved links inside each schema are used on their own."],[128,"Add-on"],[51,"Add-ons"],[2660,"Add-ons"],[2907,"Add-ons"],[2934,"Add-ons"],[63,"Add-ons and downloads"],[299,"Add-ons and downloads"],[2951,"Add-ons are optional tools around the database: dashboards, notebooks and more. A persona installs the ones it needs. You can add or remove any of them later."],[2820,"Add-ons for your personas"],[70,"Add-ons the kit did not install"],[2932,"Add-ons, with each add-on's repository and documentation."],[942,"Adding a command"],[327,"Address"],[311,"Addresses the kit listens on"],[3294,"After a new link or a new table, rebuild a model yourself:"],[2957,"After an install, `exakit status` shows whether a service add-on is running, and `exakit help <add-on>` prints its full reference."],[1093,"After the approval, the cell that follows it runs the leakage check. The printed line for a column that gives the answer away has this form:"],[1946,"After you update the kit, restart the kernel. A running kernel keeps the helpers it loaded before the update. In JupyterLab, choose **Kernel**, then **Restart Kernel**."],[284,"AI clients"],[287,"AI clients"],[290,"AI clients"],[2656,"AI clients (MCP)"],[57,"AI clients and skills"],[2995,"AI clients and skills"],[155,"AI clients and the read-only user"],[3014,"AI clients and the read-only user, the security view of the same connection, with its limits."],[3189,"AI clients and the read-only user, which explains why `exakit sql` is not the read-only path."],[164,"AI clients never connect as the admin. The kit creates a second database user, `mcp_readonly` (the default of `EXAKIT_MCP_READONLY_USER`, set in `setup/lib/common.sh`), and the Exasol MCP server connects as that user. The server runs beside the database, on 127.0.0.1, by default on port 4896 (`EXAKIT_MCP_SIDECAR_PORT`)."],[2608,"AI model and tracing"],[35,"AI skills"],[3595,"All commands"],[59,"All exakit commands"],[2653,"All exakit commands"],[3234,"All three read the same definitions, so *revenue* is the same number everywhere."],[1601,"Allow this computer's address at the source: a firewall rule, a security group or the server's access list."],[1805,"Almost every row is different"],[760,"Also on the held-out rows"],[1811,"Always: its role says leave it out"],[1808,"Always. Free text is not a column the lab can read."],[1153,"Amazon sales"],[926,"An action's call exists in its notebook's code section, and calls something `exakit.nb` exports."],[502,"An add-on installation the kit did not make. See Add-ons and downloads."],[3297,"An AI client sets the prepro