me answers whether the counts or the outcome rate move. The kit runs both on the approved dataset. It shows the SQL before each result, and writes a plain-language note under it, so a result is not read without its meaning."],[656,"Comparing models"],[666,"Compute it in your own code, on the rows you have, and say in your write-up that the kit did not compute it. `cv` is the mean of the fold scores and `cv_sd` is their standard deviation, so the two are a starting point. They are not a full analysis."],[1368,"Confidence"],[2997,"Connect"],[1428,"Connect a database or lake that stays where it is, read its tables as you query them, connect from this computer, and keep passwords out of the notebook."],[2291,"Connect a text model and, optionally, Langfuse tracing. Where to get each key, how to give it to the kit, what the kit sends, and how to check it works."],[2545,"Connect AI clients"],[56,"Connect an AI client"],[3633,"Connect an external source as a virtual schema, from a notebook cell."],[4282,"Connect an external source as a virtual schema, from a notebook cell. `connector` is the kit's id or alias\n(`postgresql`, `pg`, `mysql`, `snowflake` ...; `exakit help connect` lists them), `name` becomes the\nschema `VS_<NAME>`. Give the source's connection string as `url` (a JDBC URL, `postgres://...`), or each\ninput as a keyword (`host=`, `database=`, `schema=`, `user=` ...; the connector's skill lists them).\nThe password is asked in a hidden box (Enter: none), or read from `password_file`; a password inside `url` is\ntaken out of it and used, never shown. Marimo has no hidden prompt: pass a password field as `password`\n(`mo.ui.text(kind=\"password\")`, its value is read) or a `password_file`. `dry_run` checks the inputs and\nconnects nothing. A connector with several kinds of source in one takes its settings as keywords too\n(`catalog=\"unity\", files=\"s3\"` for a Lakehouse; nb.connector_inputs lists them). A source with a second secret\n(a Lakehouse catalog login plus storage keys) takes it as `storage_secret_file`, or as `storage_secret` (the\ntext, a Marimo password field, or a function that asks for it): it reaches the kit in a file only this user can\nread, removed as soon as the kit has read it. Returns the schema name (`VS_SALES`) when connected, None for a dry run; raises SourceProblem with the kit's reason otherwise."],[1430,"Connect from this computer"],[2996,"Connect your AI clients to the database, check the connection, and see the skills the kit gives them."],[2696,"Connect your AI clients."],[4280,"connect_source runs `exakit connect <connector> --name <name> ... --password-stdin --yes --json`. The password is\nasked in a hidden box and goes to the command on standard input: never into the cell, the command line or a log."],[3344,"Connect, SQL and tracing"],[3177,"Connection refused"],[3203,"Connectors"],[2744,"Copy a file into BucketFS and print the path a UDF reads it from."],[2779,"Copy an older kit's container database into this one."],[1245,"Correct the map"],[1252,"Correct the map when the search misses a link or finds a wrong one:"],[2134,"Count"],[1181,"Count rows by group and over time with the SQL shown, and read the plain-language notes the kit writes under each result."],[1133,"Counting rows without repeats"],[2429,"Create an account at cloud.langfuse.com/auth/sign-up, or sign in if you have one. The getting-started guide describes the same steps."],[4268,"Create and health-check a preview; on Windows use build + healthcheck."],[2236,"Create the joined view"],[2242,"Create the joined view when you want it:"],[4016,"Create the view (after the user has read it), describe it, carry the table's roles over and approve them; returns the view's dataset, which the later steps then use."],[2747,"Create, build and deploy a Rust scoring UDF from exported coefficients."],[461,"Created by"],[2255,"Created by"],[4318,"Credential-shaped payload keys are checked recursively, including JSON-encoded metadata strings. A secret-named key\nor a DSN containing a password is refused (a\nValueError - the caller's mistake, before anything is written). SQL text is screened rather than refused: a statement\nthat mentions PASSWORD, API_KEY, IDENTIFIED BY and the like - or carries a DSN with a password - is logged with its\ntext replaced by `<redacted: credential-like SQL>` and `redacted: true`, its digest kept, and one warning; the\nlogger never fails the query it records, which has already run. Other SQL text is kept so the user can find the\nquery again."],[305,"Credentials"],[204,"Credentials and passwords"],[1886,"Cross-validated R squared"],[1883,"Cross-validated ROC AUC, or PR AUC when the rarer answer is under 5%"],[1729,"Cross-validation falls by 0.005 or more"],[1726,"Cross-validation rises by 0.005 or more, and the held-out score does not fall by more than 0.002"],[3147,"CSV, Parquet and JSON are loaded. JSON is split into tables by an engine the kit installs for you on macOS, Linux and WSL. A `;`-separated CSV is loaded with its delimiter. A tabular `.txt` or `.tsv` file is listed with the rename to `.csv` that the loader needs."],[108,"Dash Server (`dash-server`)"],[3373,"Dash Server tools"],[151,"Dash Server, dbt-exasol, pyexasol and the notebook package are pinned by version only. The kit checks no digest for them."],[2943,"dash-server"],[1945,"Dashboards and hand-off bundles are not rebuilt by a rerun. Make a new draft and a new bundle when the result changes."],[2102,"Data checks"],[3380,"Data checks"],[3156,"Data in another database is not copied. It is connected with `exakit connect` and read where it lives. See Sources."],[3389,"Data map"],[61,"Data Scientist"],[3127,"Data Scientist, ML Engineer"],[3130,"Data Scientist, ML Engineer"],[1434,"Data source"],[2819,"Data to load"],[335,"Database"],[1047,"Database users and roles, for the users behind the credentials folder."],[1146,"Dataset"],[3114,"Dataset"],[2906,"Datasets"],[3107,"Datasets"],[3415,"Datasets"],[38,"Datasets to practise on"],[2944,"dbt-exasol"],[112,"dbt-exasol, pyexasol, notebook"],[2850,"Define your own persona"],[3211,"Definitions only, no rows"],[3691,"Delete what use_model(..., remember=True) saved (the model, Langfuse, or both) and clear it from this kernel."],[4223,"Delete what use_model(..., remember=True) saved (the model, Langfuse, or both) and clear it from this kernel."],[523,"Deploying a model"],[525,"Deploying a model"],[3493,"Describe `SCHEMA.TABLE` (or a dataset id's table): the approved descriptor when the table still matches it,\nelse a fresh draft. Uses the connection given, else opens the kit's. Only SELECTs run."],[3663,"Describe `SCHEMA.TABLE` (or a dataset id's table): the approved descriptor when the table still matches it, else a fresh draft."],[3486,"Describe a table"],[3487,"Describe a table from a notebook (DS-2, DS-5): the role-per-column descriptor of setup/lib/descriptor."],[3182,"Describe it first"],[384,"Describe what you did and what you saw. These help the team reproduce it:"],[3490,"describe() on a table whose approved descriptor still matches it returns that one (force=True profiles again);\notherwise the table is profiled once, in SQL, and every column gets one of eight roles with the evidence that chose\nit; the slots name the columns the notebooks use. show() lists each column with the schema and table it came from,\nits type, role, confidence, evidence and note, low confidence first, the slots above (rows() gives the same as dicts;\na notebook renders it as a table). approve() checks every column has a role and none sits in two slots, checks\nthe table has not changed since it was profiled, writes the next version into the kit's store and rebuilds the\nschema's Exasol Semantic Views model with it - the roles become its dimensions, facts and metrics; Semantic Views is\ninstalled first when the database does not have it (a publish that fails leaves the approval standing, and says\nwhy). The active workflow's log gets one line."],[340,"Destination"],[1464,"Details"],[1437,"Details and optional settings"],[434,"Detection is a set of patterns. It can miss personal data that does not match them, for example a free-text note that contains a name. Check a column map before you approve it, and mark a column yourself if it is wrong."],[3952,"Determinism (AC-ML3.4): the plan is a pure function of the handoff and the options - the features keep the handoff's\norder (the input schema, which the feature view fixes), a constant feature is dropped by a MIN/MAX query whose answer\ndepends on the data alone, and the rendered UDF trains `LogisticRegression(random_state=seed, solver=\"lbfgs\")` over\nrows it sorts first - so the same handoff, seed and data give the same metrics and the same coefficients."],[10,"Developers"],[937,"Development"],[153,"Digests taken from a release, rather than from `versions.json`, check the download against that release only."],[3362,"Display the chosen model and endpoint without the API key or custom header values; makes no request."],[3747,"Display the chosen model and endpoint without the API key or custom header values; makes no request."],[1690,"Do not judge a rare answer by accuracy"],[2350,"Do not put a username, a password, a query or a request path such as `/chat/completions` in the base URL. Put authentication in the key setting, not in a custom `Authorization` or `api-key` header."],[390,"Do not send the contents of `~/.exasol-starter-kit/credentials/`, `~/.exapump/config.toml`, the notebook connection store, or an `exakit.env` file. Describe the problem without them."],[144,"Do not set these for a normal install. A setting left in your shell applies to every later install."],[3544,"Documentation"],[2,"Documentation for the Exasol Personal Local Starter Kit, one section for the kit itself and one per persona."],[2381,"Download LM Studio from lmstudio.ai and install it."],[3109,"Downloaded datasets"],[3128,"Downloaded when you load it"],[3131,"Downloaded when you load it"],[121,"Downloads must use `https://`. `_https()` in `marketplace/addons/semantic_views.py` refuses any other scheme and refuses a redirect that leaves HTTPS. The UDF path checks the redirect the same way."],[3078,"Draft"],[1106,"Draft a column map for a table"],[1105,"Draft and approved"],[2723,"Draft each column's role in a table (key, time, measure, category, flag, text, identifier, other), approve it, and publish it as an Exasol Semantic Views model for the notebooks and AI clients."],[4030,"Draft Exasol SQL from a plain-language question, without an AI model: nb.draft_question."],[3307,"Draft SQL from the user's opted-in model endpoint; `proposed_sql` supports manual drafting."],[3609,"Draft SQL from the user's opted-in model endpoint; `proposed_sql` supports manual drafting."],[4029,"Draft SQL without a model"],[2475,"Drafts SQL for your question"],[150,"Each add-on's output goes to `logs/marketplace.log` in the kit home, created at mode 600. `run_logged()` in `marketplace/runtime.py` replaces the values of any environment variable whose name ends in `PASSWORD`, `TOKEN`, `_KEY` or `SECRET` before the output is written."],[1287,"Each approval adds a line to the workflow log with the question, the approved SQL, its digest and the column map version. Each run adds a line with the row count."],[493,"Each approved column map is kept as a version, in `~/.exasol-starter-kit/descriptors/<SCHEMA>.<TABLE>/`. The module docstring of `setup/lib/descriptor/store.py` gives the layout:"],[3207,"Each column gets a role: key, time, measure, category. You approve it"],[2482,"Each column's name, type, role, evidence and top values. Never a row."],[2609,"Each entry gives the message or the symptom, then the command to run. The AI entries are at the end."],[1581,"Each entry gives the message the kit shows, then what to do."],[2962,"Each entry gives what the add-on is (the one line the catalog holds), how the kit installs it, its repository, and its documentation. Where the kit pins a version or a SHA-256 digest for an add-on, Add-ons and downloads lists it."],[622,"Each entry quotes the message or describes the step that stops."],[1905,"Each entry quotes the message the kit prints, or describes the step that stops."],[2020,"Each entry quotes the message the kit shows, or describes the step that stops."],[856,"Each entry quotes the warning or describes the score you see."],[2277,"Each entry starts with the finding or symptom you see. Find it, then read the fix."],[1409,"Each entry starts with the message or symptom you see. Find it, then read the fix."],[654,"Each finding says what it does to a result. The kit does not fix the table or drop rows for you. Decide what to do, make the change in your own cleaned view or column map, and run the check again. The cleaned views are on Prepare."],[1717,"Each idea shows its title, the reason it was proposed, and the SQL. Read the SQL before you keep it. It is the same expression the kit would run on your table."],[2452,"Each key is typed into a hidden prompt. It is never part of a command, so it is not in the shell's history."],[2043,"Each kind of change to your data, what the kit notices about it, and the stage to return to."],[1366,"Each link comes back with its evidence. Measured on a real database, between the Amazon sample data and a PostgreSQL source read live:"],[757,"Each model is scored with the metric for its task. The metric the lab picks by comes first in the table. The board shows the other columns as well."],[4065,"Each note says what one row of the result is, what each number means in the data's own words (`ds.grain`: \"one\nrow per order line\" makes them order lines), the overall figure, the highest and lowest groups, which groups are too small to\ntrust, and that a difference between groups is not a cause. Nothing is computed that the result does not hold."],[2598,"Each notebook opens with a guided card. A card has buttons and forms for the page's steps. The first card has a **Docs** button beside the logo. It opens this documentation on the page for that notebook."],[738,"Each of its values is nearly always 1 (at least 99% of its rows) or nearly always 0 (at least 99%)."],[605,"Each preview and each publish adds a line to the workflow log, with the query's digest, the descriptor version and the revision number. The kinds are listed on The workflow log."],[2363,"Each provider below needs one of two things: a key from its console, or a server you run yourself. The links go to the provider's own page. Check the model list on the provider's page, because model names change. The Home card lists the models your key may use, so you rarely need to look one up."],[4022,"Each provider is reached through its OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions address, the one the kit's client speaks\n(model_config.py). Listing the models is one GET with the key, to the provider only (never anywhere else, never\nover plain http to another computer); the key is not kept here. Effort is the provider's own `reasoning_effort`:\noffered only where the provider documents it for that model. Anthropic's OpenAI-compatible API ignores it, so a\nClaude model is offered none."],[2015,"Each trace is tagged with the database session, the workflow id and, with a dataset, its id and descriptor version. When the block ends, the kit prints the trace id and where to find it, and adds a `trace` line to the workflow log. The secret key is never printed or logged."],[2270,"Each view gets its own approved column map. The new map starts from the roles of the table it came from. A text column that became a date takes the time role. If the time slot is empty, the converted column fills it."],[2251,"Each view gets its own column map"],[2271,"Each view is a separate dataset with its own versions, so approving a view does not change its source table's map. A view you create is saved with the same rules as any column map: each approval is a new version, and nothing is overwritten. See Approve the column map."],[881,"Edit"],[892,"Edit an `.mdx` file, or add one and list it in its folder's `meta.json`. Each page starts with:"],[2400,"Effort"],[2495,"Either no model is set, or the dataset has no column for that step. Run `nb.model_settings()` to see what is set. Set the model as shown above. The themes step also skips on a dataset with no text column, and says so. The reference datasets, `amazon_sales` and `fraud_transactions`, have no text column."],[2626,"Either no model is set, or the dataset has no column for that step. Run `nb.model_settings()` to see what is set. Set the model as shown on Set up AI and Langfuse. The themes step also skips on a dataset with no text column, and says so. The reference datasets, `amazon_sales` and `fraud_transactions`, have no text column."],[2119,"Empty cells"],[2142,"Empty cells"],[416,"Entity names and tables, grains, relationships, dimension and fact names and comments, metric expressions, and up to ten values of a category dimension"],[3167,"Errors come with their fix"],[68,"Escape hatches"],[2436,"EU"],[697,"Evaluate"],[703,"Evaluation answers one question: how well will this model do on rows it has not seen? A score on the rows it learned from says little, because a model can memorise them. The kit holds rows out before it trains, reports the metric that fits your task, and warns you about the traps it can detect: columns that give the answer away, rare answers, and held-out sets that are too small. It does not run significance tests. The page on comparing models says what to do about that."],[2952,"Every add-on is listed with its state, its version and what it is. Nothing is installed. Add `--json` for a script."],[2829,"Every add-on, with your personas' own ticked. Tick or untick any, then Enter installs what is ticked."],[1095,"Every approval is a new version. Nothing is overwritten."],[2033,"Every approval is a new version. Nothing is overwritten."],[18,"Every button is one call, so clicking **Approve** and running the approve call do the same thing. The notebook's own code sits below the cards. You can use either way, or switch between them as you work."],[3848,"Every call runs the same `exakit` the terminal runs (on PATH, else in the kit's bin folder), detached from any\nterminal: a question the command would ask takes its default, and a choice is given up front through the variables\nthe command documents (`nb.exakit(\"mcp-setup\", env={\"EXAKIT_MCP_CLIENTS\": \"claude\"})`). Nothing is read from the\nnotebook's input. The result says the exit code and keeps the output, so a cell can test `run.ok`."],[2599,"Every card has a **Guided / Code** switch. **Guided** is the default. **Code** shows the calls behind each button. Two ways through each notebook explains both."],[2286,"Every column already has its type, and nothing needs cleaning. That is the right result. No view is created."],[1056,"Every column has a role, and no column sits in two slots."],[1653,"every column name and its role. A column marked sensitive is left out."],[2654,"Every command of the kit, 42 in all, with what it takes and what it does."],[3148,"Every CSV, Parquet and JSON (.json, .geojson) file at the folder's top level becomes one table named after the file. The schema is asked once:"],[1483,"Every data project starts with data that is in one place, can be read again, and is the same each time you read it. In this stage you put a table in front of the kit. The kit offers three origins: a sample dataset that comes with the kit, your own file or folder, and an external database or lake that the kit reads live. Each origin ends in a table the rest of the workflow can describe."],[2528,"Every data science project needs a place to work: a database that holds the data, a way to query it, and a notebook to write in. The kit gives you all three on your computer: a local Exasol database, the tools that load and query it, and four notebooks that run on it. Setup takes one install command and one check."],[3538,"Every dataset with an approved column map, newest approval first: \\{id, table, version, approved_at}."],[3607,"Every dataset with an approved column map, newest approval first: \\{id, table, version, approved_at}."],[550,"Every distinct query the workflow ran, each with its SHA-256 and row count"],[929,"Every exported helper has a page in these docs, and every link in them leads somewhere."],[3154,"Every file is listed with its table and the rows that landed, or the reason it did not load. A file the loader refuses leaves no empty table behind."],[3837,"Every line of a workflow's log, in order."],[4333,"Every line of a workflow's log, in order. A missing log is a FileNotFoundError naming the path."],[2689,"Every log the kit can show."],[1402,"Every metric the AI proposes is checked before the kit offers it. Semantic Views checks it again when the model is built. A refused metric is skipped, and the preview names it. Without a model, the fields keep the names the column maps give."],[674,"Every model in the lab is trained on the same training rows and scored on the same held-out rows. The held-out rows are the test. Keeping them apart is the only way to see how a model does on rows it has not seen."],[1872,"Every model in the lab, the name that selects it, and the rule that picks the best one."],[15,"Every notebook opens with a **guided card**. A card has buttons and forms for the page's steps. Each card has a **Guided / Code** switch at its top right."],[3597,"Every notebook starts with `import exakit.nb as nb`. Each name below is one call a cell can make, and the same\ncall a guided card makes behind its buttons."],[312,"Every outbound call the kit makes"],[2921,"Every persona connects all the AI clients found on this computer."],[75,"Every pin is in `versions.json` at the root of the repository. The kit reads the copy that shipped with it, not a copy fetched from the network. Each module says so in a comment, for example \"The kit copy's own pin, never the fetched document (SEC-13)\" in `setup/lib/exapump.sh`."],[3291,"Every proposed metric is checked before it is used: it may only add up a fact of its view, combine that view's metrics, and filter on a dimension with one of its known values. The product validates it again when it is applied. A refused one is skipped, and the output names it and says why."],[4025,"Every provider the notebooks offer: id, name, the Chat Completions address, whether it needs a key\n(\"required\", \"optional\", \"none\"), where to get one, and whether it runs on this computer."],[3745,"Every provider the notebooks offer: id, name, the Chat Completions address, whether it needs a key (\"required\", \"optional\", \"none\"), where to get one, and whether it runs on this computer."],[3596,"Every public helper of exakit.nb, 120 in all, with the page that documents it."],[3026,"Every run first writes the kit's current connection into the notebooks' encrypted store, so a database restart or a port change needs no edit. It also copies any kit notebook you do not have yet. Yours are never overwritten."],[3901,"Every sample dataset this kit ships, in the kit's order: \\{id, label, description, schema, default, loaded,\ndescribed} - described: it ships a column map, so nb.load_sample opens it ready to use.\n`loaded` (ids) marks the ones in the database; by default the kit's status says which."],[3783,"Every sample dataset this kit ships, in the kit's order: \\{id, label, description, schema, default, loaded, described} - described: it ships a column map, so nb.load_sample opens it ready to use."],[3540,"Every saved version of a dataset's column map, oldest first: \\{version, approved_at, roles, slots, evidence} -\nwhat approving one of them again (RoleReview\\.approve) would restore."],[3625,"Every saved version of a dataset's column map, oldest first: \\{version, approved_at, roles, slots, evidence} - what approving one of them again (RoleReview\\.approve) would restore."],[3719,"Every schema with its number of tables, virtual ones (connected sources) marked."],[4052,"Every schema with its number of tables, virtual ones (connected sources) marked."],[3791,"Every semantic model in the database: name, published schema, whether the kit built it (and can refresh it)."],[4185,"Every semantic model in the database: name, published schema, whether the kit built it (and can refresh it)."],[2056,"Every semantic model the table is in is rebuilt by the approval"],[1386,"Every statement of the search is bounded: one aggregate per table, one `SELECT DISTINCT ... LIMIT 500` per column, one count with a list of values per pair, and at most 400 pairs. Measured: six schemas with 25 tables took 223 statements and about 60 seconds, most of it the live source. Three schemas took 26 statements and 23 seconds."],[961,"Every step follows the same path, whether you run a cell or click a card:"],[3275,"Every table"],[1314,"Every table has a row count, `<entity>_count`."],[3283,"Every table needs an approved column map first."],[2253,"Every view the preparation steps create goes into one schema, `EXAKIT_PREPARED`. Your table is never changed. The kit creates a view and never alters the table under it. Each view is a separate dataset, so the later stages can read it like any table."],[1976,"Every workflow has one log, `~/.exasol-starter-kit/workflows/<id>.jsonl`: one JSON object per line, append-only, readable by you only. While a workflow is active, each helper that does something adds a line. The kinds you will see are:"],[2655,"Everyday"],[1461,"Everything `exakit connect` asks for that source, in one place:"],[489,"Everything is under the kit home, `~/.exasol-starter-kit` (or `EXAKIT_HOME`). Three rules apply to the files there:"],[1007,"Everything is under the kit's home, `~/.exasol-starter-kit` (or `EXAKIT_HOME` when set)."],[972,"Everything is under the kit's home, `~/.exasol-starter-kit`, or `EXAKIT_HOME` when it is set. The main folders are:"],[897,"Everything under a persona's `refe