fted one set), its reason and evidence under it - the columns drafted at low confidence first, under their own heading; then one dropdown per slot with the table's columns; then the Approve button."],[294,"One helper sends row text"],[2279,"One identifier repeats in some rows. If one row should be one value, those rows count twice. Count distinct values, or keep one row per value. If the repeats are correct, for example an order with several lines, keep the data as it is and say so in your notes."],[3184,"One JSON object comes back and nothing else: the rows and their count on success, or the error with a command to run, when there is one."],[1456,"One list of every kind of source the kit connects, each with a line saying what it is. Type in the box at its top to narrow it. The list opens inside the card, under the field, so it never covers the page."],[1300,"One model across sources"],[3256,"One model across sources"],[4301,"One model call per side (label = 1, label = 0): the model sorts that side's texts into two to four themes\nand answers in JSON, so the result is a table - theme, how many texts, their share, an example - with a note in plain\nwords under it. A theme found on one side only is the clue: what those texts are about that the others are not."],[3255,"One model per schema"],[3915,"One model-lab run: the task, its settings, the data it read and what came out (board and pick for a\nprediction, groups or unusual rows otherwise). `features` are the feature ideas it was trained with."],[3711,"One model-lab run: the task, its settings, the data it read and what came out (board and pick for a prediction, groups or unusual rows otherwise)."],[3781,"One proposal."],[4086,"One proposal. Jupyter shows a dropdown per column and an Approve button; elsewhere approve(choices) is the same\npath. dataset() stops the next cell until approval happened (a headless run hands the draft on, see the module)."],[915,"One Python call for each thing a notebook does"],[956,"One 