red error (RMSE)"],[785,"Rare answers"],[2125,"Rare outcome"],[2148,"Rare outcome"],[2810,"Re-place the AI skills the kit copy carries (repair only)."],[2582,"Re-running the installer is safe. It skips the steps that finished and retries the ones that failed."],[1912,"Read `lab_data.left_out`. It gives the reason for each column left out: gives the answer away, personal data, a key or identifier, free text, or marked Leave out. A column marked sensitive, or flagged by the leakage check, is not used. Change the column map if the role is wrong, and approve it again."],[4283,"Read a source's connection string exactly as `exakit connect --url` does: it is handed to the kit's engine\n(its `paste` command, on standard input, never as an argument). Returns \\{connector, values, notes, dropped,\nmasked, credential_in_string, secret_input, missing}: `values` by input name, each checked as if typed;\n`masked` the string with every credential as \\*\\*\\*\\*; `missing` the connector's required inputs the string does\nnot give (and no default covers). The string's password is used by nb.connect_source(url=...) and is never\nreturned, printed or logged here. For a connector with settings (a Lakehouse's `catalog=`, `files=`) give the\nones already chosen: a setting the string itself shows (an s3:// path\nis a folder with no catalog) comes back in `values`, and `missing` is what that combination still needs."],[3773,"Read a source's connection string exactly as `exakit connect --url` does: it is handed to the kit's engine (its `paste` command, on standard input, never as an argument)."],[1999,"Read it with the commands in the table on Monitor and iterate, or in a notebook:"],[3042,"Read the log of a piece of work from the terminal - every query, approval and dashboard, in order."],[1609,"Read the note the kit gives. It tells you whether the name is wrong, or whether this network's DNS does not answer. Another network, a VPN, or a DNS server of 1.1.1.1 or 8.8.8.8 on this computer can fix it."],[389,"Read the output before you send it. The kit redacts the secrets listed on the Credentials page in the places that page names. Logs can still hold your data, file paths and table names."],[1283,"Read the proposal, and edit it if it is wrong:"],[1291,"Read the SQL the kit returns before you approve it. The repository does not record the SQL or the answer for either question. To see the SQL the kit drafts, draft the question and read the proposal's SQL. Drafting is not approval, so nothing runs:"],[2589,"Read these docs from a notebook"],[1261,"Read, edit and approve"],[830,"Reading ROC AUC"],[832,"Reading ROC AUC"],[3165,"Reads only unless you say otherwise"],[1598,"Reason"],[2773,"Rebuild a database that cannot start."],[4183,"Rebuild a model the kit published, with the column maps and links approved since (`exakit describe --model\nNAME --refresh`). Approving a column map refreshes every model it is in by itself."],[3777,"Rebuild a model the kit published, with the column maps and links approved since (`exakit describe --model NAME --refresh`)."],[2663,"Reference"],[2065,"Refresh the semantic model"],[3341,"Refuse a pickle whose scikit-learn version differs before any scoring SQL runs."],[3619,"Refuse a pickle whose scikit-learn version differs before any scoring SQL runs."],[3767,"Refuse stale input, create the view, drop constant features and render the UDF and training SELECT."],[3953,"Refuse stale input, create the view, drop constant features and render the UDF and training SELECT."],[869,"Regenerate"],[992,"Regenerate the notebooks and the command reference with `python3 tools/notebooks.py --marimo` and `python3 tools/nb_docs.py`."],[2433,"Region"],[3221,"Region"],[4166,"Remove a link that is wrong, by the column it starts from: `unlink(\"ORDERS.O_CLERK\")`."],[2823,"Remove a persona"],[2814,"Remove exactly what upgrade-kit2 added (internal)."],[2808,"Remove the kit's MCP entries from named AI clients."],[2782,"Remove what the kit installed.