oved column maps in the kit's store, and the semantic layer is Exasol Semantic Views: a table\nthat is an entity of a semantic model the kit built says which model (SEMANTIC_CATALOG.ENTITIES). The links are the\napproved schema maps' and the multi-source models' (nb.semantic_model). Columns that share a key-like name across\ntwo tables are listed as possible links: a lead to check, never a join made for you. Only metadata is read."],[2080,"Roles for the columns whose name and type did not change are carried over."],[1620,"Roles written beside a file"],[1102,"Roles: what a column is"],[421,"Row values"],[2059,"Rows changed, with no column change"],[3241,"Rows copied out of a source"],[2117,"Rows equal to another row in every column except the key"],[409,"Rows. Values of sensitive columns"],[2854,"Rules"],[2346,"Rules the kit enforces:"],[904,"Rules the tests enforce"],[3851,"Run `exakit <args>` and show its output line by line as it comes (`show=False` keeps it quiet); the\nKitRun says how it ended. A command that takes longer than `timeout` seconds is stopped and says so."],[3681,"Run `exakit <args>` and show its output line by line as it comes (`show=False` keeps it quiet); the KitRun says how it ended."],[2618,"Run `exakit notebook --no-browser`. It prints the address. The login token is in `~/.exasol-starter-kit/credentials`. Do not paste the token anywhere else."],[2619,"Run `exakit notebook check`. It finds the kit's database connection and checks it."],[2617,"Run `exakit notebook setup`. Every `exakit notebook` command registers the kernel again."],[2616,"Run `exakit notebook setup`. It installs the kit's JupyterLab again at its pinned version. Without a terminal it does this without asking. If the notebook environment itself is broken, run `exakit update notebook`."],[2591,"Run `exakit notebook` again after an install or an update to check the notebook environment and the database connection. It fixes what it can and says what it cannot fix."],[3178,"Run `exa