],[1489,"The **Choose your data** card in `00_quickstart`. Tick kit datasets, your own tables and external sources, any number of them together."],[2534,"The **Home** card in `00_quickstart`, tab **Your kit**"],[2360,"The **Langfuse tracing** row works the same way: pick your region (the pencil types your own Langfuse's address), paste the public and secret keys, and click **Trace to Langfuse**. See Get Langfuse for where the keys come from."],[3092,"The **target** is never drafted. Only a person sets it."],[441,"The `clear_text_ok()` test applies to the Langfuse address only inside `use_model()`. A Langfuse address set in your shell or in `exakit.env` is not checked."],[971,"The `exakit` commands are described in `setup/help/exakit.json`. `exakit <command> --help` shows a command's reference and changes nothing."],[2414,"the `o` series, `gpt-5` and later (OpenAI reasoning guide)"],[1899,"The 0.01 rule is a rule for choosing a simple model. It is not a test that the gap between two models is real. To judge a gap, read `cv_sd` on the board. See Comparing models on the Evaluate pages."],[1779,"The 0/1 target"],[3217,"The 21 rows are misspelt state names. The link stands, and you get the list to clean. It took 26 small queries."],[823,"The 30-row limit is one constant, `SMALL`, in `readout.py`. It is the same for groups and periods."],[3647,"The active workflow id: the session's, else the one inherited through EXAKIT_WORKFLOW_ID, else None."],[4322,"The active workflow id: the session's, else the one inherited through EXAKIT_WORKFLOW_ID, else None."],[1061,"The active workflow's log gets one line."],[2942,"The add-ons"],[352,"The address in `EXAKIT_PROVIDER_BASE_URL`"],[356,"The address in `LANGFUSE_BASE_URL`"],[2395,"The address is `https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/`."],[2368,"The address is `https://api.mistral.ai/v1/`."],[2365,"The address is `https://api.openai.com/v1/`."],[2326,"The address of the model's API, including its version prefix, such as `/v1/`. Not a full