d links."],[2024,"The approval stands, but the semantic model could not be rebuilt. The message says why. Fix the cause, then run `exakit describe <id> --comments`. See Versions and semantic models."],[1418,"The approval still stands, and the message says why. Retry with `exakit describe <id> --comments`, or refresh the model with `nb.refresh_semantic(connection, \"<name>\")` once the cause is fixed."],[2225,"The approval warns about `STATUS` in `AMAZON.ORDER_LINES`. A cancelled order has a cancelled status, so the status gives the answer away. You can check this on the table. These two queries are read-only, and both were run on a real database on 12 November 2026:"],[1275,"The approved column map and the question. No rows."],[2476,"The approved column map and your question. No rows."],[546,"The approved column map, copied from the kit's store"],[454,"The approved column maps"],[3942,"The approved data the lab trains on, read once (newest first, at most ROW_LIMIT rows): every usable column,\nwith the ones that give the answer away (nb.leakage_check, unless `leaks` is given) and personal data left out\n(`.left_out` says why). Pass it to model_lab(data=...) to train several times without reading it again."],[3713,"The approved data the lab trains on, read once (newest first, at most ROW_LIMIT rows): every usable column, with the ones that give the answer away (nb.leakage_check, unless `leaks` is given) and personal data left out (`.left_out` says why)."],[4108,"The approved dataset: the one approved here, else the approved version the review opened on."],[548,"The approved schema map, when the schema has one"],[2082,"The approved version stays approved for the old columns. Nothing is overwritten."],[3541,"The approved version's number from `current`, or None when there is none (or the file does not hold one)."],[3645,"The approved version's number from `current`, or None when there is none (or the file does not hold one)."],[3306,"The archived Governed SQL server is 